[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mmain · ▸ follow_link(#fn-140002b6c) · 23441 chars\u001b[39m                         \r\n                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mmain · ▸ follow_link(#fn-14003e62c) · 4566 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                      \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mmain · ▸ follow_link(#fn-140001e10) · 2897 chars\u001b[21;1H\u001b[93m📌 #q-toolchain-packing — What language/toolchain built this binary, and is it packed or obfuscated?\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mFile identity in #file-identity: 745472-byte x64 PE (image base 0x140000000), build timestamp 2025-04-02T20:08:03Z, overall entropy 6.21 (not\r\npacked-looking). #runtime-noise says a recognized MSVC/CRT runtime is statically linked.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                              \r\n\u001b[93mDetermine with evidence:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m- Compiler/linker (MSVC version? Rich header?), subsystem, section layout and per-section entropy.\r\n- Is any section packed/encrypted? Is the import table normal or minimized (dynamic API resolution)?\r\n- Any TLS callbacks or unusual entry-point behavior?\r\n- Note where main/the real payload entry is (entry → CRT → main address).\u001b[32;140H\u001b[37mcreate\u001b[Cpost\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.026, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m Decrypt a representative set of blobs to prove the scheme, especially the ones at 0x14007d838/0x14007da08 region — expect C2 URL/domain,\r\nuser-agent, paths, browser names.\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[94m4. \u001b[93mReport the key, algorithm, and decrypted plaintexts (as many as practical; at minimum the C2/config-related ones).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                      \r\n\u001b[93m📌 #q-embedded-pe — What is the PE embedded in .data at file offset 0x890d0, and what consumes it?\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mDetector finding (comment !1 under #file-level): a PE executable is embedded in .data at \u001b[1mfile offset 0x890d0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m.\u001b[11;1HDetermine:\u001b[39m                           \u001b[13;1H\u001b[93m- Read the headers at that offset: is it a real PE (MZ/PE magic, machine, timestamp, sections, size)? 32 or 64-bit, DLL or EXE? Export names if any.\r\n- Map the file offset to a virtual address and find \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mcross-references: which code reads/copies/decrypts/loads it (manual mapping? write-to-disk?\r\ninjection?).\u001b[39m                                       \r\n\u001b[93m- Note: Stealc v2 is known to embed/side-load helper DLLs (e.g. for browser credential decryption). Identify whether this is such a helper or a\r\nsecond-stage payload.\u001b[39m                             \u001b[19;1H\u001b[93m📌 #q-family-attribution — Confirm family attribution: is this Stealc v2? What traits should we verify in the binary?\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mThree YARA rules matched the raw file (#file-level): Windows_Trojan_Stealc_41db1d4d (Elastic), MALPEDIA_Win_Stealc_Auto, and\r\nRUSSIANPANDA_Win_Mal_Stealc_V2. Build timestamp 2025-04-02 (#f\u001b[Cle-identity)\u001b[Cfits th\u001b[C Stealc v2 release window (March 2025).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                             \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mResearcher task:\u001b[Csummarize what\u001b[Cis publicly known\u001b[Cabout \u001b[1mStealc v2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m that we can fals\u001b[Cfy/verify statically here:\u001b[25;1H- St\u001b[Cing obfuscat\u001b[Con scheme (base64+RC4?), config format, how the C2 URL is stored.\r\n- C2 protocol (HTTP POST? JSON? endpoints/paths, user-agent), message flow (hwid beacon → config → exfil).\u001b[27;4Hapabilities: browsers/wallets/extensions targeted, file\u001b[Cgrabber, loader functionality (download&exec), screenshot, self-delete.\u001b[28;3HEmbedded PE / helper DLL usag\u001b[C in v2 (64-bit rewrit\u001b[2Cdetai\u001b[Cs).\u001b[39m                                    \u001b[29;5H\u001b[93mti-analysis traits\u001b[C(locale/CIS checks?\u001b[Canti-VM? date checks?).\u001b[30;3HDistinctive IOC patterns\u001b[Cto hunt\u001b[Cfor in decrypted strings. Output a checklist the reverse engineers can confirm against the sample.\u001b[32;114H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠙\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
