[0.012, "o", "\u001b[4;90H\u001b[90m4\u001b[C5\u001b[6;90H2\u001b[C6\u001b[8;90H278\u001b[10;91H88\u001b[12;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Europa)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                        \r\n\u001b[97mRich header decode confirmed by the native tool. Now let me check the dynamic API resolution — decompile two non-CRT GetProcAddress callers.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Europa) · ▸ decomp_function(0x14003c0a8) · 2540 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                        \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Europa) · ▸ decomp_function(0x140059e50) · 3277 chars\u001b[39m                                                                     \u001b[19;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                           \r\n\u001b[97mThis is the Chromium app-bound-encryption bypass flow: build browser path from CSIDL 0x1a/0x1c, check \"Local State\", create a\u001b[93m \\\\.\\pipe\\\u001b[97m named pipe,\r\ncall FUN_14003a048 (the injector) with a process name, then read ~0x1ff bytes (the key) back from the pipe. Now let me (a) verify the API pointer\r\nidentities in the injector, and (b) dump strings from the embedded DLL's .rdata (blob offset 0x15000 → file 0x9E0D0).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ xrefs_to(DAT_1400b4b50) · 250 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                \r\n                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ strings_range(647376) · 7993 chars\u001b[39m                                                   \u001b[28;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Amalthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                            \r\n\u001b[97mNo Stealc-related memories exist in the library yet, so I'll work from recalled public reporting (SEKOIA's v1 analysis, Zscaler ThreatLabz's and\r\nRussianPanda's v2 analyses), clearly labeled, and post a falsifiable checklist. First batch of evidence comments:\u001b[42;101H\u001b[90m66\u001b[C759\u001b[8C4\u001b[2C787\u001b[12C710\u001b[C546\u001b[4C6\u001b[C077\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.003, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97mThis is the Chromium app-bound-encryption bypass flow: build browser path from CSIDL 0x1a/0x1c, check \"Local State\", create a\u001b[93m \\\\.\\pipe\\\u001b[97m named pipe,\r\ncall FUN_14003a048 (the injector) with a process name, then read ~0x1ff bytes (the key) back from the pipe. Now let me (a) verify the API pointer\r\nidentities in the injector, and (b) dump strings from the embedded DLL's .rdata (blob offset 0x15000 → file 0x9E0D0).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ xrefs_to(DAT_1400b4b50) · 250 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mallisto) · ▸ strings_range(647376) · 7993 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                        \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Amalthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97mNo Stealc-related memories exist in the library yet, so I'll work from recalled public reporting (SEKOIA's v1 analysis, Zscaler ThreatLabz's and\r\nRussianPanda's v2 analyses), clearly labeled, and post a falsifiable checklist. First batch of evidence comments:\u001b[17;1H\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-family-attribution\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Amalthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                    \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1m(1/8) Family/lineage context and prior\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93m[external knowledge] Stealc is a C-based info-stealer sold as MaaS since\u001b[1m Jan 2023\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (advertised by actor \"Plymouth\"