[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mderived from the Vidar/Raccoon/Mars/Arkei lineage. v1 builds were\u001b[1m 32-bit\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m.\u001b[1m Stealc v2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (versions 2.x) appeared ~\u001b[1mMarch 2025\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m as a substantial rewrite:\r\n\u001b[1m64-bit payloads\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, RC4-protected strings and network traffic, a\u001b[1m JSON-based C2 protocol\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, loader enhancements (EXE/MSI/PowerShell delivery), and an\r\nembedded builder with Telegram integration (per Zscaler ThreatLabz and RussianPanda public reporting).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m[binary fact] This sample is a 745KB\u001b[1m x64\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m PE, MSVC/CRT toolchain (#runtime-noise), build timestamp\u001b[1m 2025-04-02\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (#file-identity) — squarely inside the\r\nv2 release window — and matched three independent Stealc rules including a\u001b[1m v2-specific\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m rule (RUSSIANPANDA_Win_Mal_Stealc_V2) at 8 distinct offsets\r\n(#file-level !4).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mPrior:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m attribution to Stealc v2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m is high-confidence as a lead, but YARA is content-derived; final confirmation should rest on the behavioral checklist\r\nin the following comments (string crypto scheme, C2 message format, capability strings, no-persistence profile).\u001b[39m \u001b[32;91H    \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠏ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mResearch\u001b[Cr(Am\u001b[2Cthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: cal\u001b[Cing create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.030, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mstyle literals (v1). Which one is present tells us v1 vs v2 protocol.\r\n\u001b[94m3. \u001b[93mImports/dynamic resolution of wininet.dll or winhttp.dll POST primitives.\u001b[39m                                                                       \r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b[93m hwid generation: v1 derived it from volume serial / SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\MachineGuid — check for GetVolumeInformation / that registry\r\npath.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                \u001b[9;1H\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-family-attribution\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Amalthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1m(4/8) Checklist — capability set\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m[external knowledge] Advertised/observed Stealc capabilities (v1 and v2):\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[93m-\u001b[1m B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m\u001b[1mrowsers:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Chromium family (Chrome, Edge, Brave, Opera, Vivaldi, …) — passwords, cookies, autofill, CC; Gecko family (Firefox, Thunderbird) —\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[93mkey4.db/logins.json. v2 additionally handles\u001b[1m Chrome App-Bound Encryption (ABE)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m cookies (see comment 5).\u001b[39m          \r\n\u001b[93m-\u001b[1m Extensions/wallets:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m 100+ browser-extension targets, dominated by crypto wallets (MetaMask, TronLink, Phantom, Ronin, etc.) + 2FA extensions;\r\ndesktop wallets (Elec\u001b[2Cum, Exodus, Atomic, Coinomi, Guarda, Daedalus, Ledger Live…).\r\n- \u001b[1mOther apps:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Telegram, Discord, Tox, Pidgin; email (Outlook, Thunderbird); VPN clients (ProtonVPN, OpenVPN); Steam.\r\n- \u001b[1mFile grabber:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m rules (masks/paths/size caps) are \u001b[1mserver-configured\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, so expect generic grabber plumbing in code, not hardcoded masks.\r\n- \u001b[1mLoader / download-and-execute:\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mv1 ran download\u001b[Cd EXE\u001b[C; \u001b[1mv2 adds MSI (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mmsiexec\u001b[1m) and PowerShell script exe\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m\u001b[1mcution\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m options.\u001b[39m                       \r\n\u001b[93m- \u001b[1mScreenshots:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m yes; \u001b[1mv2 added multi-monitor capture\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m.\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[93m- \u001b[1mSelf-delete:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m optional, via a\u001b[Ccmd /c timeout ... & del ...-style command on exit.\u001b[39m                                                             \r\n\u001b[93m-\u001b[1m SQLite:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m nee\u001b[2Cd\u001b[Cfor Chromium DB parsing —\u001b[Cv1\u001b[1m downloaded\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m sqli\u001b[Ce3.dll from C2; v2 reportedly\u001b[1m statically embeds\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m SQLite (expect sqlite3_open/SQL\r\nliterals like SELECT ... FROM logins/cookies in the binary or in decrypted strings).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mCaveat:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m b\u001b[Ccause target lis\u001b[Cs come from th\u001b[C server, \u001b[Che static string\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m set\u001b[Cmay contain su\u001b[Cprisingly few application names — mostly path/registry/API\r\nprimitiv\u001b[Cs, SQL queries, and the functional strings above. Absence of a big wallet-name list does\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m falsify Stealc.\u001b[29;1H\u001b[1mFalsifiable checks:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m GDI/GDI+\u001b[Cscreenshot APIs (GetDC/BitB\u001b[Ct/GdipSaveImageToStream or s\u001b[Cmilar) + EnumDispl\u001b[CyM\u001b[2Citors (multi-monitor);\u001b[39m                  \r\n\u001b[93mCreat\u001b[CPr\u001b[Ccess/ShellEx\u001b[Ccute paired\u001b[Cwith msiex\u001b[Cc/powershell lite\u001b[Cals;\u001b[CSQL SELECT\u001b[Cliterals; cmd + tim\u001b[Cout\u001b[C+ del literals.\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
