b0b30 / length slot\r\nDAT_1400b0b40 — the exact globals the RC4 KSA at FUN_\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m140023048 indexes (key[i % DAT_1400b0b40]).\u001b[39m                                                     \r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Byte route:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m read at 0x14007d6e0 returns 43 67 65 4f 76 45 4f 37 68 75 00 = \"CgeOvEO7hu\\0\"; search_memory(\"CgeOvEO7hu\") finds exactly this one\r\nsite.\r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Functional route:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m decrypting known blobs with base64+RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\") yields 100%-printable, semantically coherent plaintext (see task-5\r\ncomment), e.g. jE/hfE0XsWHHzMlk/dS1Tg== → GdipDisposeImage.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93mSecondary constant: the same initializer sets DAT_1400b05f0 = 512e7bd984984fb6 (16 hex chars, plain, not RC4 key) — likely the Stealc build/campaign\r\nID; worth tracking under #q-crypto-keys / config.\u001b[39m                   \u001b[28;1H\u001b[93mNote for #fn-140002b6c detector findings (!8–!25): those \"candidate symmetric keys\" are NOT keys — they are mid-string carvings of these base64(RC\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m4)\r\nstring blobs (e.g. !8 = GdipDisposeImage, !15 is a fragment of jE78T2wMsHTGy/... → GetSystemPowerStatus-class API names). The only real key is\r\nCgeOvEO7hu.\u001b[39m                                                        \u001b[32;90H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠋ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngin\u001b[Cer(Ganymede)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
