[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mved the DLL-download dependency (SQLite statically linked) and added a\u001b[1m Chrome App-Bound Encryption (ABE) bypass\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. Public v2 reporting\r\n(RussianPanda / Zscaler era, 2025) describes stealers of this generation (Stealc v2, Vidar, Lumma)\u001b[1m embedding a helper module that is injected into /\r\nexecuted in the context of Chrome\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m to recover the app-bound key or cookies, e.g. via the IElevator COM elevation service.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m[binary fact] This sample has a PE embedded in .data at file offset 0x890d0 (!1) — consistent with the v2 ABE-helper pattern, and a notable\r\n\u001b[3mdivergence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m from v1.\u001b[39m                                                \u001b[22;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mFalsifiable checks for #q-embedded-pe:\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                     \r\n\u001b[94m1. \u001b[93mExtract the embedded PE; record bitness, DLL vs EXE, exports, com\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mpile timestamp (expect it close to the host's 2025-04-02).\r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m Hunt its strings for: Chrome, app_bound, app-bound, Local State, os_crypt, encrypted_key, elevation, IElevator, a named pipe (\\\\.\\pipe\\...), or\r\nthe Chrome elevation-service CLSID {708860E0-F641-4611-8895-7D867DD3675B}.\r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m In the host, find the consumer: code referencing the blob's VA + injection primitives\u001b[39m          \r\n\u001b[93m(OpenProcess/VirtualAllocEx/WriteProcessMemory/CreateRemoteThread or NtCreateSection-style mapping), likely gated on a Chrome process/path.\r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Alternative hypothesis to rule out:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the blob is just a dropped next-stage payload (loader behavior) rather than an ABE helper — if the host writes\r\nit to disk and executes it instead of injecting into Chrome, reclassify.\u001b[32;92H\u001b[39m   \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠋ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mTh\u001b[2Cking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mRe\u001b[2Carcher(Amalthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.031, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-family-attribution\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Amalthea)\r\n\u001b[93m(8/8) IOC hunting patterns + attribution decision rule\u001b[8;1H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m[ext\u001b[Crnal knowledge] Distinctive patterns to hunt in \u001b[1mdecrypted\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m strings:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                            \r\n\u001b[93m- C2 URL (often bare IP + path; v1 gates ended in /<hex>.php; v2 path convention differs — recover, don't assume) and a short\u001b[1m build/campaign tag\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m(\u001b[C.g. default, actor-chosen names).\r\n- Protocol tokens: v1 hwid, build, message, token; v2 JSON key names (recover exact set — they are good YARA/IOC material).\u001b[13;2H Hardcoded \u001b[1mUser-Ag\u001b[Cnt\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m literal.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m- System-info\u001b[Crepor\u001b[C scaffolding (Vidar-style labels like OS:, Display/resolution, HWID:, install-date, local\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93me fields).\u001b[15;2H SQL queries (SELECT \u001b[Crigin_url, us\u001b[Crname_valu\u001b[C, p\u001b[Cssword_value FROM logins,\u001b[CFROM cookies, FROM autofill, FROM credit_cards).\u001b[39m               \r\n\u001b[93m- Browser data paths (\\User Data\\,\u001b[CLocal State, logins.json, key4.db, formhistory.sqlite), MachineGuid, cmd/timeout/del.\u001b[39m                            \r\n\u001b[93m- RC4 key string itself (reusable\u001b[Cas\u001b[Ca build-sp\u001b[Ccific IOC).\u001b[39m                                                             \u001b[19;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mAttribution decision rule — call it Stealc v2 CONFIRMED if most of these hold:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                             \r\n                   \r\n\u001b[94m1. \u001b[93mSingle hardcoded-key \u001b[1mRC4 (±base64)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m string decryption (comment 2) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93mMinimal embedded config = \u001b[1mC2 URL + build ID\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m; target lists absent/server-side (comment 3) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
