[0.006, "o", "\u001b[42;100H\u001b[90m862\u001b[C569\u001b[9C8\u001b[C707\u001b[12C9\u001b[C1\u001b[C276\u001b[6C7196\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m- C2 URL (often bare IP + path; v1 gates ended in /<hex>.php; v2 path convention differs — recover, don't assume) and a short\u001b[1m build/campaign tag\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m(e.g. default, actor-chosen names).\r\n- Protocol t\u001b[Ckens: v1 hwid, build, message, token; v2 JSON key\u001b[Cnames (recover exact set — they are good YARA/IOC material).\r\n- Hardcoded \u001b[1mUser-Agent\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m literal.\u001b[8;3HSystem-in\u001b[Co repo\u001b[Ct\u001b[Cscaffolding (Vidar-styl\u001b[C labels like OS:, Display/resolution, HWID:, install-date, locale fields).\u001b[39m                         \r\n\u001b[93m- SQL\u001b[Cqueries (SELECT origin_url, username_value, password_value FROM logins, FROM cookies, FROM autofill, FROM credit_cards).\u001b[10;3HB\u001b[2Cwser data paths (\\User\u001b[CData\\\u001b[2CLocal Sta\u001b[Ce, logins.json, key4.db, formhistory.sqli\u001b[Ce), Machin\u001b[CGuid,\u001b[Ccmd/timeout/del.\u001b[39m   \u001b[11;3H\u001b[93mRC4 key string itself (r\u001b[Cusable as a build-specific IOC).\r\n\u001b[39m        "]
[0.001, "o", "                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mAttribution decision rule — call it Stealc v2 CONFIRMED if most of these hold:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                \r\n                                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[94m1. \u001b[93mSingle\u001b[Cha\u001b[Cdcoded-key\u001b[C\u001b[1mRC4 (±base64)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m str\u001b[Cng decryption (comment 2) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93mMinimal embedded config = \u001b[1mC2 URL + build ID\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m; target lists absent/server-side (comment 3) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m3. \u001b[93mC2 messaging is \u001b[1mHTTP POST + JSON\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (v2) rather than form-data (v1) (comment 3) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m4. \u001b[93mx64 + statically-linked SQLite + no DLL-download URLs (comments 1, 4) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m5\u001b[2C\u001b[93mEmbedded PE plausibly a \u001b[1mChrome ABE helper\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[C\u001b[93m(comment 5) ✔/✘\u001b[39m           \r\n\u001b[94m6\u001b[2C\u001b[93mL\u001b[Cght anti-analysis: HAL9TH/JohnDoe and/or da\u001b[Ce kill switch and/or CIS locale \u001b[Check (comment 6) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m7\u001b[2C\u001b[93m\u001b[1mNo persistence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m,\u001b[Cself-delete present (comment\u001b[C7) ✔/✘\u001b[39m                             \r\n                                                                            \r\n\u001b[93mIf (3) shows form-data/.php gates instead of\u001b[CJSON, the sample may be v1-lineage code in an x64 build — downgrade to \"Stealc, version uncertain\". If\r\n(1) fails outright, re-examine attribution entirely despite t\u001b[Ce YARA hits.\u001b[39m                            \r\n                                                      \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ search_forum(init_decrypted_string_table decrypted s…) · 4220 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                       "]
