[0.016, "o", "\u001b[4;3H\u001b[93mRC4 key string itself (reusable as \u001b[C build-specific IOC).\u001b[39m                                                            \r\n                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mAttribution decision rule — call it Stealc v2 CONFIRMED if most of these hold:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                          \r\n                                                           \r\n\u001b[94m1. \u001b[93mSingle hardcoded-key \u001b[1mRC4 (±base64)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m string decryption (comment 2) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93mMinimal embedded config = \u001b[1mC2 URL\u001b[C+ build ID\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m; target lists absent/server-side (comment 3) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m3. \u001b[93mC2 messaging is \u001b[1mHTTP POST + JSON\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (v2) rather than form-data (v1) (comment 3) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m4\u001b[2C\u001b[93mx64 + st\u001b[Cti\u001b[Cally\u001b[Clinked SQLite + no DLL-download URLs (co\u001b[Cments 1, 4) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m5\u001b[2C\u001b[93mEmbedded PE plausibly a\u001b[C\u001b[1mChrome ABE\u001b[Chelper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (comment 5) ✔/✘\u001b[39m                                   \r\n\u001b[94m6\u001b[2C\u001b[93mLight ant\u001b[C-analysis: HAL9TH/JohnDoe and/or da\u001b[Ce kill switch\u001b[Cand/or CIS locale check (comment 6) ✔/✘\r\n\u001b[94m7\u001b[2C\u001b[93m\u001b[1mNo persistence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, self-delete prese\u001b[Ct\u001b[C(comment 7) ✔/✘\u001b[39m                      \r\n                                                            \r\n\u001b[93mIf (3) shows form-data/.php gates inste\u001b[Cd of JSON,\u001b[Cthe sample m\u001b[Cy be v1-lineage cod\u001b[C in an x64 build — downgrade to \"Stealc, version uncertain\". If\r\n(1) fails outright, re-examin\u001b[2Cattribution entirely despite the YARA hits.\u001b[19;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ search_forum(init_decrypted_string_table decrypted s…) · 4220 chars\u001b[39m                                                \r\n                                                                          \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m!60/!61 confirm:\u001b[93m decrypt_string_b64_rc4\u001b[97m @ 0x140007d04, RC4 key\u001b[93m CgeOvEO7hu\u001b[97m. Now I'll find the base64 ciphertexts fed into the globals used by the\r\ninjector, inside\u001b[93m init_decrypted_string_table\u001b[97m. Let me look at the call sites.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ get_function(init_decrypted_string_table) · 287 chars\u001b[39m                                                           \r\n                                                                            \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ read(140005310) · 96 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Europa)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mNow posting the evidence comments under #q-toolchain-packing.\u001b[42;100H\u001b[90m929\u001b[C2\u001b[C6\u001b[8C60\u001b[2C41\u001b[13C90\u001b[C007\u001b[6C9002\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
