[0.001, "o", "\u001b[38;5;251mDAT_1400b4cd8 = \u001b[38;5;109mLoadLibraryA\u001b[38;5;251m(<global std::string>);          \u001b[38;5;243m// DLL name, decrypted at runtime\u001b[39m                                                  \r\n\u001b[38;5;251mDAT_1400b4df8 = \u001b[38;5;109mGetProcAddress\u001b[38;5;251m(hMod, <global std::string>);  \u001b[38;5;243m// first API by name\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[38;5;251mDAT_1400b4df0 = (*DAT_1400b4df8)(hMod, <string>);            \u001b[38;5;243m// then bootstraps further\r\n\u001b[38;5;251m... \u001b[38;5;173m10\u001b[38;5;251m+ more pointers stored into DAT_1400b4d58\u001b[38;5;236m..\u001b[38;5;251mDAT_1400b4ea0\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93m```\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C           \r\n\u001b[93mEvery name argument is an MSVC SSO std::string global in .data (if (0xf < capacity) use heap ptr idiom) that is populated by the string-decryption\r\ninit (init_rc4_key_and_strings, called as the \u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mfirst statement of wWinMain) — i.e.\u001b[1m plaintext API/DLL names decrypted from the base64/RC4 string table,\r\nthen plain GetProcAddress\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. There is\u001b[1m no API hashing\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: no hash constants/loops in the resolver, and GetProcAddress xrefs are only this function, one\r\nmore name-based site (FUN_1400446fc), and CRT-internal api-set lazy loaders (FUN_140059e50, FUN_14003ef2c, FUN_140052640).\u001b[39m                    \r\n                      \r\n\u001b[93mThis matches Stealc v2's documented resolution style (relevant to #q-family-attribution and #q-string-decryption: the decrypted-string globals\r\nfeeding this resolver are a direct window into the string-decryption output).\u001b[39m            \u001b[32;88H    \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Eur\u001b[Cpa)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create_comment\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
