[0.089, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Ganymede) · ▸ set_comment(14007d6e0) · 97 chars\u001b[39m      \r\n                                                                       \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Ganymede) · ▸ set_status(#q-string-decryption) · 10028 chars\u001b[39m                                                                  \r\n                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Researcher(Amalthea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97mTask complete. Summary of what was done for \u001b[1m#q-family-attribution\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (now marked \u001b[1msolved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m):\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mPosted an 8-part falsifiable checklist as evidence comments (!56–!65):\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[94m1.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Lineage/prior\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — Stealc (MaaS since Jan 2023, Vidar/Arkei lineage); v2 = March 2025 64-bit rewrite. The sample's x64 + MSVC + 2025-04-02 timestamp\r\n+ v2-specific YARA hit give a high prior, pending behavioral confirmation.\r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m String obfuscation\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — base64 → RC4 \u001b[Cith one \u001b[Cardcoded ASCII key; concrete KSA/PRGA and key-hunting checks; falsifier: stack-strings/XOR/AES would\r\ncontradict Stealc.\r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Config/C2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — key insight: embedded config is\u001b[3m minimal\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (C2 URL + build ID + RC4 key; target lists are server-side). v1 form-data/\u001b[93m.php\u001b[97m gates vs v2\r\nRC4+base64 JSON POST as the version discriminator; exact v2 paths/JSON keys flagged as unverifiable offline — recover, don't assume.\r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Capabilities\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — browsers/wallets/extensions, server-configured grabber, loader (v2 adds MSI/PowerShell), multi-monitor screenshots, self-delete,\r\nembedded SQLite in v2.\r\n\u001b[94m5.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Embedded PE\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — v2 Chrome App-Bound-Encryption bypass helper hypothesis for the blob at 0x890d0, with string/CLSID/injection-API checks and an\r\nalternative (dropped payload) to rule out.\r\n\u001b[94m6. \u001b[97m\u001b[1mAnti-analysis\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — HAL9TH/JohnDoe check, hardcoded date kill switch (high confidence), CIS locale check (medium), anti-VM (low/verify).\r\n\u001b[94m7. \u001b[97m\u001b[1mPersistence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — historically NONE; gave checks to properly verify the negative in \u001b[3mdecrypted\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m strings, plus self-delete positive expectation.\r\n\u001b[94m8. \u001b[97m\u001b[1mIOC patterns + a 7-point attribution decision rule\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m with explicit downgrade/falsification conditions.\u001b[28;1H\u001b[1mAlso:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m cross-posted targeted hypothesis pointers under #q-string-decryption, #q-embedded-pe, and #q-ransomware; filed a flag_for_review distinguishing\r\nhigh- vs low-confidence recall items; and saved a new\u001b[93m stealc-family-intel-v1-v2\u001b[97m family-intel memory (the library previously had zero Stealc\r\nknowledge). All claims are labeled [external knowledge] vs [binary fact] throughout.\u001b[32;94H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇\u001b[42;97H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m4\u001b[C035\u001b[C813\u001b[9C4\u001b[C098\u001b[12C109\u001b[C9\u001b[C1\u001b[7C1175\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
