[0.004, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m7. \u001b[97m\u001b[1mPersistence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — historically NONE; gave checks to properly verify the negative in \u001b[3mdecrypted\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m strings, plus self-delete positive expectation.\r\n\u001b[94m8. \u001b[97m\u001b[1mIOC patterns + a 7-point attribution decision rule\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m with explicit downgrade/falsification conditions.\u001b[7;1H\u001b[1mAlso:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m cross-posted targeted hypothesis pointers under #q-string-decryption, #q-embedded-pe, and #q-ransomware; filed a flag_for_review distinguishing\r\nhigh- vs low-confidence recall items; and saved a new\u001b[93m stealc-family-intel-v1-v2\u001b[97m family-intel memory (the library previously had zero Stealc\r\nknowledge). All claims are labeled [external knowledge] vs [binary fact] throughout.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Europa)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m#q-toolchain-packing is now \u001b[1msolved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Summary of the answer\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[97m, all posted as evidence comments (!66, !67, !71, !72, !75):\u001b[14;1H\u001b[1mToolchain\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — MSVC\u001b[CC++ (static\u001b[Clly linked CRT + MS\u001b[CC STL), l\u001b[Cnked with\u001b[1m linker 14.43 build 34809 = VS 2022 v17.13\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (early 2025, consistent with th\u001b[C\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[97m2025\u001b[C04-02 build timestamp). Rich heade\u001b[C pr\u001b[Csent (XOR key 0x541FD7A5), decoded and cross-verified with two independent methods: C/C++ objects at\r\nbuilds 30795/34321/34809, LTCG\u001b[CC++ objects + ILTCG/POGO\u001b[Cdebug\u001b[Centries → built with incremental LTCG.\u001b[CNo PDB path.\u001b[39m                                  \r\n                  \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mSubsystem\u001b[Clayout\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m —\u001b[CPE32+ x64,\u001b[1m GUI subsystem (2)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, DllCharacteristics 0x8160 (HEVA/ASLR/DEP).\u001b[C5 \u001b[2Candard sections, no\u001b[Coverlay. Per-section \u001b[Cntropy:\r\n.text 6.43, .rdata 5.25, .data 5.36, .pdata 5.73, .reloc\u001b[C5.33 —\u001b[93m entropy_map\u001b[2C\u001b[97mound\u001b[1m zero regions ≥7.5 bits/byte\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, so\u001b[1m nothing is packed or encrypted\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (the\r\nembedded PE in .data i\u001b[C stored in plaintext; obfuscation is per-st\u001b[Cing base64/RC4, not section packing).\u001b[39m                                          \r\n                      \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mImports\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — functionally minimal: 93 KERNEL32 CRT-su\u001b[Cport functions + \u001b[Cxactly one WININET import (\u001b[93mInternetSetOptionA\u001b[97m). All stealer APIs are resolved at\r\nruntime by\u001b[93m resolve_dynamic_apis_by_name\u001b[97m @ 0x14003c0a8 via\u001b[93m LoadLibraryA\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mGetProcAddress\u001b[97m on\u001b[1m decrypted name strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (MSVC SSO std::string globals) —\u001b[1m no\r\nAPI hashi\u001b[Cg\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                           \r\n                                                                                 "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                           \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTLS\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — directory present (RVA 0x82C00) but the callback array at 0x14006FC68 start\u001b[C w\u001b[Cth a NULL qword: \u001b[1mzero TLS callbacks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, no pre-entry code.\u001b[28;1H\u001b[1mEntry trace\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — entry 0x14003F864 →\u001b[93m __security_init_cookie\u001b[97m (0x14003FF10) →\u001b[93m __scrt_common_main_seh\u001b[C\u001b[97m(0x14003F6F0) →\u001b[93m wWinMain\u001b[97m\u001b[1m @ 0x14002A88C\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m(renamed in\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97mthe project). Bonus findings noted for the other threads: wWinMain opens with the string-d\u001b[Ccrypt init and API \u001b[Cesolver, then \u001b[C\u001b[1m CIS locale kill-switch\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m(0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443) and an OpenMutex(0x1F0003)\u001b[Cguard loop — both relevant to #q-family-attribution and the anti-analysis enumeration.\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
