[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mInternetSetOptionA\u001b[97m). All steal\u001b[2C APIs are res\u001b[Clved at\r\nruntime by\u001b[93m resolve_dynamic_apis_by_name\u001b[97m @ 0x14003c0a8 via\u001b[93m LoadLibra\u001b[CyA\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mGetProcAddress\u001b[97m on\u001b[1m decrypted name strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (MSVC SSO std::string globals) —\u001b[1m no\u001b(B\u001b[m  \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mAPI hashing\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                                                                                            \u001b[22;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTLS\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — directory present (RVA 0x82C00) but the callback array at 0x14006FC68\u001b[Cstarts with\u001b[Ca NULL\u001b[Cqword: \u001b[1mzero TLS callbacks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, no pre-entry code.\u001b[39m         \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mEntry trace\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — entry 0x14003F864 →\u001b[93m __security_init_cookie\u001b[97m (0x14003FF10) →\u001b[93m __scrt_common_main_seh\u001b[97m (0x14003F6F0) →\u001b[93m wWinMain\u001b[97m\u001b[1m @ 0x14002A88C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (renamed in\r\nthe project). Bonus findings noted for the other threads: wWinMain opens with the string-decrypt init and API resolver, then a\u001b[1m CIS locale kill-switch\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m(0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443) and an OpenMutex(0x1F0003) gu\u001b[Crd loop — both relevant to #q-family-attribution and the anti-analysis enumeration.\u001b[28;1H🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ganymede)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m#q-st\u001b[Cing-decryption \u001b[Cs now solv\u001b[3Cwith all fou\u001b[3Casks completed. Let me\u001b[Ccross-post the key finding \u001b[Co the open #q-crypto-keys question, since it\u001b[3