[0.002, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mImports\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — functionally minimal: 9\u001b[C KERNEL32\u001b[CCRT-support functions + exactly\u001b[Cone WININET import (\u001b[93mInternetSetOptionA\u001b[97m). All stealer APIs are resolved at\r\nruntim\u001b[C by\u001b[93m resolve_dynamic_apis_by_name\u001b[97m @ 0x14003c0\u001b[C8 via\u001b[93m LoadLibraryA\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mGetProcAddress\u001b[97m on\u001b[1m decrypted name strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (MSVC SSO std::string globals) —\u001b[1m no\r\nAPI hashing\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTLS\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — directory present (RVA 0x82C00) but\u001b[Cthe callb\u001b[Cck array at 0x14006FC68 starts with a NULL qword: \u001b[1mzero TLS callbacks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m,\u001b[Cno pre-entry c\u001b[Cde.\u001b[39m       \r\n            \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mEntry trace\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — entry 0x14003F864 →\u001b[93m __security_init_cookie\u001b[97m (0x1\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m4003FF10) →\u001b[93m __scrt_common_main_seh\u001b[97m (0x14003F6F0) →\u001b[93m wWinMain\u001b[97m\u001b[1m @ 0x14002A88C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (renamed in\r\nthe\u001b[Cproject). Bonus findings\u001b[Cnoted for the other threads: wWinMain opens with the string-decrypt init\u001b[Cand API resolver, then\u001b[Ca\u001b[1m CIS locale kill-switch\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m(0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443) and an OpenMutex(0x1F0003) guard loop — both relevant to #q-family-attribution and the anti-analysis enumeration.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ganymede)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97m#q-string-decryption is now solved with all four tasks complete\u001b[C. Let\u001b[Cme cross-post \u001b[Che key \u001b[Cinding \u001b[Co\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m the open #q-crypto-keys questio\u001b[C, since it\r\ndirectly answers what those \"candidate keys\" protect.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-crypto-keys\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ganymede)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93mResolved under #q-string-decryption (see !60, !61, !73, !74): the detector's \"candidate symmetric keys\" in .rdata (0x14007d838–0x14007f280) are\u001b[1m not\r\nkeys\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — they are base64(RC4) ciphertext blobs of the Stealc v2 string table (API names, registry paths, file-grab masks, C2 endpoint).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                               \r\n\u001b[93m- Real key: RC4 key CgeOvEO7hu (10 ASCII\u001b[Cbytes @ 0x14007d6e0), loa\u001b[2Cd into glob\u001b[Cl DAT_1400b0b30 by init_rc4_key_\u001b[Cnd_strings @ 0x140\u001b[2C1ee0, consumed\r\nby RC4\u001b[Croutine @ 0x140023048.\u001b[39m                   "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m- Scheme: plaintext = RC4(base64_decode(blob), \"CgeOvEO7hu\") — bulk decrypt with decode_bytes steps=[{op:\"base64\"},{op:\"rc4\",key:\"CgeOvEO7hu\"}].\u001b[25;3HWh\u001b[Ct\u001b[Cthe key protects: all embedded strings including C2 45.93.20.28 + /3d15e67552d448ff.php.\u001b[CPer family reporting (!68) the same key may al\u001b[Co\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93mprotect C2 traffic — the traffic path still needs tracing.\u001b[27;4Heparate plaintext constant 512e7bd984984fb6\u001b[C@ DAT_1400b05f0\u001b[C(li\u001b[Cely build/campaign ID, not\u001b[Ca key).\u001b[39m                                           \r\n                                                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                              \r\n\u001b[97mNow I'll bind each injector API poi\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
