[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97mnMutex(0x1F0003) guard loop — both relevant to #q-family-attribution and the anti-analysis enum\u001b[Cr\u001b[Ction.\u001b[39m \r\n                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ganymede)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97m#q-string-decryption is now solved with all four tasks completed. Let me cross-post the key finding to the open #q-crypto-keys question, since it\r\ndirectly answers what those \"candidate keys\" protect.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-crypto-keys\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ganymede)\u001b(B\u001b[m    \r\n\u001b[93mResolved under #q-s\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mtring-decryption (see !60, !61, !73, !74): the detector's \"candidate symmetric keys\" in .rdata (0x14007d838–0x14007f280) are\u001b[1m not\r\nkeys\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — they a\u001b[Ce base64(RC4) ciphertext blobs of the Stealc v2 string table (API names, registry paths, file-grab masks, C2 endpoint).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[93m- Real\u001b[Ckey:\u001b[CRC4\u001b[Ckey CgeOvEO7hu (10 ASCII bytes @ 0x14007d6e0), loaded into\u001b[Cglobal DAT_1400b0b30\u001b[Cby init_rc4_key_and_strings @ 0x140001ee0, consumed\r\nby RC4 routine @ 0x140023048.\u001b[22;3HScheme: plaintext\u001b[C= RC4(base64_decode(blob),\u001b[C\"CgeOvEO\u001b[Chu\") —\u001b[Cbulk \u001b[Cecrypt with decode_bytes steps=[{op:\"bas\u001b[C64\"},{op:\"rc4\",key:\"CgeOvEO7hu\"}].\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93m- What\u001b[Cthe key\u001b[Cprotects: all embedded strings including C2 45.93.20.28 + /3d15e67552d448ff.php. Per\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[93m family reporting (!68) the same key may also\r\nprotect C2 traffic — the tr\u001b[Cffic path sti\u001b[Cl needs tracing.\u001b[39m                                                                                      \u001b[25;3H\u001b[93mSeparat\u001b[2Cplaintext constant 512e7b\u001b[C984984fb6 @ DAT_1400b05f0 (likely\u001b[Cbuil\u001b[C/campaign ID, not a\u001b[Ck\u001b[Cy).\u001b[39m                                           \r\n                                                          \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97mNow I'll bind each injector API pointer to its decrypted name. First, find the init sites for the remaining globals.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ xrefs_to(DAT_1400b2210) · …running\u001b[39m                                                  \u001b[32;90H     "]
