[0.092, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[90m└───────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93mNo write-to-disk and no decryption\u001b[Cof the blob anywhere:\u001b[Cthe\u001b[Csingle consumer\u001b[Ccopies it as-is into another process. Callers of the injector:\r\nFUN_14001f100 (call site 0x140\u001b[C1f55b) ← FUN_140029f68 — see task-9 comment for the\u001b[Cfull pipeline.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ import_child(stealc_abe_helper_blob) · 157 chars\u001b[39m    \u001b[11;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                   "]
[0.001, "o", "                                                                            \r\n\u001b[97mImported (549 functions). Quick census of the DLL's core logic: who uses the ABE strings and GUIDs.\u001b[14;33H\u001b[90mstring\u001b[Crefs(stealc_abe_helper_blob) · 2\u001b[2C chars\u001b[39m \u001b[16;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ string_refs(stealc_abe_helper_blob) · 273 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ decomp_function(0x140001e28) · 205 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ decomp_function(FUN_140001210) · 7939 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mThe DLL's main worker \u001b[93mFUN_140001210\u001b[97m is fully conclusive. Let me grab the pipe-name derivation for completeness.\u001b[25;59H\u001b[90m73c\u001b[4C2306\u001b[28;5H\u001b[97mpipe name suffix is derived from the system volume serial number\u001b[C(G\u001b[CtVolumeInformationA on the Windows drive + LCG mixing constants\r\n0x14A30B/0x96BD8AAF) — both host and DLL compute it independently to rendezvous on the same pipe. Now posting the task-9 evidence and renaming the\r\nkey functions.\u001b[39m                                                             \u001b[42;83H\u001b[90mctx: 2 · in: 5,747,895 · out: 101\u001b[C807\u001b[12C84\u001b[2C702\u001b[7C8483\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.009, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mGoogle Chrome's Elevation Service (IElevator)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (both verified byte-by-byte against the known Chromium elevation_service GUIDs, little-endian field\r\norder)\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mDLL worker \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mFUN_140001210\u001b[1m (child) — full decompiled flow:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                         \u001b[9;1H\u001b[94m1. \u001b[93mResolves kernel32/shlwapi/shell32/oleaut32/ole32/crypt32 at runtime (LoadLibraryA/GetProcAddress)\r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m Builds pipe name \\\\.\\pipe\\ + suffix from FUN_14000173c:\u001b[1m suffix = hex digest derived from the system drive's volume serial number\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m(GetVolumeInformationA + LCG mixing consts 0x14A30B/0x96BD8AAF) — deterministic, so host and DLL compute the same pipe name independently, no\r\nparameters needed\u001b[39m                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m SHGetFolderPathA(CSIDL 0x1c=LOCALAPPDATA) + \\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Local State; FUN_140001000 extracts the app_bound_encrypted_key JSON value,\r\nbase64-decodes it (crypt32), expects the APPB prefix\u001b[39m                           \r\n\u001b[94m4. \u001b[93mOpens the host's pipe (CreateFileA GENERIC_WRITE, WaitNamedPipeA retry loop)\r\n\u001b[94m5.\u001b[93m CoInitializeEx → CoCreateInstance(CLSID_Elevator, NULL, CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER=4, IID_IElevatorChrome) → CoSetProxyBlanket(PKT_PRIVACY=6,\r\nIMPERSONATE=3, EOAC_DYNAMIC_CLOAKING=0x40) → calls the\u001b[1m IElevator::DecryptData\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m vtable method on the key blob. This COM service path-validates its\r\ncaller — which is WHY the code must run inside a spawned Chrome process (the Early-Bird APC injection of task 8)\r\n\u001b[94m6. \u001b[93mHex-encodes the recovered \u001b[1m32-byte key\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m with 0123456789abcdef (64 chars) and WriteFiles it to the pipe\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                                                                         \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mHost side (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mFUN_14001f100\u001b[1m @ 0x14001f100, caller of the injector):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m builds browser dir from CSIDL 0x1a/0x1c, checks Local State exists\r\n(GetFileAttributesA — ptr DAT_1400b4c58), and only if the browser-descriptor flag param_2[0xd] (ABE-capable) is set:\r\nConvertStringSecurityDescriptorToSecurityDescriptorA (DAT_1400b4de0, blob iETmemwM… @ 0x14007dab0) →\u001b[1m CreateNamedPipeA\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (DAT_1400b4db0 ← blob @\r\n0x14007df78) → FUN_14003a048 injects the DLL into the freshly spawned browser process (name from the browser descriptor) →\u001b[1m ReadFile\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (DAT_1400b4dd0 ←\r\nblob @ 0x14007df50) up to 0x1ff bytes = the hex key → key is combined with report strings and used downstream for cookie/credential decryption\r\n(AES-256-GCM \"v20\" blobs).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mVerdict:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the embedded PE is\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m a second-stage payload and is never written to disk; it is Stealc v2's\u001b[1m in-memory ABE-bypass helper DLL\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (64-bit,\r\nreflective/sRDI form, no exports), used solely to obtain Chrome's app-bound AES key from inside a trusted Chrome process. Pipe-name suffixes,\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[93minjection APIs, and all consuming code are enumerated above (tasks 7/8).\u001b[32;89H\u001b[39m \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠸ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngin\u001b[Cer(Ca\u001b[Clisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: ca\u001b[Cling create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
