[0.009, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mVerdict:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the\u001b[Cembedded PE is\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m a second-stage payload and is never written to disk; it is Stealc v2's\u001b[1m in-memory ABE-bypass helper DLL\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (64-bit,\r\nreflective/sRDI form, no exports), used solely to obtain Chrome's app-bound AES key from inside a trusted Chrome process. Pipe-name suffixes,\r\ninjection APIs, an\u001b[C all consuming\u001b[Ccode are enumerated above (tasks 7/8).\u001b[39m                                                                       \r\n                                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ rename_function(FUN_14003a048) · 145 chars\u001b[11;57H1f100\u001b[6C4\u001b[13;57H3c2ac\u001b[6C9\u001b[15;49Hstealc_abe_helper_blob) · 144 chars\u001b[17;77H5\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[19;33H\u001b[90ms\u001b[Ct_comme\u001b[Ct(14008acd0) · 97 chars\u001b[39m                  \u001b[21;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                     \r\n\u001b[97mNow completing the question's tasks with the evidence comments and marking it solved.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ complete_task(ReverseEngineer(Callisto)) · 242 chars\u001b[39m \u001b[26;77H\u001b[90m31\u001b[28;77H40\u001b[30;1H○\u001b[31Cset_status(#q-emb\u001b[Cdd\u001b[Cd-pe) · …runn\u001b[Cng\u001b[39m               \u001b[32;91H   \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mTh\u001b[2Cking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mRev\u001b[CrseE\u001b[Cgineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling set_status\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[34;2H"]
[0.045, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ rename_function(stealc_abe_helper_blob) · 144 chars\u001b[39m                                                            \r\n                                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ rename_function(stealc_abe_helper_blob) · 145 chars\u001b[9;33Hs\u001b[Ct_comme\u001b[Ct(14008acd0) · 97 chars\u001b[39m         \u001b[11;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                              \r\n\u001b[97mNow completing the question's tasks with the evidence comments and marking it solved.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                        \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ complete_task(ReverseEngineer(Callisto)) · 242 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ complete_task(ReverseEngineer(Callisto)) · 231 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ complete_task(ReverseEngineer(Callisto)) · 240 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                               \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ set_status(#q-embedded-pe) · 11619 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-family-attribution\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                             \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mSupporting evidence from #q-embedded-pe (now solved), confirming the v2 ABE-helper trait predicted in !62:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the PE embedded in .data @ 0x890d0 (VA\r\n0x14008ACD0) i\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93ms a 64-bit, export-less helper DLL in sRDI shellcode-polyglot form (MZ header is executable, chains to a reflective loader appended at\r\n+0x25000; build timestamp 2025-01-10). The host injects it into a freshly spawned browser process via\u001b[1m CreateProcessA(CREATE_SUSPENDED) →\r\nVirtualAllocEx(RWX) → WriteProcessMemory(0x25600 bytes) → QueueUserAPC → ResumeThread\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (Early-Bird APC; all APIs proven via the\r\nbase64+RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\") string table). Inside Chrome it calls the\u001b[1m IElevator COM elevation service (CLSID {708860E0-F641-4611-8895-7D867DD3675B}, IID\r\n{463ABECF-410D-407F-8AF5-0DF35A005CC8})\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m to decrypt app_bound_encrypted_key from Local State, then writes the 32-byte key (hex) back to the host over\r\na named pipe whose name both sides derive from the volume serial number. This is the Stealc v2 Chrome app-bound-encryption bypass — a hard v2-over-v1\r\ndiscriminator. Details/evidence: !77 !78 !79.\u001b[39m                        \u001b[32;90H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling creat\u001b[C_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
