[0.028, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Callisto) · ▸ flag_for_review(ReverseEngineer(Callisto)) · 889 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m⚑ flagged for analyst review: GUID-name mapping and IElevator vtable slot identified partly from domain recall\u001b[10;1H🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask complete — #q-embedded-pe solved.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Summary of what was established, all evidence posted as comments !77/!78/!79:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m1. The embedded PE (task 7):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m A real 64-bit\u001b[1m DLL\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (machine 0x8664, characteristics 0x2022, P\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.004, "o", "\u001b[97mE32+, MSVC linker 14.42, timestamp\u001b[1m 2025-01-10 14:56:39 UTC\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m —\r\nverified by two independent decodes). Stored\u001b[1m pre-mapped\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (raw ptrs == RVAs), SizeOfImage 0x25000, sections .text/.rdata/.data/.pdata/.reloc,\u001b[1m no export\r\ntable\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (dir zeroed, byte-verified). Its MZ header is weaponized:\u001b[93m MZ\u001b[97m is followed by shellcode that calls\u001b[1m base+0x25000\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, where a reflective sRDI loader\r\n(CRC32-poly API hashing, PEB walk) is appended — total blob 0x25600 bytes. Carved and imported as\u001b[93m ste\u001b[Clc_abe_helper_blob\u001b[97m (SHA256\u001b[93m 55494\u001b[C74…5c3b8f\u001b[97m).\u001b[39m  \r\n                                                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m2. VA + consumers (task 8):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m File 0x890d0 →\u001b[1m VA 0x14008ACD0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (.data+0xCD0). Single consumer:\u001b[93m inject_abe_helper_dll_earlybird_apc\u001b[97m @ 0x14003a048\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m(renamed), which performs\u001b[1m Early-Bird APC injection\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: CreateProcessA(CREATE_SUSPENDED) → VirtualAllocEx(RWX, 0x25600) → WriteProcessMemory of the blob\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97m→ QueueUserAPC(remote base) → ResumeThread → WaitForSingleObject → VirtualFreeEx. Every API identity was\u001b[3m proven\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m by extracting each pointer's feeding\r\nciphertext from\u001b[93m init_d\u001b[Ccrypted_string_table\u001b[97m and decrypting it with base64→RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\"). No disk write, no blob decryption — it's copied as-is.\u001b[39m  \r\n                                             \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m3. Purpose (task 9):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m It is Stealc v2's\u001b[1m Chrome App-Bound Encryption bypass helper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, not a second stage. Inside the injected browser process it parses\r\n\u001b[93mLocal State\u001b[97m for\u001b[93m app_bound_encrypted_key\u001b[97m (APPB prefix), calls the\u001b[1m IElevator COM elevation service\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (CLSID {708860E0-…}, IID {463ABECF-…},\r\nCoS\u001b[CtProxyB\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97mlanket\u001b[CPKT_PRIVACY + dynamic cloaking)\u001b[Ct\u001b[C decrypt\u001b[Cth\u001b[2C32-byte key, hex-encodes\u001b[Cit, and writes it back \u001b[Co the host over\u001b[Ca\u001b[1m named pipe whose\r\nname both sides independently derive from the system volume serial number\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. The host (\u001b[93mchromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key\u001b[97m @ 0x14001f100) reads the key\r\nfor downstream v20 cookie/credential decryption.\u001b[39m                                      \u001b[29;1H\u001b[97mCross-posted the v2-discriminator evidence to #q-family-attribution, renamed the key functions in both programs, and flagged the one recall-based\r\nGUID-name\u001b[Cmappi\u001b[Cg for\u001b[Canalyst\u001b[Creview.\u001b[39m                                                                         \u001b[42;98H\u001b[90m483\u001b[C2\u001b[C8\u001b[10C5\u001b[2C0\u001b[13C588\u001b[C824\u001b[7C9430\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[34;2H"]
