[0.006, "o", "\u001b[4;1H \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Callisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask complete — #q-embedded-pe solved.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Summary of what was established, all evidence posted as comments !77/!78/!79:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                          \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m1. The emb\u001b[Cdded\u001b[CPE (task 7):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m A real 64-bit\u001b[1m DLL\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m(mac\u001b[Cine 0x8664, characteristics 0x2022, PE32+,\u001b[CMSVC linker 14.42, timestamp\u001b[1m 2025-01-10 14:56:39 UTC\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m —\r\nverified by two independent decodes). Stored\u001b[1m pre-mapped\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (raw ptrs == RVAs), SizeOfImage 0x25000, sections .text/.rdata/.data/.pdata/.reloc,\u001b[1m no export\r\ntable\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (dir zeroed, byte-verified). Its MZ header is weaponized:\u001b[93m MZ\u001b[97m is followed by shellcode that cal\u001b[Cs\u001b[1m base+0x25000\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, where a reflective sRDI loader\u001b[39m  \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m(CRC32-pol\u001b[2CAPI\u001b[Chashing, PEB walk) is\u001b[Cappen\u001b[Ced — total blob 0x25600 byte\u001b[C. Carv\u001b[Cd and imported as\u001b[93m stealc_abe_helper_blob\u001b[97m (SHA256\u001b[93m 55494e74…5c3b8f\u001b[97m).\u001b[39m   \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m2. VA + consumers (task 8):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m File 0x890d0 →\u001b[1m VA 0x14008ACD0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (.data+\u001b[CxCD0). Single consumer:\u001b[93m inject_abe_helper_dll_ea\u001b[Clybird_apc\u001b[97m @ 0x14003a048\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[97m(renamed), which performs\u001b[1m Early-Bird APC injection\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: CreateProcessA(CREATE_SUSPENDED) → VirtualAllocEx(RWX, 0x25600) → WriteProcessMemory of the blob\r\n→ QueueUserAPC(remote base)\u001b[C→ R\u001b[CsumeThread → WaitForSingleObject → VirtualFreeEx. Every API identity was\u001b[3m proven\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m by extracting\u001b[Ceach pointer's feeding\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97mciphertext\u001b[Cfrom\u001b[93m init_decrypted_string_table\u001b[97m and decrypting it with base64→RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\"). No disk write, no blob\u001b[Cdec\u001b[Cyption — it's copied as-is.\u001b[39m \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m3. Purpose (task 9):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m It is Stealc v2's\u001b[1m Chrome App-Bound Encryption bypass helper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, not a second stage. Inside the injected br\u001b[Cwser process it\u001b[Cparses\r\n\u001b[93mLocal State\u001b[97m for\u001b[93m app_bound_encrypted_key\u001b[97m (APPB prefix), calls the\u001b[1m IElevator COM elevation service\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (CLSID {708860E0-…}, IID {463ABECF-…},\r\nCoSetProxyBlanket PKT_PRIVACY + dynamic cloaking) to decrypt the 32-byte key, hex-encode\u001b[C it, and writes \u001b[Ct back\u001b[Cto the host ov\u001b[3Ca\u001b[1m named pipe whose\r\nname both sides independently derive from the system vo\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m\u001b[1mlume serial number\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. The host (\u001b[93mchromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key\u001b[97m @\u001b[C0x14001f100) reads the key\r\nf\u001b[Cr downstre\u001b[Cm v20 cookie/credential decryptio\u001b[C.\u001b[39m                                                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97mCross-po\u001b[2Ced the v2-discriminator evi\u001b[2Cnce \u001b[Co #q-family-attribution, renamed the key functions in both programs, and flagged the one recall-based\r\nGUID-name mapping for analyst review.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[39m                                   \r\n\u001b[97m■ Swarm(Io) finished: 4 succeeded, 0 failed\r\n\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mmain · ▸ follow_link(#q-string-decryption) · 10028 chars\u001b[32;89H\u001b[39m           \u001b[C             \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mmain\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling follow_l\u001b[Cnk\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
