[0.039, "o", "\u001b[32;114H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇\u001b[42;99H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m7\u001b[2C4\u001b[C2\u001b[9C11\u001b[C886\u001b[13C88\u001b[C378\u001b[7C816\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.006, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1m3. Purpose (task 9):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m It is Stealc v2's\u001b[1m Chrome App-Bound Encryption bypass helper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, not a second stage. Inside the injected browser process it parses\r\n\u001b[93mLocal State\u001b[97m for\u001b[93m app_bound_encrypted_key\u001b[97m (APPB prefix),\u001b[Cc\u001b[Clls \u001b[Che\u001b[1m IElevator COM elevation service\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (CLSID\u001b[C{\u001b[C08860E0-…}, IID {463ABECF-…},\r\nCoSetProxyBlanket PKT_PRIVACY + dynamic cloaking) to decrypt the 32-byte key, hex-encodes it, and writes it back to the host over a\u001b[1m named pipe whose\r\nname both si\u001b[2Cs\u001b[Cindependently derive from the system volume serial number\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. The host (\u001b[93mchromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key\u001b[97m @ 0x14001f100) reads the key\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mfo\u001b[C downstream v20 cooki\u001b[C/credential decryption.\u001b[39m                                                                                                     \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97mCross-posted the v2-discriminator evidenc\u001b[C to #q-fami\u001b[Cy-attribution, renamed th\u001b[C key functions\u001b[Cin both programs, and flagged the one recall-based\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mGUID-name mapping for analyst review.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m■\u001b[CSwarm(Io) finished:\u001b[C4 \u001b[Cucceed\u001b[Cd, 0 failed\u001b[39m                                                                                                         \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mmain · ▸ follow_link(#q-string-decryption) · 10028 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-crypto-keys\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mAnswered via #q-string-decryption (evidence !60, !61, !73, !74):\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m- The detector's 18 \"candidate symmetric keys\" (!8–!25 under #fn-140002b6c) are\u001b[1m not keys\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — they are mid-string carvings of base64(RC4)\u001b[3m ciphertext\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mstring blobs (e.g. !8 jE/hfE0XsWHHzMlk/dS1Tg== decrypts to the API name GdipDisposeImage).\r\n- The\u001b[1m only real embedded key is RC4 key\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m CgeOvEO7hu (10 ASCII bytes @ 0x14007d6e0, loaded into global DAT_1400b0b30 by init_rc4_key_and_strings @\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93m0x140001ee0).\u001b[39m                        \r\n\u001b[93m- What it protects: the entire embedded string table (~200 blobs decrypted pre-main by init_decrypted_string_table @ 0x140002b6c via\r\ndecrypt_string_b64_rc4 @ 0x140007d04) — including the C2 endpoint 45.93.20.28 + /3d15e67552d448ff.php, runtime-resolved API names, file-grab masks,\r\nregistry paths, and report templates. It does\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m encrypt victim files — no ransomware use (see #q-ransomware).\r\n- A plaintext constant 512e7bd984984fb6 (build/campaign ID) is set alongside the key.\r\n- Whether the same RC4 key also protects C2 traffic is being traced under #q-c2-protocol.\u001b[32;111H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThink\u001b[2Cg…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mmain\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create_comme\u001b[Ct\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.078, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[93mFor each check, give the function address, the decompiled logic, decrypted strings/constants involved, and the action taken on trigger (exit? skip?).\r\nSpecific\u001b[Clly:\u001b[39m                                                                                                                          \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m- The locale check: exact LANGIDs and behavior.\u001b[39m                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m- The mutex: its (decrypted) name and semantics (anti-reinfection?).\r\n- Any date/expiry kill switch (compare SystemTime against hardcoded date).\r\n- Computer-name/username checks (HAL9TH, JohnDoe), anti-VM, anti-debug beyond CRT noise.\u001b[39m                                                         \r\n                                     \r\n\u001b[93m📌 #q-persistence — Does the sample establish any persistence (registry, services, tasks, startup)?\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mStealc historically installs\u001b[1m no persistence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (smash-and-grab stealer, often self-deletes) — see #q-family-attribution !63. Verify this negative\r\nproperly:\u001b[39m                                  \u001b[17;1H\u001b[93m- Search decrypted strings (base64→RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\") per #q-string-decryption) and plaintext strings for: Run/RunOnce keys, CurrentVersion\\Run,\r\nservice APIs (CreateService/OpenSCManager), schtasks/Task Scheduler COM, Startup folder paths, WMI event subscription.\r\n- Ch\u001b[Cck the runtime-re\u001b[Colved API name table (initializers @ 0x140002b6c / 0x140001ee0) for persistence-related APIs.\r\n- Note the SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Uninstall string is for installed-app enumeration, not persistence.\r\n- Conclude: persistence present or absent, with the search evidence.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m📌 #q-bu\u001b[Ck-\u001b[Ctrin\u001b[Cs\u001b[C— Bulk-decrypt the full RC4/base64 \u001b[Ctring table\u001b[Cand publish the complete plaintext list\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mScheme proven in #q-string-decryption (!60/!61/!73): every base64 blob referenced\u001b[Cby init_decrypted_string_ta\u001b[Cle @\u001b[C0x140002b6c and\u001b[39m              \r\n\u001b[93minit_rc4_key_and_strings @ 0x140001ee0 decrypts with base64_decode then RC4(key=\"CgeOvEO7hu\").\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93mD\u001b[Cveloper task: write a Rhai script that wa\u001b[Cks those two\u001b[Ci\u001b[Citializer functions (or scans .r\u001b[Cata \u001b[Cor base64 tokens), d\u001b[Ccrypts ev\u001b[Cry\u001b[Cblob, and\u001b[Cpo\u001b[Ct\u001b[C\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mthe\u001b[1m complete decrypted string list\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (address → plaintext),\u001b[Cgrouped roughly by category (C2/network, API names, file paths/masks, registry keys, report\r\ntemplates, browser/wallet targets, other). This is the master IOC source for\u001b[C#q-capabilities and the final report. Flag any plaintexts that look like\r\nadditional endpoints, mutex names, or campaign IDs.\u001b[39m                                      \u001b[32;111H   \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠏ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mTh\u001b[2Cking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mmain\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling cr\u001b[Cate_pos\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
