[0.008, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mSpecifically:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m- The loca\u001b[Ce check: exact LANGIDs and behavior.\r\n- The mutex: its (decrypted) name and semantics (anti-reinfection?).\u001b[8;3HAny\u001b[Cdate/\u001b[Cxpiry kill switch (compare SystemTime against hardcoded date).\u001b[9;3HComputer-name/username checks (HAL9TH, JohnDoe), anti-VM, anti-debug beyond CRT noise.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                          \r\n\u001b[93m📌 #q-persistence — Does\u001b[Ct\u001b[2C sample establish any pers\u001b[Cstence (registry, services, ta\u001b[Cks, startup)?\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mStealc historically installs\u001b[1m no persistence\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (smash-and-grab stealer, often self-deletes) — see #q-family-attribution !63. Verify this negative\r\nproperly:\u001b[39m                                                                                               \r\n                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[93m- Sea\u001b[Cch decrypted strings (base64→RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\") per #q-string-decryption) and plaintext strings for: Run/RunOnce keys, CurrentVersion\\Run,\r\nservice APIs (CreateService/OpenSCManager), schtasks/Task Scheduler COM, Startup folder paths, WMI event subscription.\u001b[17;3HCheck th\u001b[C \u001b[Cun\u001b[Cime-resolved API name tabl\u001b[C (initializ\u001b[2Cs @ 0x140002b6c / 0x140001ee0) for persistence-\u001b[Celated APIs.\u001b[39m                           \r\n\u001b[93m- Note the SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Cu\u001b[CrentVersion\\Uninstall string is\u001b[Cfor instal\u001b[Ced-a\u001b[Cp enumeration, not pe\u001b[Csiste\u001b[Cce.\u001b[19;4Hon\u001b[Clude:\u001b[Cpers\u001b[Cstence pr\u001b[Csent or absent, with \u001b[Che sea\u001b[Cch evidence.\u001b[39m                                                \r\n                                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[93m📌 #q-b\u001b[Clk-string\u001b[C — Bulk-decrypt the full\u001b[CRC4/bas\u001b[C64 string table and publish the complete plaintext list\u001b[36m\u001b[1m main\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mScheme proven in #q-string-decryption (!60/!61/!73): every base64 blob referenced by init_decrypted_string_table @ 0x140002b6c and\r\ninit_rc4_\u001b[Cey_and_\u001b[Ctrings @ 0x140001e\u001b[C0 decrypts with base64_decod\u001b[2Cthen RC4(key=\"CgeOvEO7hu\").\u001b[39m                 \r\n                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93mDeveloper task: write a Rhai script that walks those\u001b[Ctwo initializer functions (or scans .rdata for base64 tokens), decrypts every blob, and posts\r\nthe\u001b[1m complete decrypted string list\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (address → plaintext), grouped roughly by category (C2/network, API names, file paths/masks, registry keys, report\r\nt\u001b[Cmp\u001b[Cat\u001b[Cs, browse\u001b[C/wallet targets, o\u001b[2Cer). This is the master IOC source for #q-capabilities and the final\u001b[Creport. Flag any plaintexts th\u001b[Ct lo\u001b[Ck like\r\nadditional endpoints, mutex names,\u001b[Cor campaign IDs.\u001b[39m                                                                                                  \r\n                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mmain · ▸ set_status(#q-crypto-keys) · …running\u001b[39m   \u001b[32;114H \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠙ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mmain\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: ca\u001b[Cling s\u001b[Ct_status\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
