[0.000, "o", "                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m- The same function also makes two\u001b[1m plaintext\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m(non-RC4) global assignments: DAT_1400b0b30 ← \"CgeOvEO7hu\" (the RC4 key) and DAT_1400b05f0 ←\r\n\"512e7bd984984fb6\" (build/campaign ID) — consistent with !61.\r\n-\u001b[1m Anomaly worth chasing for #q-anti-analysis:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the first four decrypted strings are the 2-char fragments \"11\", \"04\", \"20\", \"25\" (slots 0x1400b09f0 /\r\n0x1400b0e90 / 0x1400b1ab0 / 0x1400b1e10) — stored right next to GetUserDefaultLangID/GetLocalTime-class APIs. These look like\u001b[1m date kill-switch\r\ncomponents (11 / 04 / 20+25 → 11-Apr-2025?)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. Xref consumers of those four slots to confirm.\u001b[23;2H\u001b[1m Correction to !73:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the\u001b[Cbinary's blob at 0x14007e060 is jE78T3wMsHTGy/xf/9a3WE6kuQ== (byte-verified: 6a 45 37 38 54 33 77 ...) → GetCurrentProcessId\r\n(correct spelling). !73's \"GetCerrentProcessId (sic, author's typo)\" came from transcribing T2w for T3w — there is\u001b[1m no m\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[93m\u001b[1misspelled API in the binary\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m,\r\nso it is not usable as a family fingerprint.\u001b[39m                                                                                                       \r\n                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Sinope)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                 \r\n\u001b[97mFormat is\u001b[93m %p\u001b[97m → the event name's first token is the image-base-relative pointer printed as 16 hex digits. Tasks 17/18 are now fully evidenced. Now for\r\nthe date kill switch and HAL9TH/JohnDoe checks — first, compute what the encrypted blobs for \"HAL9TH\"/\"JohnDoe\" would look like, and decompile the\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mmain dispatcher:\u001b[39m                            \u001b[34;2H"]
