[0.102, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m Verified the section header myself\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (raw bytes @0x230):\u001b[93m .rdata\u001b[97m raw 0x6e200, size 0x1a200, VA 0x6f000 →\u001b[1m VA = 0x140000000 + file_offset + 0xe00\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. The\r\ntask prompt's \"raw 0x71800 → VA 0x140073000\" (delta 0x1800) was wrong; mapping was functionally confirmed because my decrypt at VA 0x14007d838 →\r\n\u001b[93m45.93.20.2\u001b[C\u001b[97m matches the earlier independent decrypt (!73) at that exact address.\r\n- Script\u001b[93m stealc_fulltable_sweep\u001b[97m (promoted to the library as\u001b[93m scan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m): scans the entire raw\u001b[93m .rdata\u001b[97m for NUL-terminated base64-charset\r\ntokens, decodes each via the native pipeline\u001b[93m base64 → RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")\u001b[97m, keeps ≥95%-printable results.\r\n\u001b[39m                                             \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## Results\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                              \r\n                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m 270 decrypted strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m at min_len=8,\u001b[1m +6 real short tokens\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m at min_len=4 (incl. the date-killswitch quartet\u001b[93m 11/04/20/25\u001b[97m next to the RC4 key) =\u001b[1m 276\r\ntotal\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, posted\u001b[1m in full\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m as !82/!83 under #q-bulk-strings. Independently cross-validated by sibling Thebe's xref-walk (!84, also 276 pairs).\r\n- All\u001b[1m 67 rejected tokens individually accounted for\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m as plaintext strings that merely match the base64 charset (CRT locale names, wininet imports, the\r\nkey itself, build ID\u001b[93m 512e7bd984984fb6\u001b[97m) —\u001b[1m no encrypted blob left undecoded in .rdata\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## Ransomware sweep (posted as !85, #q-ransomware marked solved)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m ZERO matches\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (across all 276 plaintex\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97mts):\u001b[93m vssadmin, shadow, wmic, bcdedit, wbadmin, cipher, ransom, readme, recover, restore, bitcoin, btc, monero,\r\ndecrypt your, all your files, .locked, MoveFile, CryptEncrypt\u001b[97m.\r\n-\u001b[1m Second independent route\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m:\u001b[93m grep_bytes\u001b[97m over the entire 745,472-byte file, ASCII+UTF-16LE, case-insensitive →\u001b[1m 0 matches\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m for all 15 ransomware keywords\r\n(coverage: 0x0–0xb6000).\u001b[39m                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[93m encrypted\u001b[97m: 3 hits — all browser credential-store JSON field names (\u001b[C\u001b[93mncrypted_key\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m encryptedUsername\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m encryptedP\u001b[Cssword\u001b[97m) = stealer semantics.\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[93mGetVolumeInformationA\u001b[97m: 1 hit, HWID fingerprinting.\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m Grabber patterns\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!86): single embedded wildcard mask list = Steam creds (\u001b[93mssfn*,config.vdf,...\u001b[97m); otherwise only server-driven schema keys\r\n(\u001b[93mcsidl/start_path/masks/recursive/max_size\u001b[97m) — enumeration feeds\u001b[1m read-and-exfiltrate\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93mupload_file\u001b[97m opcode), with no encrypt/rename API pair anywhere in\r\nthe re\u001b[Colved-import\u001b[Cset.\u001b[39m                                                                                                             \r\n                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97mCalibration note (also flagged for the analyst): this\u001b[1m excludes ransomware strings/APIs\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m from the binary; the C2-pushed\u001b[93m loader\u001b[97m capability (IEX cradle,\r\nmsiexec) means arbitrary follow-on delivery remains possible by design — that is downloader capability, not ransomware capability in this binary.\u001b[32;97H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠧\u001b[42;97H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
