[0.015, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m45.93.20.28\u001b[97m matches the earlier independent d\u001b[Ccrypt (!73) at that exact addre\u001b[Cs.\u001b[39m                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m- Script\u001b[93m stealc_fulltable_sweep\u001b[C\u001b[97m(promoted to\u001b[Cth\u001b[C library as\u001b[93m scan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m): scans the entir\u001b[C raw\u001b[93m .rdata\u001b[97m for NUL-terminated base64-charset\r\ntokens, decodes each via the nat\u001b[Cve \u001b[Cipeline\u001b[93m base64 → RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")\u001b[97m, keep\u001b[C ≥95%-printable results.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## Results\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                            \u001b[10;1H\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m 270 decrypted strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m at min_len=8,\u001b[1m +6 real short tokens\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m a\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mt min_len=4 (incl. the date-killswitch quartet\u001b[93m 11/04/20/25\u001b[97m next to the RC4 key) =\u001b[1m 276\r\ntotal\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, posted\u001b[1m in full\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m as !82/!83 under #q-bulk-strings. Independently cross-validated by sibling Thebe's xref-walk (!84, also 276 pairs).\u001b[12;2H All\u001b[C\u001b[1m67 \u001b[Cejected tokens individually\u001b[Caccounted for\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m as plain\u001b[Cext strings that mer\u001b[Cly match the base64 charset (CRT local\u001b[C names, wininet imports, the\r\nkey itself, build ID\u001b[93m 512e7bd984984fb6\u001b[97m)\u001b[C—\u001b[1m no encrypted blob left undecoded in .rdata\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                                                     \r\n                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## Ransomware sweep (posted as !85, #q-ransomware marked solved)\u001b(B\u001b[m                    \u001b[17;1H\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m ZERO matches\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (across all 276 plaintexts):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m vssadmin, shadow, wmic, bcdedit, wbadmin, cipher, ransom, readme, recover, restore, bitcoin, btc, monero,\r\ndecrypt your, all your files, .locked, MoveFile, CryptEncrypt\u001b[97m.\u001b[19;3H\u001b[1mSecond ind\u001b[Cpendent route\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m:\u001b[93m grep_bytes\u001b[97m over the entire 745,472-byte file, ASCII+UTF-16LE, case-insensitive →\u001b[1m 0 matches\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m for all 15 ransomware keywords\r\n(coverage: 0x0–0xb6000).\u001b[39m                                      \u001b[21;2H\u001b[93m encrypted\u001b[97m: 3 hits — all browser credential-store JSON field names\u001b[C(\u001b[93mencrypted_key\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m encryptedUsername\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m encryptedPassword\u001b[97m) = steale\u001b[C semantics.\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[93mGetVolumeInformationA\u001b[97m: 1 hit, HWID fingerprinting.\u001b[23;2H\u001b[1m Grabber patterns\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!86):\u001b[Csingl\u001b[C emb\u001b[2Cded wildca\u001b[Cd\u001b[Cmask\u001b[Cl\u001b[Cst = St\u001b[Cam creds (\u001b[93mssfn*,confi\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mg.vdf,...\u001b[97m); otherwise only server-driven schema keys\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97m(\u001b[93mcsid\u001b[C/start_path/masks/recursive/max_size\u001b[97m) — e\u001b[Cumeration feeds\u001b[1m read-and-exfiltrate\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93mupload_file\u001b[97m opcode), with no encrypt/rename API pair anywhere in\r\nthe resolved-import set.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                   \r\n                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97mCalibration note (al\u001b[Co flagged for the analyst): this\u001b[1m excludes ransomware strings/APIs\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m from the binary; the C2-pushed\u001b[93m loader\u001b[97m capability (IEX cradle,\r\nmsiexec) means arbitrary follow-on delivery remains possible by design — that is downloader capability, not ransomware capability in this binary.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Carme) · ▸ search_memory(uFjuYiNSoX7G) · …running\u001b[39m                                                                              \u001b[32;94H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠧ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThink\u001b[2Cg…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mRevers\u001b[CEngineer(Ca\u001b[Cme)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling search\u001b[Cmemory\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[34;2H"]
