[0.010, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Leda)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m#q-bulk-strings is now\u001b[1m solved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. A library script named\u001b[93m scan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m already exists (a sibling agent promoted an equivalent sweep), so I\r\nwon't overwrite it — no need for a duplicate.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                 \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## Summary of what I did\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                        \r\n                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mScript\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93mbulk_decrypt_b64_rc4\u001b[97m, session): reads the entire\u001b[93m .rdata\u001b[97m section (0x14006f000, 107,008 bytes) from program memory, finds NUL-bounded\r\nbase64-charset C-string tokens ≥ 8 chars (337 candidates), decodes each with the native\u001b[93m decode_bytes\u001b[97m pipeline\u001b[93m base64 → RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")\u001b[97m, keeps\r\n100%-printable results (\u001b[1m270 plaintexts\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m), prints them grouped by category, and runs a persistence-keyword sweep. One bug found & fixed en route:\r\n\u001b[93mdecode_bytes\u001b[97m blobs iterate as\u001b[93m u8\u001b[97m, so the printable check had to index rather than compare iterator values against i64.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mPosted under #q-bulk-strings\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (comments !89,\u001b[C!90, !92,\u001b[C!93, !96, !98, !100, !102, !103): the complete 270-entry address → plaintext table in 7\r\ncategory groups — C2/network (15), registry (3) + Firefox DBs (3) + app targets (6), paths/masks (24), API names (122, two parts), report templates\r\n(30), JSON protocol/config/loader tokens (67) — plus the requested callouts:\u001b[20;1H-\u001b[1m Endpoints:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m exactly one —\u001b[93m 45.93.20.28\u001b[97m +\u001b[93m /3d15e67552d448ff.php\u001b[97m; no other URL/domain/IP anywhere in the table; the PowerShell\r\n\u001b[93miex(...).DownloadString('\u001b[97m cradle carries no embedded URL.\r\n- \u001b[1mMutex:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m no stored name; \u001b[93mCreateEventW\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mOpenEventW\u001b[97m resolved → runtime-built named event.\r\n- \u001b[1mCampaign/build ID:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m \u001b[93m512e7bd984984fb6\u001b[97m (plaintext constant, not RC4).\r\n- \u001b[1mPersistence sweep:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m zero Run/RunOnce/schtasks/service hits across all 270 plaintexts.\u001b[26;1H\u001b[1mConflict reconciled by byte-trace\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (comment !104, stance\u001b[3m disproves\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m on !73, plus a review flag): the famous \"GetCerrentProcessId (sic)\" is\u001b[1m not in this\r\nbinary\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — the token at 0x14007e060 is\u001b[93m jE78T3wM...\u001b[97m → correctly spelled\u001b[93m GetCurrentProcessId\u001b[97m (raw-file bytes, Ghidra memory, and\u001b[93m search_memory\u001b[97m all agree;\r\nthe\u001b[93m jE78T2wM\u001b[97m variant has 0 hits). The genuine author typo\u001b[93m Error dumping proccess list\u001b[97m @ 0x14007f030 stands. Two other decodes (\u001b[93m45.93.20.28\u001b[97m, the\r\n\u001b[93mContent-Type: application/json\u001b[97m header — whose trailing\u001b[93m \\r\\n\u001b[97m is literal backslash characters, byte-verified) were re-verified via independent raw-file\r\nroutes. Sibling agents' parallel tables (!82–!106) independently match mine entry-for-entry, including the same correction.\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
