[0.001, "o", "                     \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mOne correction, byte-verified:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the blob at\u001b[1m 0x14007e060\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m is jE78T3wMsHTGy/xf/9a3WE6kuQ== (raw read: 6a 45 37 38 54 33 77 4d 73 48 54 47 ... — note\r\nT3wM, matching the detector's mid-string carving T3wMsHTGy/... in !15), and base64→RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\") decrypts it to the ordinary GetCurrentProcessId\r\n(native decode hexdump: 47 65 74 43 75 72 72 65 6e 74 ...).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                              \r\n\u001b[93mThe \"GetCerrentProcessId (sic — author's \u001b[Cypo, good fam\u001b[Cly fingerprint)\" reading came from deco\u001b[Cing the\u001b[Ctranscribed\u001b[Ctoken\u001b[CjE78T2wMsHTGy/\u001b[C..\u001b[C(T2wM,\r\none base64 char off), which indeed yields GetCerrentProcessId\u001b[2CThat typo fingerprint does\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m exist in this binary — please don't carry it into\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[93mIOC/YARA material. Everything\u001b[Celse in the\u001b[Ctable\u001b[Cr\u001b[C-verified correct during the bulk decrypt (!88/!99/!105).\u001b[23;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Carme)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97mSix consumers. The key one for the grabber (near the rule-builder helpers) is \u001b[93mFUN_1400082d8\u001b[97m — decompile it to see what happens to enumerated files.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Carme) · ▸ decomp_function(FUN_1400082d8) · 14942 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                       \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Adrastea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[97mOther agents' parallel tables converge with mine (same 260-blob mapping, same GetCurrentProcessId correction, same 11/04/20/25 observation) — good\r\ncross-validation. Remaining: make the script's keyword list configurable and promote it to the library, plus a short pointer under #q-anti-analysis.\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
