[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mec | +ho=\u001b[C| \"11\"   -> global\u001b[C0x1400\u001b[C09f0\u001b[39m                                                          \r\n\u001b[93m0x14007d6f4 | +x8= | \"04\"   -> global 0x1400b0e90\r\n0x14007d6fc | +Rs= | \"20\"   -> global 0x1400b1ab0\r\n0x14007d704 | +R4= | \"25\"   -> global 0x1400b1e10\u001b[39m                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93m```\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                       \r\n\u001b[93mGetLocalTime/GetSystemTime are both in the resolved-API table and the build timestamp is 2025-04-02 — these look like a hardcoded expiry date\r\n(day=11? month=04? year=20+25?), matching the Stealc date-kill-switch trait (!63).\u001b[1m Field order is NOT verified\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — whoever owns this question should\r\nxref the four global slots (0x1400b09f0/0x1400b0e90/0x1400b1ab0/0x1400b1e10) to the comparing code and read the comparison order before asserting a\r\ndate.\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                                               \u001b[32;92H    \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠴ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mDeveloper(Adr\u001b[Cst\u001b[Ca)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: ca\u001b[Cling create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
