[0.014, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[93m```\r\nloop:  h = OpenEventW(0x1F0003, FALSE, name)\u001b[39m                             \r\n\u001b[93m       if (h) { CloseHandle(h); Sleep(0x100A /*4106 ms*/); goto loop; }\r\n       h = CreateEventW(NULL, FALSE /*auto-reset*/, FALSE /*non-signaled*/, name)\r\n       if (!h) ExitProcess(0);        // 0x14002a9f9\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[93m       ... payload ...; CloseHandle(h) at exit\u001b[39m                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[93m```\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mSemantics: it does NOT exit when another instance runs — it WAITS\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (poll every ~4.1 s) until the previous\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m instance's event handle disappears, then\r\nregisters its own. Single-instance serialization / anti-re-entrancy, not anti-reinfection-forever.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mEvent name (built at 0x14002a8d5–0x14002a968 into a wostringstream, extracted by\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mbasic_stringbuf::str\u001b[1m = FUN_14002e6d0):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m L\"<%p of\r\n0x140007c78>_<ComputerName>_<UserName>\"\r\n\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93m- First token: wWinMain streams the raw\u001b[1m function pointer\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m &build_string_suka\u001b[1m (0x140007c78)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m into the stream; FID-matched\r\nstd::num_put<wchar_t>::do_put(..., const void*) @ 0x14002db70 formats it with the literal \"%p\" @ 0x140081624 (bytes 25 70 00) → 16 uppercase hex\r\ndigits, e.g. 0000000140\u001b[C07C78 at the preferred \u001b[Case (varies with ASLR per boot, but identical for every concurrently running copy of the module, so\r\nthe guar\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93md still works).\u001b[39m                          \r\n\u001b[93m- Separator: wide L\"_\" @ 0x1400814a8 (bytes 5f 00).\r\n- get_computer_name_w_str @ 0x140037d90 (GetComputerNameW, 16-wchar buffer) and get_user_name_w_str @ 0x140037cf4 (GetUserNameW, 0x101-wchar buffer).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[93mEx\u001b[Cmple on a default-base load: 0000000140007C78_DESKTOP-ABC1234_vi\u001b[Ctim.\u001b[39m                                                                          \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[93mAmusing detail: 0x140007c78 is a helper that builds the string\u001b[1m \"suka\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m from the space-padded literal \"suka \" @ 0x14007d6a8 (Russian profanity; also\r\ngenuinely called by FUN_140026214 in the payload). The developer appa"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mrently streamed the function itself instead of its result, so operator<< bound\r\nto const void* and the event name got a pointer instead of \"suka\". Good family/build fingerprint either way.\u001b[32;92H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Sinope"]
