[0.008, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m       ... payload ...; CloseHandle(h) at exit\u001b[6;1H\u001b[39m                                            \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mSemantics: it does NOT exit when another instance runs — it WAITS\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (\u001b[Coll every ~4.1 s) until the previous instance's event handle disappears, then\r\nregisters its own. Single-instance serialization \u001b[C anti-re-e\u001b[Ctrancy, not anti-r\u001b[Cinfection-forever.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mEvent name (built at 0x14002a8d5–0x14002a968 into a wostringstream, extracted by\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m basic_stringbuf::str\u001b[1m = FUN_14002e6d0):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m L\"<%p of\r\n0x140007c78>_<ComputerName>_<UserName>\"\u001b[13;1H- First token: wWinMain streams the raw\u001b[1m fu\u001b[Cc\u001b[Cion poi\u001b[Cter\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m &build_string_suka\u001b[1m (0x140007c78)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m in\u001b[Co the stream; FID-match\u001b[Cd\u001b[39m                           \r\n\u001b[93mstd::num_pu\u001b[C<wchar_t>::do_put(...,\u001b[Cconst void*) @ 0x14002db70 formats \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mi\u001b[2Cwi\u001b[Ch the literal \"%p\" @ 0x140081624 (bytes 25 70 00) → 16 uppercase hex\r\ndigits, e.g. 0000000140007C78 at the preferred base (varies with ASLR per boot, but identical for every concurrently running copy of the module, so\r\nthe guard still works).\u001b[39m                                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[93m- Separator: wide L\"_\" @ 0x1400814\u001b[C8 (bytes 5f 00).\r\n- get_computer_name_w_str @ 0x140037d90 (GetComputerNameW, 16-wchar buffer) and get_user_name_w_str @ 0x140037cf4 (GetUserNameW, 0x101-wchar buffer).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[93mExample on a def\u001b[Cul\u001b[C-base load: 0000000140007C78_DESKTOP-ABC1234_victim.\u001b[39m                                                                        \r\n                                                                              "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93mAmusing \u001b[Ceta\u001b[2C:\u001b[C0x140007c78 is a helper that builds the string\u001b[1m \"suka\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m from the space-padded literal \"suka \" @ 0x14007d6a8 (Russian profanity; also\r\ngenuinely calle\u001b[C by FUN_140026214 in\u001b[Cthe payload). The developer apparently streamed the function itself instead of its result, so operator<< bound\r\nto const void* and the event name got a\u001b[Cpointer inste\u001b[Cd of\u001b[C\"suka\". Good family/build fingerprint either way.\u001b[39m                                         \u001b[26;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Elara)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                               \r\n\u001b[97mFormat at 0x140082610 =\u001b[93m %08lX-%04hX-%04hX-%02hhX...\u001b[97m — a GUID-style HWID from the volume serial. FUN_140028978 = loader type-0 handler: download to\r\nCSIDL folder + random name +\u001b[93m .exe\u001b[97m, then ShellExecu\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97mteExA (verb\u001b[93m runas\u001b[97m if the run_as_admin flag is set), 10 retries.\u001b[39m                                 \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97mMy context is getting tight — posting evidence comments now.\u001b[39m                                                \u001b[34;2H"]
[0.014, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mTask 10 — HTTP send/receive functions + transport identified.\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m   \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mCore sender: \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mFUN_14000b384\u001b[1m @ 0x14000b384\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — (outResp, hostWide, uriWide, bodyString). Decompiled sequence (all pointers runtime-resolved):\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m (*DAT_1400b4d70)(&DAT_14007f5\u001b[Cc,0,0,0) =\u001b[1m InternetOpenW\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m with\u001b[1m user-agent = EMPTY wide string\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (read @ 0x14007f5cc = 00 00 00 00, immediately before\r\nL\"POST\" and the Content-Type literal in .rdata). No Mozilla UA exists on this path.\r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93mInternetSetOptionA(h, 2, &160000) — the single static WININET import; option 2 = INTERNET_OPTION_CONNECT_TIMEOUT, 160 s.\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[94m3. \u001b[93m(*DAT_1400b4d88)(h, host, 0x50, 0, [user=0, pass=0, service=3, flags=0, ctx=0]) = \u001b[1mInternetConnectW, port 0x50 = 80, INTERNET_SERVICE_HTTP (3)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m.\r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b[93m (*DAT_1400b4d50)(hc, L\"POST\", uri, 0, [referrer=0, accept=0, flags=0, ctx=0]) =\u001b[1m HttpOpenRequestW, verb POST, flags 0 → no INTERNET_FLAG_SECURE →\r\nplain HTTP\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (consistent wi\u001b[Ch port 80).\u001b[39m                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[94m5. \u001b[93m(*DAT\u001b[C1400b4d38)(hr, L\"Content-Type: application/json\\r\\n\", 0x20, body, bodyL\u001b[Cn) = \u001b[1mHttpSendRequestW\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m with JSON content type.\u001b[39m                  \r\n\u001b[94m6.\u001b[93m Read\u001b[Cloop\u001b[C(*DAT_140\u001b[Cb4d68)(hr, buf, 0x1000,\u001b[C&n) =\u001b[1m InternetReadFile\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m; close via\u001b[1m InternetCloseHandle\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (DAT_1400b4d48); then base64_decod\u001b[C_st\u001b[C(out,\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[93mresponse).\u001b[39m             \r\n                                                   \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mAPI identities are proven, not inferred:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m r\u001b[Csolve_api_ptrs_from_dec\u001b[Cypted_stri\u001b[Cgs @ 0x14003c2ac contains literal plain\u001b[Cext: DAT_14\u001b[C0b4c90 =\u001b[39m           \r\n\u001b[93mLoadLibrary(\"wininet.dll\"), then DAT_1400b4d88=GetProcAddress(...,\"InternetConnectW\"), d48=\"InternetCloseHandle\", d38=\"HttpSendRequestW\",\r\nd68=\"InternetR\u001b[CadFile\", d70=\"InternetOpenW\", d\u001b[2C=\"InternetOpenUrlA\", d50=\"HttpOpenRequestW\" — these wininet names are\u001b[1m plaintext .rdata literals\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m,\r\nunlike the rest of the string table.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mCorrection to the question premise:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m although WinHttp* names ARE in the RC4 string table (Wi\u001b[CH\u001b[CtpOpen/Connect/SendReque\u001b[Ct... per\u001b[C#strtable-global-map)\r\nand winhttp.\u001b[Cll is\u001b[Cload\u001b[Cd, \u001b[Che\u001b[1m C2 path uses WinINet\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, not WinHttp. (The WinHttp po\u001b[Cnter set resolv\u001b[Cd from DAT_1400b4c98 is a separate, secondary set.)\u001b[26;1H\u001b[1mSecond network function:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m FUN_14000b1e0\u001b[1m @ 0x14000b1e0 — loader file downloader\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: InternetOpenW(same empty UA) → (*DAT_1400b4d78)=InternetOpenUrlA(h,\r\nurl, 0, 0, flags=0x800000\u001b[C0) → CreateFileW(pat\u001b[C, GENERIC_WRITE=0x40000000, CREATE_ALWAYS=2, FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL=0x80) → InternetReadFile/WriteFile\r\n0x1000-byte loop. Takes (url, local path), returns bool.\u001b[39m                                                         \u001b[30;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mTransport summary: HTTP (cleartext), port 80, verb POST to \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mhttp://45.93.20.28/3d15e67552d448ff.php\u001b[1m, empty User-Agent, \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mContent-Type: application/json\u001b[1m.\u001b[32;92H\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠹ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngin\u001b[Cer(Elara\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
