[0.020, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mExpiry string recovery\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — build_expiry_date_string @ 0x14002a4c0 concatenates into a std::stringstream: DAT_1400b09f0 + '/' + DAT_1400b0e90 + '/' +\r\nDAT_1400b1ab0 + DAT_1400b1e10, where the four globals\u001b[Care decrypted in\u001b[Cinit_rc4_key_and_strings from blobs @ .rdata 0x14007d6\u001b[Cc/6f4/6fc/704 (r\u001b[Cw\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[93mbytes 2b686f3d / 2b78383\u001b[C / 2b52733d / 2b52343d = +ho=,+x8=,+Rs=,+R4=):\u001b[39m                                                                              \u001b[8;1H\u001b[93m- +ho= → \u001b[1m\"11\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, +x8= → \u001b[1m\"04\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, +Rs= → \u001b[1m\"20\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, +R4= → \u001b[1m\"25\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (base64→RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\"), each verified individually\u001b[C\u001b[39m                                       \r\n\u001b[93m- separator char read from 0x1400814a4 = 2f = \u001b[1m'/'\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (streamed by FUN_14\u001b[2C3\u001b[C6b0) → assembled string \u001b[1m\"11/04/2025\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m.\u001b[39m                                      \r\n                                      "]
[0.000, "o", "                  \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mField order verified by the parser itself\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: parse_expiry_date_dd_mm_yyyy @ 0x14002a298 feeds an istringstream + std::time_get (FUN_140030484) with the\r\nformat literal \"%d/%m/%Y\" (visible in the decompile) → day=11, month=04, year=202\u001b[C →\u001b[1m 2025-04-11\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, i.e. 9 days after the 2025-04-02 build timestamp\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93m(#file-identity) — a classic short-lived Stealc build expiry. (Two independent routes: per-blob decrypts + the format string; not a single-read\r\ninterpretation.) If the date string fails to parse (iostate & 6), it calls\u001b[1m ExitProcess(0)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (same DAT_1400b4e08 pointer).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mComparison logic\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (date_killswitch_is_expired):\u001b[39m                                                   \u001b[18;1H\u001b[93m```c\u001b[39m                                                     \r\n\u001b[38;5;251mnow  = \u001b[38;5;109m_Xtime_get_ticks\u001b[38;5;251m() / \u001b[38;5;173m10\u001b[38;5;251m,\u001b[38;5;173m000\u001b[38;5;251m,\u001b[38;5;173m000\u001b[38;5;251m      \u001b[38;5;243m// seconds; gmtime_s -> tm (fail -> ExitProcess(0))\r\n\u001b[38;5;251mexp  = \u001b[38;5;109mparse_expiry_date_dd_mm_yyyy\u001b[38;5;251m(\"\u001b[38;5;144m11/04/2025\u001b[38;5;251m\")\u001b[39m             \r\n\u001b[38;5;139mreturn\u001b[38;5;251m \u001b[38;5;109mmktime\u001b[38;5;251m(exp_tm) < \u001b[38;5;109mmktime\u001b[38;5;251m(now_tm);     \u001b[38;5;243m// true = expired\r\n\u001b[93m```\u001b[39m                                                           \u001b[24;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mAction in wWinMain:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m ok = date_killswitch_is_expired(...); if (!ok) stealer_main_payload(); — i.e.\u001b[1m when the current date is past 11/04/2025 the entire\r\nstealer payload (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mstealer_main_payload\u001b[1m @ 0x140029f68: string re-init, API re-resolve, browser/ABE collection via chromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key,\r\nC2) is skipped and the process exits cleanly\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (CloseHandle on the guard event, destructors, return 0). No self-delete on this path; it just does\r\nnothing.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                         \r\n             \r\n\u001b[93mNote: this corrects the reading in !75 that called 0x14002a774 the \"C2 dispatch\" and 0x140029f68 the \"failure path\" — it is exactly inverted:\r\n0x14002a774 is the date gate, 0x140029f68 is the real payload entry (its callees include chromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key @ 0x14001f100).\u001b[32;87H\u001b[39m     \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mR\u001b[CverseEngineer(Sinope)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
