[0.016, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mField order ve\u001b[Cified by the parser itself\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: pa\u001b[Cse_expiry_date_dd_mm_yyyy @ 0x14002a298 feeds a\u001b[C istringstream + std::time_get\u001b[C(FUN_14\u001b[C030484)\u001b[Cwith the\r\nformat literal \"%d/%m/%Y\" (visibl\u001b[C in the decompile) → day=11, month=04, yea\u001b[C=2025 →\u001b[1m 2025-04-11\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, i.e. 9 days\u001b[Cafter the 2\u001b[C25-04-02 build timest\u001b[Cmp\r\n(#file-identity)\u001b[C— a classic short-lived Stealc\u001b[Cbuild expiry. (Two independent routes: per-blob decrypts + the format string; not a single-read\r\ninterpretation.) If the date string fails to parse (iostate & 6), it calls\u001b[1m ExitProcess(0)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (same DAT_1400b4e08 pointer).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mComparison logic\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m(d\u001b[Cte_killswitch_is_expired):\u001b[39m                                                                \u001b[11;1H\u001b[93m```c\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[38;5;251mnow  = \u001b[38;5;109m_Xtime_get_ticks\u001b[38;5;251m() / \u001b[38;5;173m10\u001b[38;5;251m,\u001b[38;5;173m000\u001b[38;5;251m,\u001b[38;5;173m000\u001b[38;5;251m      \u001b[38;5;243m// seconds; gmtime_s -> tm (fail -> ExitProcess(0))\u001b[39m                                                  \r\n\u001b[38;5;251mexp  = \u001b[38;5;109mparse_expiry_date_dd_mm_yyyy\u001b[38;5;251m(\"\u001b[38;5;144m11/04/2025\u001b[38;5;251m\")\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[38;5;139mreturn\u001b[38;5;251m \u001b[38;5;109mmktime\u001b[38;5;251m(exp_tm) < \u001b[38;5;109mmktime\u001b[38;5;251m(now_tm);     \u001b[38;5;243m// true = expired\u001b[39m                                                          \r\n\u001b[93m```\r\n\u001b[39m                                              \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mAction in wWinMain:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m ok = date_killswitch_is_expired(...); if (!ok) stealer_main_payload(); — i.e.\u001b[1m when the current date is past 11/04/2025 the entire\r\nstealer payload (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mstealer_main_payload\u001b[1m @ 0x140029f68: string re-init, API re-resolve, browser/ABE collection via chromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key,\r\nC2) is skipped and the process exits cleanly\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (CloseHandle on the guard event, destructors, return 0). No self-delete on this path; it just does\r\nnothing.\u001b[39m                                         \r\n                                                             \r\n\u001b[93mNote: this corrects the reading in !75 that called 0x14002a774 the \"C2 dispatch\" and 0x140029f68 the \"failure path\" — it is exactly inverted:\r\n0x14002a774 is the date gate, 0x140029f68 is the real payload entry (its callees include chromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key @ 0x14001f100).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-bulk-\u001b[2Crings\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Adrastea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mTool\u001b[Cng note for fu\u001b[Cure \u001b[Cuns:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the session script bulk_\u001b[Cecrypt_b64_rc4 is finalized and gene\u001b[Cic — all inputs via args\u001b[C{base, size, key, min_len,\r\nkeywords[]}; it scans any VA range for NUL-bounded base64 tokens, decodes base64→RC4(key) natively, prints the full categorized list plus a\r\nconfigurable keyword sweep. It was validated here (277/277 plaintexts, zero decode errors, cross-checked against !73 and the raw-file route).\r\n\u001b[1mPromotion to the persistent library was attempted but did not execut\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m\u001b[1me (context limit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — a future\u001b[Csession should promote_script i\u001b[C as-is\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[93m(technique-named, honest docs\u001b[Calready drafted in\u001b[Cthis\u001b[Cthread's method comments).\u001b[39m                                                           \u001b[32;92H    \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠧ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mDeveloper(Adrastea\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
