[0.048, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mNo RC4 on traffic:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m callers(FUN_140023048) (the only RC4 implementation, the one keyed with \"CgeOvEO7h\u001b[C\") \u001b[Ceturns exactly ONE caller:\u001b[39m         \r\n\u001b[93mdecrypt_string_b64_rc4 @ 0x140007d04 — the string-table decryp\u001b[Cer.\u001b[CNo network function reaches it\u001b[C So this build's C2 bodies are\r\n\u001b[1mbase64(JSON-plaintext)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, refining the family expectation of \"RC4+base64\" (!58/!68): the RC4 key protects only the embedded string table.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mJSON field names\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (all resolved via #strtable-global-map; globals observed as json[key] in the senders):\u001b[10;1H- Beacon/config request (FUN_140026\u001b[C14): type (0x1400b0c90) = \"create\" (0x1400b09d0),\u001b[Chwid\u001b[C(0x1400b1010\u001b[C, build (0\u001b[C1400b0830).\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[93m- Tasking \u001b[Ce\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
