mory\u001b[1m):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m every obfuscated str\u001b[Cng in th\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mis sampl\u001b[C is a\u001b[C independent ba\u001b[Ce64(RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")) blob\r\nwith the k\u001b[Cystre\u001b[Cm restar\u001b[Cing pe\u001b[C blob, so a blob beginning with a given plaintext has a deterministic b\u001b[Cse64 pr\u001b[Cfix. Ke\u001b[Cstr\u001b[Cam (ve\u001b[Cified \u001b[Cgainst the\r\nknown GetUserDefaultLangID blob): CB 2B 88 0C 09 7E C2 11 A8 BF AC 2D 90 B5 D2 2B 3D ED DD 09…\r\n- \"HAL9TH\" → cipher 83 6a c4 35 5d 36 → base64 g2rENV02. Searched g2rENV02 and even the 3-byte prefix g2rE (\"HAL…\"):\u001b[1m 0 matches\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m in the whole program\r\nimage.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m    - \"JohnDoe\"\u001b[C→ cipher 81 44 e0 62\u001b[C4d\u001b[C11 a7 → base64\u001b[CgUTgYk0Rpw==. Searched gUTgYk0Rpw:\u001b[C\u001b[1m0 matches\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m.\u001b[39m            \r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Consumer enumeration (xref-complete):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the resolved pointers are read at exactly one site each — GetComputerNameW ptr DAT_1400b4ea0 only at\r\n0x140037dc9 (get_computer_name_w_str, feeds the guard-event name and later the sysinfo report), GetUserNameW ptr DAT_1400b4b38 only at 0x140037d2d\r\n(get_user_name_w_str). Neither result is ever string-compared against a constant; wWinMain passes them straight into the event-name wostringstream.\u001b[28;1HSo the v1/Vidar-era HAL9TH/JohnDoe emulator check predicted in !63 was\u001b[1m dropped in this v2 build\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (\"not proven present\" is here backed by full xref\r\ncoverage of the only name-fetching APIs plus exhaustive ciphertext-prefix search; a mid-string occurrence inside a larger blob is the only shape\r\nthese searches cannot see — the pending #q-bulk-strings full table decrypt can double-confirm, but no plausible check consumes the names anyway).\u001b[32;92H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠙ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[C\u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Sin\u001b[3C)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling cre\u001b[Cte_comm\u001b[Cnt\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
