[0.011, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mcoverage of the only name-fetching APIs\u001b[Cplus exhaustive ciphertex\u001b[C-prefix search; a mid-string occurrence inside a larger blob is the only shape\r\nthese searches cannot see — the pending #q-bulk-strings full table decrypt can double-confirm, but no plausible check consumes the names anyway).\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                          \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Adrastea)\r\n\u001b[97mFinal handoff — task complete.\u001b(B\u001b[m                              \u001b[10;1H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## What was done\u001b(B\u001b[m                                    \u001b[12;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mBulk decrypt (#q-bulk-strings — solved):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Reused/extended the session Rhai script\u001b[93m bulk_decrypt_b64_rc4\u001b[97m to scan the entire\u001b[93m .rdata\u001b[97m section (VA\r\n0x14006f000, 107,008 bytes) for NUL-bounded base64 tokens and decrypt each with the proven native pipeline\u001b[93m base64 → RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")\u001b[97m. Result:\u001b[1m 385\r\ncandidate tokens, 277 fully-printable plaintexts, zero decode errors\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — the complete list (VA | token | plaintext) is posted verbatim in\u001b[1m !88\r\n(C2/registry/SQL/paths/apps), !99 (122 API names), !105 (templates + config/JSON fields + short tokens)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Parallel tables by other agents (!82–!106)\r\nindependently converge on the same 260-blob initializer mapping.\u001b[18;1H\u001b[1mPersistence verdict (#q-persistence — solved, !107):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m No persistence mechanism exists in this binary, proven by four sweeps with stated coverage: (1)\r\nkeyword sweep over all 277 decrypted strings → only 4 hits, all benign (\u001b[93mGdiplusStartup\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m run_as_admin\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m runas\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m \\t- Running Path:\u001b[97m ); (2) the resolved\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97mregistry API set is strictly read-only — 