[0.080, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mCorrections & leads:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m !73's \"GetCerrentProcessId (sic)\" fami\u001b[Cy-fingerprint claim is\u001b[1m disproved byte-level\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!109): the real tok\u001b[Cn is\u001b[93m jE78T3wM…\u001b[97m →\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[97mordinary\u001b[93m GetCurrentProcessId\u001b[97m; the \"typ\u001b[C\" was \u001b[C \u001b[Cranscription error — do not carry it\u001b[Cinto IOCs. New lead posted to #q-anti-\u001b[Cnalysis (!110): th\u001b[C four\r\n2-char strings\u001b[93m 11/04/20/25\u001b[97m beside the RC4 key are a probable date kill-switch (field order unverified — xref targets given).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mOutstanding:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m script promotion\u001b[2Co the \u001b[Cersistent lib\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mra\u001b[Cy d\u001b[Cd not execute\u001b[C(context l\u001b[Cmit) —\u001b[Cnoted\u001b[Con th\u001b[C forum (!114) for a future session; the script\r\nis generic and promotion-ready.\u001b[39m                                                                                             \u001b[12;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Thebe) · ▸ set_status(#q-bulk-strings) · 79633 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n                               \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-anti-analysis\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Thebe)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mLead from the full string-table decrypt (!84 under #q-bulk-strings): init_rc4_key_and_strings @ 0x140001ee0 decrypts four 2-char fragments as its\r\nvery first blobs — \"11\" → DAT_1400b09f0, \"04\" → DAT_1400b0e90, \"20\" → DAT_1400b1ab0, \"25\" → DAT_1400b1e10 — alongside GetUserDefaultLangID\r\n(DAT_1400b1630), GetLocalTime (DAT_1400b2490), GetSystemTime (DAT_1400b1510). These look like\u001b[1m date kill-switch components (11 / 04 / 2025, i.e.\r\n11-Apr-2025?)\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mper the Stealc date-expiry trait (!63). To confirm: xref the read\u001b[Crs of those four DAT slots and check\u001b[3Cr a compare \u001b[2Cai\u001b[Cst\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[93mG\u001b[CtLocalTime/GetSystemTime output followed by\u001b[Cexit/self-delete. Interpretation (dd vs mm order, how \"20\"+\"25\" comb\u001b[Cn\u001b[C) is NOT yet verified — only the\r\ndecrypted fragments and their\u001b[Cslots are.\u001b[39m                                                                                                       \r\n                                                                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Thebe) · ▸ flag_for_review(Developer(Io)) · 542 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n                                        \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Io)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m⚑ flagged for analyst review: Probable date kill-switch fragments \"11\"/\"04\"/\"20\"/\"25\" — consumers untraced\u001b[27;1H\u001b[31m\u001b[1m⚠ Developer(Thebe) context warning (flush findings to the forum): ~168059 of 200000 tokens\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Elara)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mNow the flow (task 12). Cheap checks: which globals the other two loader handlers reference, and who calls the message functions.\u001b[42;97H\u001b[90m378\u001b[C267\u001b[10C3\u001b[C238\u001b[13C791\u001b[C505\u001b[5C2\u001b[C22\u001b[C0\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
