[0.010, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mThe\u001b[93m CurrentVersion\\Uninstall\u001b[97m string is confirmed as installed-app enumeration via read-only Reg APIs, as the question anticipated. Calibration: the\r\nC2-driven loader (EXE/MSI/PowerShell download-and-execute) could deliver a second stage that persists — that is a server-side capability, not a\r\nmechani\u001b[Cm i\u001b[2Cthis binary. The positive counterpart matches the Stealc smash-a\u001b[Cd-grab\u001b[Cprofile:\u001b[93m self_delete\u001b[97m config\u001b[Cflag +\u001b[93m cmd /c timeout /t 5 & del /f\r\n/q \"<own path>\"\u001b[97m routine @\u001b[CFUN_14003b870.\u001b[39m         \u001b[9;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Carme) · ▸ read(0x14007de40) · 224 chars\u001b[11;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Sinope)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m#q-anti-analysis is solved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — all four tasks completed with byte-level \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mevidence. Summary of findings:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[94m1.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m CIS locale kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (wWinMain\u001b[C@ 0x\u001b[C4002a96d):\u001b[93m GetUserDefaultLa\u001b[CgID()\u001b[97m (decrypted API name proven) compared via subtract-chain against exactly\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m{0x419 ru-RU, 0x422 uk-UA, 0x423 be-BY, 0x43F kk-KZ, 0x443 uz-Latn-UZ}\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m →\u001b[1m ExitProcess(0)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m immediately, before\u001b[Cany\u001b[2C2 contac\u001b[C. (!108)\u001b[39m             \r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m \"Mutex\" guard is actually a named EVENT guard\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m:\u001b[93m OpenEventW(EVENT_ALL_ACCESS=0x1F0003)\u001b[97m loop — if the event exists, CloseHandle + Sleep(4106 ms) and\r\nretry (it\u001b[3m waits\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m for the previous instance, not exits), then\u001b[93m CreateEventW\u001b[97m registers its own (NULL → ExitProcess(0)). N\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mame\u001b[C=\u001b[93m L\"<%p of\u001b[39m                 \r\n\u001b[93m0x140007c78>_<ComputerName>_<Use\u001b[CName>\"\u001b[97m — the first token is the pointer to the\u001b[C\"suka\" stri\u001b[Cg-builder function formatted with\u001b[93m \"%p\"\u001b[C\u001b[97mvia\u001b[39m           \r\n\u001b[93mstd::num_put<wchar_t>::do_put(const void*)\u001b[97m (apparent developer bug: streamed the function instead of its \"suka\" result). All API identities proven\r\nfrom decrypted blobs (OpenEventW/C\u001b[CeateEventW/Sleep/CloseHandle/GetComputerNameW/GetUserNameW). (!111)\u001b[39m                                            \r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Date kill switch confirmed\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: hardcod\u001b[Cd expiry\u001b[1m \"11/04/2025\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m assembled from four\u001b[CRC4 blobs (\"11\"+\"/\"+\"04\"+\"/\"+\"20\"+\"25\"), parsed\u001b[Cwith the literal\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93m\"%d/%m/%Y\"\u001b[97m →\u001b[1m 11 April 2025\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (9 days after build).\u001b[93m date_killswitch_is_expired\u001b[97m @\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m 0x14002a774 compares via mktime; when expired, the whole stealer\r\npayload (0x140029f68) is skipped and the process exits cleanly. This corrects !75's inverted reading\u001b[Cof the dispatch. (!113)\u001b[39m                       \r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m No HAL9TH/JohnDoe check\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (ciphertext-prefix searches 0 matches; GetComputerNameW/GetUserNameW consumed only by the event-name/report builders),\u001b[1m no\r\nanti-VM\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (VMware/VBox/VirtualBox/Sbie/QEMU encrypted-prefix + plaintext sweeps\u001b[Call\u001b[Cn\u001b[Cgative), and\u001b[1m no anti-debug beyond CRT\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: FUN_14003fcbc is the\u001b[Cstock\u001b[26;2HRT\u001b[93m __raise_securityfailure\u001b[97m/fastfai\u001b[2Creporter (det\u001b[Cctor flag refut\u001b[Cd under\u001b[C#fn-14003fcbc), and both other IsDebuggerPr\u001b[Csent sites are FID-ma\u001b[Cched\r\n\u001b[93m__acrt_*\u001b[97m l\u001b[Cbrary code. (!117,\u001b[C!119)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                 \r\n                                        \r\n\u001b[97mRenames/comments persisted in the Ghidra project; a review flag records the \"%p-of-suka\" interpretation and the residual mid-blob caveat pending\r\n#q-bulk-strings.\u001b[39m                                          \u001b[34;2H"]
