[0.011, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-ransomware\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Carme)\r\n\u001b[93mDetector-site triage: every T1486 anchor site is a false positive (code-level evidence).\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                      \r\n\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m FindNextFile @ 0x14005c1f7 sits inside FUN_14005c018 (renamed crt_expand_argv_wildcards). Decompile shows it is the\u001b[1m MSVC CRT argv\r\nwildcard-expansion routine\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: scans the command line for */? via wcspbrk(_Str, L\"*?\"), calls FindFirstFileExW/FindNextFileW only to expand command-line\r\nglobs, and hands the result to __acrt_allocate_buffer_for_argv (a named CRT symbol in the same function). It has\u001b[1m zero callers in malware code\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m(invoked only from CRT startup). It never opens, reads, or writes file contents.\r\n\u001b[94m2\u001b[3C\u001b[93mUN_140001e10 (#fn-140001e10) is a 3-line C++ bad_array_\u001b[Cew_leng\u001b[Ch\u001b[1m exception-object constructor\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (param_1[1] = \"bad array n\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mew length\"; *param_1 =\r\n&PTR_FUN_140073218;). The three T1486\u001b[C\"recovered strings\" there (!5–!7) are XOR replays of\u001b[Cthe junk key \"address in use\" (a CRT winsock error text\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93mfragment) over other\u001b[CCRT error\u001b[Ctext — the \"plaintexts\" (efwasmk!\u001b[C{, t{s\"emd<rz7, eo\u001b[Clqx<Ll+hy\u001b[Cad`) are\u001b[1m gibberish, not\u001b[Cl\u001b[Cnguage\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: they are false\r\ndecodes,\u001b[Cnot rec\u001b[Cvered\u001b[Ckeys or payloads.\u001b[39m                                        \r\n\u001b[94m3\u001b[11C\u001b[93m2b6c\u001b[11C2b6c\u001b[5Cthe pre-main\u001b[1m string-table initializer\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (proven in !60); its 18 \"candidate symmetric keys\" (!8–!25) are\u001b[1m ciphertext\r\nblobs\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m of the base64+RC4(\"CgeOvEO7hu\")\u001b[Cstring table, already individually d\u001b[Ccrypted to API nam\u001b[Cs/paths in !61/!73.\u001b[39m                                 \r\n                                                                                               "]
