[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mIndependent verification:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m for FindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA I first\u001b[3m predicted\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the ciphert\u001b[Cxt from the RC4 keystream (derived from two known\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93mplaint\u001b[Cxt/ciphe\u001b[Ctext pairs: GdipDisposeImage, RegQueryValueExA; keystream cb 2b 88 0c 09 7e c2 11 a8 bf ac 2d 90 b5 d2 2b…), then found the predicted\r\nbase64 tokens byte-\u001b[Cor-byte at 0x14007deb0/0x14007dec8 — two routes, same answer.\u001b[39m                                                                  \r\n                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mGrabber executor\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m FUN_1400082d8\u001b[1m → renamed\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m grabber_\u001b[Cnum_match_collect_files (recursive; literals \"%s\\\\*\", \".\", \"..\", \"%s\\\\%s\", \",\", \"%s%s\"\u001b[C@\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93m0x14007f4c0–0x14007f4e0):\u001b[39m               \r\n                                          "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[94m1. \u001b[93mwsprin\u001b[CfA(\u001b[Cuf, \"%s\\\\*\u001b[C, dir) → FindFi\u001b[CstFileA / FindNextF\u001b[CleA / FindClose loop;\u001b[Cskips ./.. via StrCmpCA.\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93mTokenizes the rule's mask list on \",\" and tests each filename with PathMatchSpecA.\r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[C\u001b[93mOn match: CopyFileA(fullpath, <stag\u001b[Cng\u001b[Cprefix DAT_1400b1170>+random, failIfExists=1) — stages a copy; optional\u001b[2Cize cap via CreateF\u001b[CleW(name,\r\nGENERIC_READ, share=3) + GetFileSizeEx (sum in KB vs rule's max_size).\r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b[93m read_whole_file_to_buffer (FUN_14001a834): GetFileSizeEx → LocalAlloc(LMEM_ZEROINIT) →\u001b[1m ReadFile\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m → CloseHandle.\u001b[1m The only data operation performed\r\non a victim file is a read.\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                 "]
[0.001, "o", "                                                     \r\n\u001b[94m5.\u001b[93m FUN_140009814 appends (report-relative-path, buffer, size) into the\u001b[1m in-memory collection vector at ctx+0x20\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — the exfil payload (matches the C2\r\nschema upload_file/filename/data and server-driven rule schema csidl/start_path/masks/recursive/max_size in !85/!86).\r\n\u001b[94m6. \u001b[93mDeleteFileA on its \u001b[1mown staging copy\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m only; recurses into subdirectories (attr & 0x10) with a depth cap.\u001b[26;1H\u001b[1mCall chain:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m wWinMain → stealer_main_payload (FUN_140029f68) → run_grabber_rules (FUN_140008b30) → grabber_enum_match_collect_files; the one hardcoded\r\nrule is built by build_steam_grabber_rule\u001b[1m (FUN_140037704)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m: reads the Steam install path from HKCU (RegOpenKeyExA/RegQueryValueExA via\r\nDAT_1400b4e50/4e48), attaches mask list ssfn*,config.vdf,DialogConfig.vdf,… (global 0x1400b1a50 ← blob 0x14007f230) and label\u001b[1m \"Steam\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (global\r\n0x1400b21d0 ← blob 0\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mx14007f2b0 mF/tbWQ=, decode re-verified). All other rules come from the C2 config — Steam credential theft + server-configured\r\ngrab, exfiltrated in memory.\u001b[1m Nothing in this path writes, renames, or encrypts a user file.\u001b[32;93H\u001b[36m⠙ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[C\u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Carm\u001b[C)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling cre\u001b[Cte_comm\u001b[Cnt\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
