[0.000, "o", "\u001b[C\u001b[93m(!85, with stated coverage).\u001b[39m                                               \r\n     \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mVerdict: ransomware (T1486) REFUTED — this is the Stealc v2 infostealer.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m The file enumeration feeds (a) the server-configured file grabber and\u001b[Cthe\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mhardcoded Steam-credential\u001b[Crule (r\u001b[Cad → in-memory collection → RC4+base64 JSON exfil to 45.93.20.28/3d15e67552d448ff.php) and (b) browser-profile\r\nharve\u001b[Cting via temporary staging copies; the detect\u001b[2C's T1486 anchors are CRT code and string-obfusc\u001b[Ction ciphertext (!125). Calibration: this\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[93mexcludes embedded encryption\u001b[Ccapability (no write-back loop, no\u001b[Crename, no\u001b[Cshadow-copy\u001b[Cdel\u001b[Ction, no ransom strings — each exclusion cited above);\r\nwhat it does\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m exclude is the C2-tasked loader (download_url_to_file + IEX cradle + msiexec) delivering an arbitrary follow-on payload — downl\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
