[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m,\r\n\u001b[93m__acrt_allocate_buffer_for_argv\u001b[97m) — CRT startup code, no\u001b[Cmalware logic.\u001b[39m                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mFUN_140001e10\u001b[97m is a C++ \u001b[93mbad_array_new_length\u001b[97m exception ctor; its three T1486 \"recovered strings\" are gibberish XOR false decodes.\r\n- \u001b[93mFUN_140002b6c\u001b[97m's 18 \"candidate keys\" are RC4 string-table \u001b[1mciphertext\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, already decrypted to API names/paths.\u001b[18;1H\u001b[1mWhat the file enumeration feeds (!126, supports):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Full code trace of the grabber\u001b[93m grabber_enum_match_collect_files\u001b[97m @ 0x1400082d8 with every\r\nruntime-resolved API identity proven by blob decryption\r\n(FindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA/FindClose/PathMatchSpecA/StrCmpCA/CopyFileA/CreateFileW/GetFileSizeEx/ReadFile/LocalAlloc/DeleteFileA).\r\nFindFirstFileA/FindNextF\u001b[CleA ciphertexts\u001b[Cwer\u001b[C\u001b[1m independently \u001b(B\u001b[m"]
