[0.093, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mThe task is complete. \u001b[1m#q-ransomware is solved with the conclusion: ransomware (T1486) refuted — this is the Stealc v2 infostealer.\u001b[6;1H\u001b[36m##\u001b[CSummary of evidence posted\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mDetector-site triage (!125, disproves #fn-140001e10 premise, echoed as !128):\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                             \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[93m FindNextFile @ 0x14005c1f7\u001b[97m is inside the\u001b[1m MSVC CRT argv wildcard-expansion routine\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93mcrt_expand_argv_wildcards\u001b[97m @ 0x14005c018;\u001b[93m wcspbrk(L\"*?\")\u001b[97m,\r\n\u001b[93m__acrt_allocate_buffer_for_argv\u001b[97m) — CRT startup code, no malware logic.\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mFUN_140001e10\u001b[97m is a C++ \u001b[93mbad_array_new_length\u001b[97m exception ctor; its three T1486 \"recovered strings\" are gibberish XOR false decodes.\u001b[13;2H \u001b[C\u001b[93mUN_140002b6c\u001b[97m's 18 \"candidate\u001b[Ckeys\" are RC4 string-table \u001b[1mciphert\u001b[2Ct\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m, already decrypted to API names/paths.\u001b[39m                                 \r\n                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mWhat the file enumeration feeds (!126, supports):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Full code trace\u001b[Cof the grabbe\u001b[C\u001b[93m grabber_enum_match_collect_files\u001b[97m @\u001b[C0x1400082d8 with every\r\nruntime-resolved API\u001b[Cide\u001b[Ct\u001b[Cty proven by blob dec\u001b[Cyption\u001b[39m                                                     \r\n\u001b[97m(FindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA/FindClose/PathMatchSpecA/StrCmpCA/CopyFileA/CreateFileW/GetFileSizeEx/ReadFile/LocalAlloc/DeleteFileA).\r\nFindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA ciphertexts were\u001b[1m independently predicted from the RC4 keystream and matched byte-for-byte\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m at \u001b[Cx14007deb0/0x14007dec8\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m.\r\nFlow: \u001b[Cnumerat\u001b[C → \u001b[CathMatchSpecA mask match → stage c\u001b[Cpy →\u001b[1m ReadFile into memory\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m → append to exfil collection → delete own staging copy. Hardcoded\r\nrule = Steam creds (\u001b[93mbuild_steam_grabber_rule\u001b[97m @ 0x140037704, masks\u001b[93m ssfn*,config.vdf,…\u001b[97m, label \"\u001b[Cteam\"); other rules are server-push\u001b[Cd\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[97m(\u001b[93mcsidl/start_path/masks/recursive/max_size\u001b[97m).\u001b[39m                                                                                                      \r\n                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mNo encryption loop (!127, supports): WriteFile has exactly one consumer binary-wide\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m —\u001b[93m download_url_to_file\u001b[97m (loader path), zero ov\u001b[Crlap with any of\r\nthe six FindFirstFileA consumers; Copy\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97mFileA/DeleteFileA usage is exclusively the staging-copy pattern (verified by full decompile of\r\n\u001b[93mbrowser_profiles_enum_and_harvest\u001b[97m); no MoveFile*/CryptEncrypt anywhere; zero ransom/vssadmin/shadow/bcdedit/bitcoin/\".locked\" strings in the full\r\n276-entry decrypted table and the whole raw file (developer sweep !85, coverage stated). Calibration noted: the C2\u001b[Cloader\u001b[Ccould d\u001b[Cliver arbitrary\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mfollow-on payloads — download\u001b[2C capabil\u001b[Cty, not ransomware capability in this binary.\u001b[39m                                               \r\n                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[97m1572 functions. R\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
