[0.028, "o", "\u001b[4;1H       \r\n\u001b[93m- The 276-string decrypted table contains\u001b[1m zero wallet or extension names\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (whole-file grep coverage in #q-bulk-strings). Targeting arrives in the C2\r\nJSON config under keys wallets 0x1400b21f0 (blob 0x14007e458), browsers 0x1400b1730, plugins, files — parsed into three list containers at\r\nsession-struct +0x48/+0x60/+0x78 (!123). This matches Stealc v2's server-side target-list design (!59): desktop wallets are grabbed via\r\nserver-s\u001b[Cpplied file-grabber rules.\u001b[39m                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[93m- Browser-extension theft plumbing is hardcoded: prefix chrome_e\u001b[Ctension_ 0x140\u001b[Cb04\u001b[C0 (blob 0x14007e67\u001b[C) consumed by\u001b[39m                            \r\n\u001b[93mbrowser_profiles_enum_and_harv\u001b[2Ct @ 0x14001d7a0 (xrefs 0x14001dfe3/0x14001dff4, plus\u001b[CFUN_14001ebe4\u001b[C@ 0x14001ed07); IndexedDB 0x1400b0710 and\u001b(B\u001b[m   \r\n\u001b[93mfrom_Index\u001b[CdDB 0x14\u001b[C0b1d1\u001b[C slots show extension LevelDB/IndexedDB stores (where w\u001b[2Clet ex\u001b[2Cnsions keep vaults) are collected.\u001b[39m                       \r\n                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mSteam — hardcoded built-in module:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m steam_steal_ssfn_vdf_module\u001b[1m @ 0x140037704\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, gated on config flag steal_steam (0x1400b2350,\u001b[Cb\u001b[2Cb 0x14007eca0) =\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mlocal_65 in\u001b[Cstealer_main_payload (call site in the orche\u001b[Ctrator\u001b[Ctail).\u001b[CDecompiled flow:\u001b[39m              \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[94m1. \u001b[93mRegOpenKeyExA(HKEY_CURRENT_USER\u001b[C/*0x80000001 sign-\u001b[Cxt*/, DAT_1400b0b10 =\u001b[C\"Software\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m\\Valve\\St\u001b[Cam\",\u001b[C0, 0x20119 /*KEY_READ*/) via\u001b[Cptr DAT_1400b4e50\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93mR\u001b[CgQ\u001b[CeryValueExA(h,\u001b[CDAT_1400b1690\u001b[C= \"SteamPath\", ...) via DAT_1400b4e48, R\u001b[CgCloseK\u001b[Cy via\u001b[CDAT_1400b4\u001b[C40\u001b[39m                                      \r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m App\u001b[Cn\u001b[Cs DAT_1400b03f0 = \\config\\, build\u001b[C a grab rule with\u001b[1m mask list DAT_1400b1a50 =\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                     \r\n\u001b[93mssfn*,config.vdf,DialogConfig.vdf,DialogConfigOverlay*.vdf,libraryfolders.vdf,loginusers.vdf (recursive=1, depth fields set)\r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b[93m Hands the rule to the generic grabber: FUN_140009040 → FUN_140008b30 — same plumbing as server-supplied grabber rules (proves the grabber executor\r\nidentity too).\u001b[23;1H\u001b[1mOutlook:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m con\u001b[Cig flag steal_outlook 0x14\u001b[C0b14b0 (blo\u001b[C 0x14007ecb8) is p\u001b[Crsed by the config parser FUN_140025b64 @ 0x140025db1 \u001b[Cnto the session flags\r\n(+0x40..0x44 range). Its runtim\u001b[C \u001b[Consumer was\u001b[1m not pinpointed\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m; notably there is\u001b[1m no Outlook registry path\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (Software\\Microsoft\\Office\\...\\Profiles)\r\namong the 276 decrypted strings — \u001b[Clagged for analyst\u001b[Creview as either server-config-driven o\u001b[C a vestigial/incomplete module.\u001b[39m         \r\n                                                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mTelegram / Discord / FTP clients / VPN clients: no built-in modules or name strings exist\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (coverage:\u001b[Cfull 276-string table + who\u001b[Ce-file\u001b[39m         \r\n\u001b[93mASCII/UTF-16LE grep, #q-bulk-strings dev scans).\u001b[CThese apps can only be reached via server-supplied grabber rules (paths/masks from C2). Calibration:\r\n\"no hardcoded targeting demonstrated\", not \"cannot steal them\" — a C2-issued rule for e.g. %\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mAPPDATA%\\Telegram Desktop\\tdata would be executed by the\r\ngeneric grabber.\u001b[39m                                                                                   \u001b[34;2H"]
