[0.013, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                              \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mMechanism identified.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m The instructions are \u001b[3mimage-base-relative\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93m140047148: movzx eax, word ptr [rcx + rdi*4 + 0x75010]\u001b[97m (rcx = 0x140000000)\r\n- \u001b[93m140047150: lea rdx, [rcx + 0x74700]\u001b[39m               \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93m1400468d1: mov eax, [r12 + rax*4 + 0x750a8]\r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93m14006134d: mov eax, [rdx + rax*4 + 0x750a8]\r\n\u001b[39m                                                               \r\n\u001b[97mThe disp32 is the\u001b[1m RVA\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x75010/0x750a8/0x74700), with a register holding\u001b[93m __ImageBase\u001b[97m — invisible to a RIP-relative scan. New scan: find disp32/imm32\r\nfields whose value equals an RVA inside the two ranges (RVA A: 0x7\u001b[Ce\u001b[2C–\u001b[Cx7280\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m0, RVA B: 0x74f00–0x750d0), validated by a mod=10 ModRM/SIB:\r\n\u001b[39m                                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ create_script(scan_rva_disp) · 69 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 1619 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97mAll first-half hits are \"loose\" (mostly RIP-relative instructions pointing\u001b[3m elsewhere\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — e.g.\u001b[93m lea rdx,[rip+0x72496]\u001b[97m lands in .rdata far above our\r\nranges — not image-base-relative refs). Second half:\u001b[39m             \u001b[24;55H\u001b[90m5363\u001b[27;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mRange B fully enumerated\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: 25 validated image-base-r\u001b[Clative instructio\u001b[C references (\u001b[93m[reg + idx*4\u001b[C+ RVA]\u001b[97m, reg=0x140000000), all inside the two UCRT\r\nfloat-convers\u001b[Con functions.\u001b[1m Range A: zero\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m validated hits under this idiom too (its \"loose\" matches are RIP-relative instructions pointing into\r\n.data). One residual possibility for A: a nearby\u001b[93m lea\u001b[97m base (0x1400700a0/0x140070590/0x140070c48/0x140070c58) plus a large constant offset. Checking\r\nthose consumers and the data:\u001b[39m                                   "]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[34;2H"]
[0.013, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m- \u001b[93m140047148: movzx eax, word ptr [rcx + rdi*4 + 0x75010]\u001b[97m (rcx = 0x140000000)\r\n- \u001b[93m140047150: lea rdx, [rcx + 0x74700]\r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93m1400468d1: mov eax, [r12 + rax*4 + 0x750a8]\u001b[39m                  \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93m14006134d: mov eax, [rdx + rax*4 + 0x750a8]\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                            \r\n\u001b[97mThe disp32 is the\u001b[1m RVA\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x75010/0x750a8/0x74700), with a register holding\u001b[93m __ImageBase\u001b[97m — invisible to a RIP-relative scan. New scan: find disp32/imm32\r\nfields whose value equals an RVA inside the two ranges (RVA A: 0x71e00–0x72800, RVA B: 0x74f00–0x750d0), validated by a mod=10 ModRM/SIB:\r\n\u001b[39m                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ create_script(scan_rva_disp) · 69 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 1619 chars\u001b[39m                                                                         \u001b[16;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                           \r\n\u001b[97mAll first-half hits are \"loose\" (mostly RIP-relative instructions pointing\u001b[3m elsewhere\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — e.g.\u001b[93m lea rdx,[rip+0x72496]\u001b[97m lands in .rdata far above our\r\nranges — not image-base-relative refs). Second half:\u001b[39m            \u001b[20;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 5363 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(T\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36m\u001b[1mhemisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                              \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mRange B fully enumerated\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: 25 validated image-base-relative instruction references (\u001b[93m[reg + idx*4 + RVA]\u001b[97m, reg=0x140000000), all inside the two UCRT\r\nfloat-conversion functions.\u001b[1m Range A: zero\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m validated hits under this idiom too (its \"loose\" matches are RIP-relative instructions pointing into\r\n.data). One residual possibility for A: a nearby\u001b[93m lea\u001b[97m base (0x1400700a0/0x140070590/0x140070c48/0x140070c58) plus a large constant offset. Checking\r\nthose consumers and the data:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ get_function(0x14003dfdb) · 260 chars\u001b[39m                                                                               \r\n                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ read(140070c58) · …running\u001b[32;100H\u001b[39m      \u001b[36m\u001b[1m"]
