[0.067, "o", "\u001b[32;106H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠦\u001b[42;98H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m689\u001b[C745\u001b[10C4\u001b[C917\u001b[13C21\u001b[2C662\u001b[6C8\u001b[C4\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.009, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mThe disp32 is the\u001b[1m RVA\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x75010/0x750a8/0x74700), with a register holding\u001b[93m __ImageBase\u001b[97m — invisible to a RIP-relative scan. New scan: find disp32/imm32\r\nfields whose value equals an RVA inside the two ranges (RVA A: 0x71e00–0x72800, RVA B: 0x74f00–0x750d0), validated by a mod=10 ModRM/SIB:\r\n\u001b[39m                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ create_script(scan_rva_disp) · 69 chars\u001b[9;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 1619 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mAll first-half hits are \"loose\" (mostly RIP-relative instructions poi\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mnting\u001b[3m elsewhere\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — e.g.\u001b[93m lea rdx,[rip+0x72496]\u001b[97m lands in .rdata far above our\r\nranges — not image-base-relative refs). Second half:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                              \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 5363 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mRange B fully enumerated\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: 25 validated image-base-relative instruction references (\u001b[93m[reg + idx*4 + RVA]\u001b[97m, reg=0x140000000), all inside the two UCRT\r\nfloat-conversion functions.\u001b[1m Range A: zero\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m validated hits under this idiom too (its \"loose\" matches are RIP-relative instructions pointing into\r\n.data). One residual possibility for A: a nearby\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m lea\u001b[97m base (0x1400700a0/0x140070590/0x140070c48/0x140070c58) plus a large constant offset. Checking\r\nthose consumers and the data:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ get_function(0x14003dfdb) · 260 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                  \r\n                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ read(140070c58) · 96 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\n                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m0x140070c58 is the C++ string\u001b[93m \"invalid random_device value\"\u001b[97m (so FUN_14003dfd8 is a\u001b[93m std::random_device\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m error-string selector — not a table consumer).\r\nBut immediately after it (0x140070c80) a ramp table\u001b[93m 00 01 02 03…\u001b[97m begins — the shuffle-mask blob may\u001b[3m start\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m there. One more sweep: image-base-relative\r\ndisp32 with RVA 0x6fe00–0x71e00 (validated forms only):\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.013, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ create_script(scan_rva_disp) · 69 chars\u001b[39m                                                                        \u001b[7;27H\u001b[90mrun_script(scan_rva_disp) · 1619 chars\u001b[39m \u001b[9;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                          \r\n\u001b[97mAll first-half hits are \"loose\" (mostly RIP-relative instructions pointing\u001b[3m elsewhere\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — e.g.\u001b[93m lea rdx,[rip+0x72496]\u001b[97m lands in .rdata far above our\r\nranges — not image-base-relative refs). Second half:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_s\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mcript(scan_rva_disp) · 5363 chars\u001b[15;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                          \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mRange B fully enumerated\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: 25 validated image-base-relative instruction references (\u001b[93m[reg + idx*4 + RVA]\u001b[97m, reg=0x140000000), all inside the two UCRT\r\nfloat-conversion functions.\u001b[1m Range A: zero\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m validated hits under this idiom too (its \"loose\" matches are RIP-relative instructions pointing into\r\n.data). One residual possibility for A: a n\u001b[Carby\u001b[93m lea\u001b[97m base (0x1400700a0/0x140070590/0x140070c48/0x140070c58) plus a large consta\u001b[Ct offset. Checking\r\nth\u001b[Cse \u001b[3Csumers and the data:\u001b[39m                                                                                                                 \r\n                               