[0.096, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mranges — not image-base-relative refs). Second half:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 5363 chars\u001b[39m                                                                               \r\n                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\r\n\u001b[97mRange B fully enumerated\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: 25 validated image-base-relative instruction references (\u001b[93m[reg + idx*4 + RVA]\u001b[97m, reg=0x140000000), all inside the two UCRT\r\nfloat-conversion functions.\u001b[1m Range A: zero\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m validated hits under this idiom too (its \"loose\" matches are RIP-relative instructions pointing into\r\n.data). One residual possibility for A: a nearby\u001b[93m lea\u001b[97m base (0x1400700a0/0x140070590/0x140070c48/0x140070c58) plus a large constant offset. Checking\r\nthose consumers and the data:\u001b[39m                                                                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ get_function(0x14003dfdb) · 260 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                   \r\n                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ read(140070c58) · 96 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m0x140070c58 is the C++ string\u001b[93m \"invalid random_device value\"\u001b[97m (so FUN_14003dfd8 is a\u001b[93m std::random_device\u001b[97m error-string selector — not a table consumer).\r\nBut immediately after it (0x140070c80) a ramp table\u001b[93m 00 01 02 03…\u001b[97m begins — the shuffle-mask blob may\u001b[3m start\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m there. One more sweep: image-base-relative\r\ndisp32 with RVA 0x6fe00–0x71e00 (validated forms only):\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ edit_script(scan_rva_disp) · 45 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                     \r\n                                                       \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Themisto) · ▸ edit_script(scan_rva_disp) · 45 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[31m\u001b[1m⚠ Developer(Themisto) context CRITICAL (forum tools only): ~180315 of 200000 tokens\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mContext critical — posting all findings to the forum now.\u001b[39m                          \u001b[32;99H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠴\u001b[42;96H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m1\u001b[C029\u001b[C34\u001b[11C6\u001b[C726\u001b[13C556\u001b[C066\u001b[8C59\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.014, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mCo\u001b[Ct\u001b[Cxt cri\u001b[Cical — po\u001b[Cting \u001b[Cll findings\u001b[Cto the\u001b[Cforum now.\u001b[6;1H\u001b[93m📌 #rdata-ranges-xref-scan — Full .text operand scan for refs into 0x140071e00-0x140072800 (A) and 0x140074f00-0x1400750d0 (B): method + results\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Devel\u001b[7;1H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mTask: prove detector-flagged .rdata addresses (0x140072581/0x1400725a1/0x1400725c1/0x140072601; 0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d) are MSVC runtime\r\nconstant tables by finding referencing code.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93mGhidra xrefs_to on the flagged addresses = empty, so I byte-scanned\u001b[1m all of .text (0x140001000..0x14006edff, 450048 bytes, two chunks with overlap;\r\nthe 1-byte chunk seam at 0x140037f00 was manually verified clean)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m with session scripts scan_rip_refs / scan_rva_disp / verify_rip_sites under four\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[93maddressing idioms:\u001b[39m           \u001b[14;1H\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m RIP-relative disp32\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (modrm mod=00/rm=101 check, instruction-end variants +0/+1/+4 imm bytes): computed target = VA_next + disp for every byte\r\noffset. Sanity-checked: finds a known genuine ref lea → 0x14006f2d8.\r\n\u001b[94m2. \u001b[93m\u001b[1mimm64 absolute\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (mov r64, 0x1400xxxxx): low-dword in 0x40000000..0x41000000 with high dword == 1.\r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m\u001b[1m Image-base-relative disp32\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m ([reg(+idx*s) + RVA], modrm mod=10, with/without SIB, reg holding 0x140000000) — RVA windows 0x71e00..0x72800 and\r\n0x74f00..0x750d0.\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[94m4. \u001b[93m\u001b[1mFile-wide rel32 + absolute pointer slots\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m via native scan_refs over both ranges (covers .rdata/.data/.pdata pointer tables too).\u001b[39m                  \r\n                                                                                                                                                   "]
