[0.058, "o", "\u001b[32;95H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠙\u001b[42;98H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m734\u001b[3C0\u001b[10C1\u001b[3C3\u001b[13C26\u001b[4C3\u001b[6C8\u001b[2C9\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m scripter\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m⚑ flagged for analyst review: Range A dead-data verdict: one access idiom not fully swept\u001b[39m                                                          \r\n                                                                                                            \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Themisto)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mFinal handoff\u001b(B\u001b[m         \r\n                                                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mStatus:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Task substantially complete; all findings posted to the forum (#rdata-ranges-xref-scan, #range-b-consumers, #range-a-unreferenced, disproof\r\ncomment !134 on #fn-14003e62c, review flag filed).\r\n\u001b[39m                     "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mFindings with evidence:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                               \u001b[15;1H\u001b[94m1.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Zero RIP-relative/imm64/pointer-slot references into either range across all of .text\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (0x140001000–0x14006edff, fully covered, seam-checked) and\r\nthe whole file (native scan_refs). 76 raw disp32 candidates were individually decoded and all rejected as coincidental dword overlaps (ModRM\u001b[39m         \r\n\u001b[97mmod=00/rm=101 filter; scanner sanity-checked against a known genuine ref).\u001b[39m                                                                        \r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Range B (0x140074f00–0x1400750d0) is proven MSVC UCRT constant data with 25 identified referencing instructions.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m The code addresses it\r\n\u001b[3mimage\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m\u001b[3m-base-relative\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93m[reg + idx*4 + RVA]\u001b[97m with reg = 0x140000000, e.g.\u001b[93m 140047148: movzx eax, word [rcx+rdi*4+0x75010]\u001b[97m), which is why RIP-scans and\r\nxrefs on the flagged addresses were empty. Tables:\u001b[93m large_power_data\u001b[97m @0x140074700,\u001b[93m large_power_indices\u001b[97m {u16,u8,u8} @0x140075010 (flagged\r\n0x140075071/7d/9d are record interiors),\u001b[93m \u001b[Cmall_powers_of_ten\u001b[97m {10…10⁹} @0x1400750a8. Consumers: FUN_1400462f4 (UCRT strtod\u001b[39m                          \r\n\u001b[93mconvert_decimal_string_\u001b[Co_flo\u001b[Cting_type\u001b[97m) and FUN_14006081c (UCRT float formatter,\u001b[C\u001b[93m1#INF\u001b[97m/\u001b[93m1#QNAN\u001b[97m). Full per-site census is in #range-b-consumers.\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Range A (0x140071e00–0x140072800) is unreferenced carried MSVC-style SIMD constant data\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: pshufb lane-shuffle masks, identity\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m ramps, and the\r\n\u001b[93m16-2*popcount(i)\u001b[97m byte table @0x140072580. The detector's \"ADD 0x70/0x72 shell command\" decodes are artifacts of that table. The binary's only\r\n\u001b[93mpshufb\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mvpshufb\u001b[97m are register-form broadcasts in memchr — no consumer exists under any swept idiom.\u001b[39m                                 \u001b[27;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mRemaining work (pickup point):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m run the already-saved session script\u001b[93m scan_rva_disp\u001b[97m twice with\r\n\u001b[93m{\"start\":0,\"len\":225024,\"lo1\":458240,\"hi1\":466432,\"lo2\":0,\"hi2\":0}\u001b[97m and\u001b[93m {\"start\":225024,...}\u001b[97m to close the last idiom for Range A (nearby-base RVA\r\n0x6fe00–0x71e00 + register offset); optionally verify the single odd Range-B candidate at disp-field 0x140060849→0x1400750b5 (likely coincidence).\r\nScripts\u001b[93m scan_rip_refs\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m scan_rva_disp\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m verify_rip_sites\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m grep_decomp_for_ranges\u001b[97m are sav\u001b[Cd in-session and reusable.\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
