[0.018, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m▶ Developer(Megaclite) — goal: Close the final addressing idiom for the Range A SIMD tables (0x140071e00–0x140072800) in the Stealc v2 sample so the\r\ndetector false-positive verdict is complete.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Megaclite) · ▸ read_script(scan_rva_disp) · 24 lines\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n                                            \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Megaclite) · ▸ list_scripts() · 1821 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                              \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Megaclite)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mThe script matches\u001b[93m disp32\u001b[97m values (as RVAs) inside\u001b[93m [lo1,hi1)\u001b[97m with modrm/SIB context — matching the handoff plan.\u001b[93m .text\u001b[97m is 0x140001000–0x14006edff =\r\n0\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[97mx6de00 = 450048 bytes, so two 225024-byte halves cover it exactly. Running both sweeps now, plus pulling bytes around the odd Range-B candidate:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Megaclite) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 82 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                   \r\n                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Megaclite) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 82 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Megaclite) · ▸ read(0x140060830) · 96 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Megaclite)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mBoth sweeps:\u001b[1m 0 hits\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. The second run clamped to 225020 scannable positions (read ended exactly at .text's end 0x14006edff), leaving a 2-byte seam at\r\noffsets 225024–225025 unscanned as disp start positions. Let me close that seam, and also confirm the Range-B candidate instruction decoding:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Megaclite) · ▸ run_script(scan_rva_disp) · 78 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Megaclite) · ▸ disassemble_function(FUN_14006081c) · 3909 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Megaclite)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mAll sweeps complete and the Range-B candidate is decoded. Posting results:\u001b[39m \u001b[42;99H\u001b[90m62\u001b[C101\u001b[10C7\u001b[C005\u001b[14C99\u001b[C106\u001b[8C63\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.041, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93mindex/second disp; the 0x71e00–0x72800 window itself was already swept with 0 validated hits per this post):\u001b[39m                                        \r\n                                            \r\n\u001b[93m```\r\nrun 1: {\"start\":0,     \"len\":225024, \"lo1\":0x6fe00(458240), \"hi1\":0x71e00(466432)} -> scanned 225024 from 0x140001000: 0 hits\r\nrun 2: {\"start\":225024,\"len\":225024, \"lo1\":458240, \"hi1\":466432}                  -> scanned 225020 from 0x140037f00: 0 hits (read clamped at .text e\r\nnd 0x14006edff)\u001b[39m                                       \r\n\u001b[93mrun 3 (seam): {\"start\":225016,\"len\":16, ...}                                       -> scanned 16 from 0x140037ef8: 0 hits (closes the 2-byte disp-pos\r\nition seam at the half boundary)\r\n```\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                               \r\n                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93mCoverage: every byte position in .text 0x140001000..0x14006edff was tested as a potential disp32 start with valid modrm/modrm+SIB context.\u001b[1m Zero\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mdisp32 fields encode an RVA in 0x6fe00..0x71e00, so no lea reg,[nearby_base]; ...[reg+const] idiom with a mod=10 memory operand can address Range A\r\nfrom a below-range base either.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                             \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mRange-B odd candidate 0x140060849 -> 0x1400750b5: coincidental dword overlap, NOT a reference.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Disassembly of FUN_14006081c:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m```\r\n140060847  4c 8b b5 50 07 00 00   MOV R14, qword ptr [RBP + 0x750]\r\n```\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                \r\n                                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[93mThe dword read at 0x140060849 is b5 50 07 00 = 0x000750b5 — i.e. the\u001b[1m modrm byte 0xB5\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m of this instruction followed by the low 3 bytes of its true\r\ndisp32\u001b[1m 0x00000750\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (a stack-frame load; RBP = RSP-0x6f0 in this frame). It references nothing in Range B. (The function is a CRT\r\nfloat-classification/format helper: it selects among string constants at 0x14007887c/88/90/98 and calls 0x140054e98.)\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                         \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mFinal conclusion stands and is now fully swept:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m all 5 addressing idioms (RIP-relative, imm64 absolute, image-base-relative [reg+RVA],\r\nrel32/pointer-slot scan_refs, and nearby-base disp32 0x6fe00..0x72800) yield\u001b[1m zero genuine code references into 0x140071e00..0x140072800\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. Range A is\r\ncarried, unreferenced MSVC SIMD constant data; the detector hits on it are false positives.\u001b[32;89H\u001b[39m      \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠋ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mD\u001b[Cveloper(Megaclite)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
