[0.043, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mTask complete. Summary of what was done and found:\u001b[39m                                                          \u001b[6;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1m1. Nearby-base RVA idiom sweep (\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mscan_rva_disp\u001b[97m\u001b[1m) — 0 hits, full .text coverage\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m- Run 1: \u001b[93m{\"start\":0,\"len\":2250\u001b[C4,\"lo1\u001b[C:4582\u001b[C0,\"hi1\":466432}\u001b[97m → scanned 225024 bytes from 0x140001000: \u001b[1m0 hits\u001b(B\u001b[m                                          \r\n\u001b[97m- Run 2: \u001b[93m{\"start\":225024,\"len\":225024,...}\u001b[97m → scanned 225020 bytes from 0x140037f00 (read clamped exactly at .text end 0x14006edff): \u001b[1m0 hits\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m- Run 3 (seam closure): I noticed the two halves left a 2-byte disp-position seam at the boundary (offsets 225024–225025), so I ran\u001b[39m                  \r\n\u001b[93m{\"start\":225016,\"len\":16,...}\u001b[97m →\u001b[1m 0 hits\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m   \r\n\u001b[97mCoverage is therefore every byte position in .text (0x140001000–0x14006edff) tested as a disp32 start with valid mod=10 modrm/modrm+SIB context. No\r\ndisp32 encodes an RVA in 0x6fe00–0x71e00, so there is no\u001b[93m lea reg,[nearby_base];\u001b[C[reg+const]\u001b[97m path into Range A from a below-range base (the\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[97m0x71e00–0x72800 window itself was already swept with 0 validated hits in the prior session).\u001b[39m                                                       \r\n                               \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m2. Range-B candidate 0x140060849 → 0x1400750b5 — coincidental overlap, not a reference\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                            \r\n\u001b[97mDisassembly of FUN_14006081c shows the containing instruction is:\r\n\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97m```\u001b[39m                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m140060847  4c 8b b5 50 07 00 00   MOV R14, qword ptr [RBP + 0x750]\r\n```\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[97mThe dword at 0x140060849 (\u001b[93mb5 50 07 00\u001b[97m = 0x750b5) is the modrm byte 0xB5 straddled with the low bytes of the true disp32 0x00000750 — a stack-frame\r\nload in a CRT float-formatting helper, referencing nothing in Range B.\u001b[39m                                               \u001b[28;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mVerdict closure:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m all five addressing idioms (RIP-relative, imm64 absolute, image-base-relative, rel32/pointer slots via scan_refs, and nearby-base\r\ndisp32) now yield zero genuine references into 0x140071e00–0x140072800. Range A is confirmed as carried, unreferenced MSVC SIMD constant data; the\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mdetector findings on it are false positives. Results posted as comment !135 under #range-a-unreferenced.\u001b[42;96H\u001b[90m2\u001b[C009\u001b[C983\u001b[12C812\u001b[13C547\u001b[C795\u001b[8C75\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
