[0.038, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m- Run 1: \u001b[93m{\"start\":0,\"len\":225024,\"lo1\":458240,\"hi1\":466432}\u001b[97m → scanned 225024 bytes from 0x140001000: \u001b[1m0 hits\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m- Run 2: \u001b[93m{\"start\":225024,\"len\":225024,...}\u001b[97m → scanned 225020 bytes from 0x140037f00 (read clamped exactly at .text end 0x14006edff): \u001b[1m0 hits\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m- Run 3 (seam closure): I noticed the two halves left a 2-byte disp-position seam at the boundary (offsets 225024–225025), so I ran\r\n\u001b[93m{\"start\":225016,\u001b[Clen\u001b[C:16,...}\u001b[97m →\u001b[1m 0 hits\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                     \r\n                                                                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[97mCoverage is therefo\u001b[2C every byt\u001b[C position\u001b[Cin .text (0x140001000–0x14006edff)\u001b[Ct\u001b[Csted as a\u001b[Cdisp32 start wi\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[C\u001b[97mh\u001b[Cvalid mod=10 modrm/modrm+SIB context. No\r\ndisp32 encodes an RVA in 0x6fe00–0x71e00, so there is no\u001b[93m lea reg,[nearby_base]; [reg+const]\u001b[97m path into Range A from a below-range base (the\r\n0x71e00–0x72800 window itself was already swept with 0 validated hits in the prior session).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1m2. Range-B candidate 0x140060849 → 0x1400750b5 — coincidental overlap, not a reference\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                    \r\n                                                                                            \r\n\u001b[97mDisassembly of FUN_14006081c shows the containing instruction is:\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m```\r\n140060847  4c 8b b5 5\u001b[C 07 00\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[C\u001b[97m00   MOV R14, qword ptr [RBP + 0x750]\r\n```\r\n\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97mThe dword\u001b[Cat 0x140060849 (\u001b[93mb5 50 07 00\u001b[C\u001b[97m= 0x750b5)\u001b[Cis the modrm byte 0xB5 straddled with the low bytes of the true disp32 0x00000750 — a stack-frame\r\nload in a CRT float-formatting helper, referencing nothing in Range B.\u001b[25;1H\u001b[1mVerdict closure:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m all five addressing idioms (RIP-relative, i\u001b[Cm64 absolute, imag\u001b[C-base-relative, rel32/pointer slots via\u001b[Cscan_refs,\u001b[Cand\u001b[Cne\u001b[Crby-b\u001b[Cs\r\ndisp32)\u001b[Cnow yie\u001b[Cd zer\u001b[C genu\u001b[2Ce\u001b[Cr\u001b[Cferences into 0x140071e00–0x140072800. Range A is confirmed as carried, unreferenced MSVC SIMD constant data; the\r\ndetector findings on it are false positives. Results posted as comment !135 under #range-a-unreferenced.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[97mBo\u001b[Ch ve\u001b[Ci\u001b[2Ccation\u001b[Croutes are c\u001b[Cosed. Now I'll post the evi\u001b[Cence und\u001b[Cr #q-decoded-confi\u001b[C.\u001b[39m                \u001b[42;99H\u001b[90m75\u001b[C515\u001b[9C40\u001b[C3\u001b[C5\u001b[13C615\u001b[C830\u001b[8C96\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[34;2H"]
[0.008, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mBoth verification routes are closed. Now I'll post the evidence under #q-decoded-config.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                           \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-decoded-config\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mTask-1 evidence — each detector decode independently reproduced from raw file bytes, and all are coincidental non-strings.\u001b(B\u001b[m         \r\n                                      \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mADD-key decodes (0x140072581/0x1400725a1/0x1400725c1/0x140072601, #fn-14003e62c !36-!39):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Raw-byte replay with byte_transform add 0x70 at file offset\r\n464769 (= VA 0x140072581 via .rdata map 0x6e200→0x14006f000) reproduces the detector string byte-for-byte: ~~|~||z~||z|zzx…. The source bytes are\u001b[1m not\r\nan encoded string\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — they are a byt\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93me LUT whose value at ind\u001b[Cx\u001b[3m i\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m is 16 − 2·popcount(i) (verified against the raw dump: 10 0e 0e 0c 0e 0c 0c 0a 0e 0c 0c\r\n0a 0c 0a 0a 08 … starting at 0x140072580). Since every value is a small even integer 0x00–0x10, adding 0x70/0x72 lands them all in the printable p…~\r\nrange — a guaranteed \"100% printable\" decode of any such counting table. The 0x72-key hits at 0x1400725a1/0x1400725c1/0x140072601 are the same table\r\nat different offsets.\u001b[39m                                                                 \u001b[16;1H\u001b[93mThat LUT sits at the end of a long run (≥0x140072100–0x140072700) of\u001b[1m 16-byte pshufb shuffle-control masks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — permutations of lane indices 0x00–0x0F at\r\nword and dword granularity (raw reads at 0x140072100, 0x140072180, 0x140072380, 0x140072480, 0x140072680 all show the pattern, e.g. 00010203 04050c0d\r\n08090a0b 0c0d0e0f). This is the standard MSVC SIMD element-compaction table layout (shuffle mask per bitmask + output-leng\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93mth byte 16−2·popcount(mask)\r\nfor 2-byte elements).\u001b[39m                                             \r\n   \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mXOR-\"address in use\" decodes (0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d, #fn-140001e10 !5-!7):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m Raw-byte replay (decode_bytes xor key_hex\r\n6164647265737320696e2075736\u001b[2Cat\u001b[Cfile offset 475761 = VA 0x140075071) yields acwwd{8hf5Xrmw'e{s*r)~…— garbage, matching the detector's output in\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93mcharacter (detector's exact bytes differ only by key-phase/start alignment; both are meaningless). The underlying bytes are a monotonically\r\nincreasing numeric record table{uint16, uint8, uint8}: 48 00 04 0a | 52 00 04 0b | 5d 00 04 0c | 69 00 05 0c …, immediately followed at 0x1400750a8\r\nby the **powers-of-ten u32 table** 10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000, 1000000, 10000000, 100000000, 1000000000 (0a000000 64000000 e8030000 10270000\u001b[39m    \r\n\u001b[93ma0860100 40420f00 80969800 00e1f505 00ca9a3b) and then the UTF-16 MSVC\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m CRT source path minkernel\\…`.\u001b[39m                                              \r\n                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mThe XOR \"key\" itself is CRT data, not a key:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m \"address in use\" at 0x1400705b8 sits inside the MSVC STL std::generic_category errno message table — the\r\nraw read at 0x140070560 shows the neighbors success, address family not supported, address in use, address not available, already connected, argument\r\nlist too long, argument out of …. The detector picked one STL error string as a \"candidate key\" and XOR-ed it over nearby numeric tables.\u001b[32;92H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠴ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThink\u001b[2Cg…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mRevers\u001b[CEngineer(Anank\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
