[0.017, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[93m- xrefs_to 0x1400750a8 (powers-of-ten table) → 6 DATA refs from exactly two functions:\u001b[1m FUN_1400462f4\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (7,806 bytes — UCRT strtod core,\r\nconv\u001b[Crt_decimal_string_to_floating_type) and\u001b[1m FUN_14006081c\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (4,749 bytes — UCRT float output formatter, carries the 1#INF/1#QNAN strings).\r\n- The developer's full instruction census (#range-b-consumers, scripted scan) found\u001b[1m 25 referencing \u001b[2Cstruc\u001b[Cions\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m, which address the tables\r\nimage-base-relative (e.g. 140047148: movzx eax, word [rcx+rdi*4+0x75010] with base reg = 0x140000000) — that addressing idiom is why plain xrefs on\r\nthe flagged interior addresses came back empty. The flagged addresses 0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d\u001b[Care\u001b[1m interiors of the\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m {u16,u8,u8}\u001b[1m big-power\u001b(B\u001b[m \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mindex records\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (large_power_indices @0x14\u001b[C07501\u001b[C, backing large_\u001b[Cower_data @0x140074700) used by strtod's big-integer power-of-t\u001b[Cn scaling.\u001b[39m           \r\n                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mRange A (0x140071e00–0x140072800, the ADD-flagged region) — no consumer exists in the binary:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m The \u001b[Ceveloper swept \u001b[Cll fiv\u001b[C addressing idioms across\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mthe \u001b[Cntirety of .t\u001b[Cxt (\u001b[Cx140001000–0x14006edff): RIP-relative disp32, imm64 absolut\u001b[C,\u001b[Cimage-base-relative disp32, rel32/absolute pointer slots\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[93m(nat\u001b[Cve scan_re\u001b[2C over the whole file), and nearby-base RVA disp32 (see #rdata-ranges-xref-scan, #range-a-unreferenced and !135) —\u001b[1m zero genuine\r\nreferences\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. The 76 raw disp32 candidates were each decoded and rejected as coincidental dword overlaps. The only pshufb in the binary (0x14003e72f,\r\ninside FUN_14003e660\u001b[C= SIMD\u001b[Cmemchr: PCMPEQB/PMOVMSKB/BSF; the adjacent 0x14003e770 is a PCMPESTRI vectorized strs\u001b[Cr) uses a\u001b[Cregister-broadcast mask,\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mn\u001b[Ct these tables. Range A is\u001b[1m carried, unreferenced MSVC SIMD constant data\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m — linker-retained\u001b[Ctables from\u001b[2C CRT/STL objec\u001b[C whose code paths weren't\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93mall pulled in.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                       \r\n                     \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mThe flagged \"decoder\" functions are themselves runtime stubs:\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93m- FUN_14003e62c decompiles to a\u001b[C3-\u001b[Cine rand_s\u001b[1m wrapper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (calls rand_s,\u001b[Cabort\u001b[2Cvia invalid-parameter handler on failure).\u001b[CIt performs no\u001b[Cdecoding and\r\nnever \u001b[Couches 0x1400725\u001b[Cx.\u001b[39m                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m- FUN_140001e10 \u001b[Cs\u001b[Cthe std::\u001b[Cad_array_new_length\u001b[1m exception constructor\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (param_1[1]\u001b[C= \"bad array new\u001b[Clength\";\u001b[C*para\u001b[C_1 = &vftab\u001b[Ce;). It performs no\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mencryption — the T1486\u001b[C\"Data Encrypted\u001b[Cfor Impact\" tag on it is baseless.\u001b[39m                                                                     \r\n                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mConclusion:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m all seven detector decodes in #fn-14003e62c and #fn-140001e10 are\u001b[1m coincidental false positives over legitimate statically-linked MSVC\r\nCRT/STL\u001b[Cconstan\u001b[C data\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (SIMD shuffle/popcount\u001b[Ct\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[C\u001b[93mbles and UCRT strtod/float-forma\u001b[C power tabl\u001b[Cs). No decoded value is \u001b[C shell\u001b[Ccommand, key,\u001b[Cor config,\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mand\u001b[Cnone\u001b[Cfeeds any runtime behavior beyond standard number parsing/formatting. This also remove\u001b[C the only \"ransomware/encryption\"\u001b[Cevid\u001b[Cnc\u001b[C attached\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[93mto FUN_140001e10 (relevant t\u001b[C #q-ransomware).\u001b[39m                                                            "]
