[0.011, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[93m- FUN_14003e62c decompiles to a 3-line rand_s\u001b[1m w\u001b[Capper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (calls rand_s, aborts via invalid-parameter handler on failure). It performs no decoding and\r\nnever touches 0x1400725xx.\u001b[7;11H01e10\u001b[Cis the std::bad_array_new_length\u001b[1m exception constructor\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (param_1[1] = \"bad array new length\";\u001b[C*param_1 = &vftable;). It performs \u001b[Co\r\nencryp\u001b[Cion — the T1486 \"Data Encrypted for Impact\" tag on it is baseless.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mConclusion:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m all seven detector decod\u001b[Cs\u001b[Cin #fn-14003e62c and #fn-140001e10 are\u001b[1m coincidental false positives over legitimate statically-linked MSVC\r\nCRT/STL constant data\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (SIMD shuffle/popcount tables and UCRT strtod/float-format power tables). No decoded value is a shell command, key, or config,\r\nand none feeds any runtim\u001b[C behavior beyo\u001b[Cd standard number parsing/formatting. This also removes the only \"ransomware/encryption\" evidence attached\r\nto FUN_140001e10 (relevant to #q-rans\u001b[Cmware).\u001b[39m                                                                                                       \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Ananke) · ▸ complete_task(reverse-engineer) · 314 chars\u001b[17;65H239\u001b[19;1H\u001b[93m💬 reply #fn-140001e10\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                           \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mDisproof of the T1486 findings (!5, !6, !7):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m FUN_140001e10 is the std::bad_array_new_length exception constructor — its full decompile is three\r\nassignments (param_1[1] = \"bad array new length\"; *param_1 = &vftable). It performs no cryptography.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[93mThe \"key\" \"address in use\" is the MSVC STL std::generic_category message string at 0x1400705b8 (neighbors: success, address family not supported,\r\naddress not available, already connected, argument list too long — raw read at 0x140070560). The \"ciphertext\" at 0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d\r\nis the interio\u001b[C of\u001b[Cthe UCRT \u001b[Ctrtod large_power_indices {u16,u8,u8} record \u001b[Cable\u001b[C(base 0x14\u001b[C075010), followed at 0x1400750a8\u001b[Cby the\u001b[Cp\u001b[Cwers-of-\u001b[2Cn u32\r\ntabl\u001b[C 10…10^9, consumed only by UCRT strtod (FUN_1400462f4)\u001b[Cand the float formatter (FUN_14006081c). R\u001b[Cplaying \u001b[Che XOR over raw file bytes yields\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93mgarbage (acwwd{8h\u001b[C5X…`). All \u001b[Chree\u001b[Cfindings a\u001b[Ce co\u001b[Cncidental decodes of legitimate CRT constant data — n\u001b[C Dat\u001b[C-Encrypted-for-Impact behavi\u001b[Cr exists\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[93mhere.\u001b[CFull evidence: !136, !137\u001b[Cunder #q-decoded-config.\u001b[39m                                                                                         \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Ananke) · ▸ set_status(#q-decoded-config) · …running\u001b[32;92H\u001b[39m    \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠋ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling s\u001b[Ct_status\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.082, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mCRT/STL constant data\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (SIMD shuffle/popcount tables and UCRT strtod/float-format power tables). No decoded value is a shell command, key, or config,\r\nand none fe\u001b[Cds any runtime\u001b[Cbeh\u001b[Cvior b\u001b[Cyond standard number pa\u001b[Csing/format\u001b[Cing. This also removes t\u001b[Ce only\u001b[C\"ransomware/encrypti\u001b[Cn\" eviden\u001b[Ce attached\r\nto FUN_140001e10 (relevant to #q-ransomware).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Ananke) · ▸ complete_task(reverse-engineer) · 314 chars\u001b[10;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Ananke) · ▸ complete_task(reverse-engineer) · 239 chars\u001b[39m                                                                        \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply\u001b[C#fn-140001e10\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mDisproof of the T1486 findings (!5, !6, !7):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m FUN_140001e10 is the std::bad_array_new_length exception constructor — its full decompile is three\r\nassignments (param_1[1] = \"bad array new length\"; *param_1 = &vftable). It performs no cryptography.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                       \r\n\u001b[93mThe \"key\" \"address in use\" is the MSVC STL std::generic_category message string at 0x1400705b8 (neighbors: success, address family not supported,\r\naddress not available, already connected, argument list too long — raw read at 0x140070560). The \"ciphertext\" at 0x140075071/0x14007507d/0x14007509d\r\nis the interior of the UCRT strtod large_power_indices {u1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m6,u8,u8} record table (base 0x140075010), followed at 0x1400750a8 by the powers-of-ten u32\r\ntabl\u001b[C 10…10^9, consumed only by UCRT strtod (FUN_1400462f4) and the float formatter (FUN_14006081c). Replaying the XOR over raw file bytes yields\r\ngarbage (acwwd{8hf5X…`). All three findings are coincid\u001b[Cntal decodes of legitimate CRT constant data — no Data-Encryp\u001b[Ced-for-Impact b\u001b[Chavior \u001b[Cxists\r\nhere. Full evidence: !136, !137 under #q-d\u001b[Ccoded-config.\u001b[39m                                            \u001b[23;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Ananke) · ▸ set_status(#q-decoded-config) · 7290 chars\u001b[39m                                                                         \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[93m💬\u001b[Creply #q-rans\u001b[Cmwar\u001b[C\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[93mSupporting the\u001b[Crefutation: the strongest detector \"encryption\" evidence —\u001b[Cthe T1486\u001b[Cfindings on FUN_140001e10 (#fn-140001\u001b[C10 !5/!6/!7, XOR\u001b[Ckey\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[93m\"\u001b[Cddress in use\") — has been\u001b[Cdisproved by raw-byte replay \u001b[Cnd consumer trac\u001b[Cng (s\u001b[Ce !136/!137 un\u001b[Cer #q-decoded\u001b[Cconfig and !138). The function is \u001b[Che\r\nstd::bad_array_new_length exception constru\u001b[Ctor; the \"key\" is an STL errc message string; the \"ciphertext\" is the UCRT strtod power-of-ten index\r\ntable consumed only by strtod/float-formatting. Likewise the ADD-key \"shell command\" decodes in #fn-14003e62c are a CRT SIMD 16−2·popcount(i) byte\r\nLUT shifted into printable range. None of these contribute any encryption-for-impact capability.\u001b[32;92H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠙ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling creat\u001b[C_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
