[0.100, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Ananke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                              \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mTask complete — #q-decoded-config is solved.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Summary of what was established, all with byte-level evidence posted to the forum:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                      \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## Verdict: all seven detector decodes are coincidental false positives over statically-linked MSVC runtime constant data\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                                            \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mADD-key decodes (0x140072581/5a1/5c1/601, flagged under #fn-14003e62c):\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                       \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m- Reproduced byte-for-byte from raw file bytes (\u001b[93mbyt\u001b[C_transform add 0x70\u001b[97m at file offset 464769) — independent verification of the detector's output.\r\n- The source data is a CRT SIMD byte LUT where\u001b[93m tabl\u001b[C[\u001b[C] = 16\u001b[C− 2·popcount(i)\u001b[97m, sitting at the end of a long run (0x140072100–0x140072700) of 16-byte\r\n\u001b[1mpshufb shuffle-control masks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (lane-index permutations of 0x00–0x0F). Every value is a small even integer 0x00–0x10, so adding 0x70/0x72\u001b[3m guarantees\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m a\r\n100%-printable \"decode\" — the tilde soup is an artifact, not a string.\r\n- A full five-idiom reference sweep of all of .text (RIP-relative, imm64, image-base-relative, rel32/pointer slots, nearby-base disp32) found\u001b[1m zero\r\nconsumers\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — it i\u001b[C \u001b[Cinker-carried, unrefer\u001b[Cnced MSVC data. The\u001b[Cflagged function FUN_14003e62c\u001b[Cis a 3-l\u001b[Cn\u001b[C\u001b[93m rand_s\u001b[97m\u001b[1m wrapper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                   \u001b[18;1H\u001b[97m\u001b[1mXOR-\"address in use\" decodes (0x140075071/7d/9d, flagged under #fn-140001e10):\u001b[20;1H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m- The \"key\" is itself CRT data: the\u001b[93m std::generic_category\u001b[97m errc message string at 0x1400705b8 (\u001b[93msuccess\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m address family not supported\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m address in use\u001b[97m,\r\n\u001b[93maddress not available\u001b[97m, ...).\r\n- The \"ciphertext\" is the UCRT strtod\u001b[93m large_power_indices {u16,u8,u8}\u001b[97m record table (base 0x140075010), followed by the powers-of-ten u32 table\u001b[93m 10…10⁹\r\n\u001b[97mat 0x1400750a8 and the UTF-16\u001b[93m minkernel\\…\u001b[97m CRT source path.\r\n- Consumers identified:\u001b[1m FUN_1400462f4\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (UCRT\u001b[93m convert_decimal_string_to_floating_type\u001b[97m, 25 referencing instructions via image-base-relative addressing)\r\nand\u001b[1m FUN_14006081c\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (UCRT float formatter). The flagged function FUN_140001e10 is the\u001b[93m std::bad_array_new_length\u001b[97m\u001b[1m exception constructor\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — the T1486 \"Data\r\nEncrypted for Impact\" tag is baseless, which I also posted as supporting evidence under #q-ransomware.\u001b[28;1HEvidence comments !136/!137 completed both gate tasks; disproof comment !138 posted under #fn-140001e10; question marked\u001b[1m solved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Ghidra annotations\r\nand renames (\u001b[93mucrt_convert_decimal_string_to_floating_type\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m ucrt_float_format_core\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m crt_rand_s_wrapper\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m std_bad_array_new_length_ctor\u001b[97m,\r\n\u001b[93mcrt_simd_memchr\u001b[97m) persist the findings for later runs.\u001b[39m                   \u001b[32;91H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠸\u001b[42;98H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m52\u001b[2C184\u001b[10C5\u001b[3C5\u001b[11C3\u001b[C072\u001b[C5\u001b[C9\u001b[8C83\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.007, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m##\u001b[CV\u001b[Crdict: all seve\u001b[C detector decodes are coincidental false positives over statically-linked MSVC runtime constant data\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mADD-key decodes (0x140072581/5a1/5c1/601, flagged under #fn-14003e62c):\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97m- Reproduced byte-for-byte from raw file bytes (\u001b[93mbyte_transform add 0x70\u001b[97m at file offset 464769) — independent verification of the detector's output.\r\n- The source data is a CRT SIMD byte LUT where\u001b[93m table[i] = 16 − 2·popcount(i)\u001b[97m, sitting at the end of a long run (0x140072100–0x140072700) of 16-byte\r\n\u001b[1mpshufb shuffle-control masks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (lane-index permutations of 0x00–0x0F). Every value is a small even integer 0x00–0x10, so adding 0x70/0x72\u001b[3m guarantees\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m a\r\n100%-printable \"dec\u001b[Cde\" — the tilde\u001b[Csoup\u001b[Cis an\u001b[Cartifact, not a string.\u001b[39m                                                                             \u001b[12;3H\u001b[97mA full five-idiom reference sweep of all of .text (RIP-relative, imm64, image-base-rela\u001b[Cive, rel32/poi\u001b[Cte\u001b[C slots, nearby-base disp32) f\u001b[Cund\u001b[1m zero\u001b(B\u001b[m \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mconsumers\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — it is linker-carried, unreferenced MSVC data. The flagged function FUN_14003e62c is a 3-line\u001b[93m rand_s\u001b[97m\u001b[1m wrapper\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                            \r\n                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mXOR-\"address in use\" decodes (0x140075071/7d/9d, flagged under #fn-140001e10):\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                    \r\n                                                            "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                            \r\n\u001b[97m- The \"key\" is itself CRT data: the\u001b[93m std::generic_category\u001b[97m errc message string at 0x1400705b8 (\u001b[93msuccess\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m address family not supported\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m address in use\u001b[97m,\r\n\u001b[93maddress not available\u001b[97m, ...).\u001b[39m                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m- The \"ciphertext\" is the UCRT strtod\u001b[93m large_power_indices {u16,u8,u8}\u001b[97m record table (base 0x140075010), followed by the powers-of-ten u32 table\u001b[93m 10…10⁹\r\n\u001b[97mat 0x1400750a8\u001b[Cand the U\u001b[CF-16\u001b[93m minkernel\\…\u001b[97m CRT source path.\u001b[39m                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[97m- Consumers identified:\u001b[1m FUN_1400462f4\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (UCRT\u001b[93m convert_decimal_string_to_floating_type\u001b[97m, 25 referencing instructions via image-base-relative addressing)\r\nand\u001b[1m FUN_14006081c\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (UCRT float formatter). The flagged function FUN_140001e10\u001b[Cis the\u001b[93m std::bad_array_new_length\u001b[97m\u001b[1m exception constructor\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — the T1486 \"Data\r\nEncrypted for Impac\u001b[C\" tag is baseless, which I also pos\u001b[Ced as supporting evidence under #q-ransomware.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97mEvidence comments\u001b[C!136/!137 completed both gate tasks; dispr\u001b[Cof comment !138\u001b[Cpos\u001b[Ced under #fn-140001e10; question marked\u001b[1m solved\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Ghidra annotations\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[97ma\u001b[Cd renames (\u001b[93mucrt_convert_decimal_string_to_floating_type\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m ucrt_float_format_core\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m crt_rand_s_wrapper\u001b[97m,\u001b[93m std_bad_array_new_length_ctor\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m,\r\n\u001b[93mcrt_simd_memchr\u001b[97m) persist the findings for later runs.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m■ Swarm(Himalia\u001b[2Cfinished: 7\u001b[Csucceeded, 0\u001b[Cf\u001b[Ciled\u001b[39m     \u001b[34;2H"]
