[0.016, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mConfirmed — FUN_140069054 is just the atexit std::string destructor for DAT_1400b10f0. Let me sweep the remaining four WinHttp globals and check the\r\nDLL loader 0x14003c0a8 to see what DAT_1400b4c98 actually holds (and whether winhttp.dll is ever loaded).\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ xrefs_to(0x1400b1110) · 388 chars\u001b[39m                                         \u001b[9;48H\u001b[90m225\u001b[11;49H13\u001b[13;48H17d\u001b[15;32Hdecomp_function(0x14003c0a\u001b[C) · 2585 chars\u001b[17;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Taygete)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                             \r\n\u001b[97mAll nine WinHttp* string globals follow the identical pattern: written only by\u001b[93m init_decrypted_string_table\u001b[97m, read only by their atexit std::string\r\ndestructors. And\u001b[93m DAT_1400b4c98\u001b[97m is loaded from a string at\u001b[93m DAT_1400b1ef0\u001b[97m (not in the posted map — it's from the second initializer). Given its slot\r\ngroup r\u001b[Csolves Reg* APIs, it should be \"advapi32.dll\", no\u001b[C winhttp. Let me verify by finding its init site and \u001b[Cecoding the blob.\u001b[39m                \r\n                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ xrefs_to(0x1400b1ef0) · 663 chars\u001b[39m                                                                 \u001b[24;49H\u001b[90m25\u001b[26;32Hread(0x14\u001b[C002360) · 64 chars\u001b[39m     \u001b[28;45H\u001b[90ma\u001b[30;1H○\u001b[43C30\u001b[5C…running\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.007, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ xrefs_to(0x1400b1110) · 388 chars\u001b[39m                                         \u001b[7;48H\u001b[90m225\u001b[9;49H13\u001b[11;48H17d\u001b[13;32Hdecomp_function(0x14003c0a\u001b[C) · 2585 chars\u001b[15;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Taygete)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                             \r\n\u001b[97mAll nine WinHttp* string globals follow the identical pattern: written only by\u001b[93m init_decrypted_string_table\u001b[97m, read only by their atexit std::string\r\ndestructors. And\u001b[93m DAT_1400b4c98\u001b[97m is loaded from a string at\u001b[93m DAT_1400b1ef0\u001b[97m (not in the posted map — it's from the second initializer). Given its slot\r\ngroup r\u001b[Csolves Reg* APIs, it should be \"advapi32.dll\", no\u001b[C winhttp\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m. Let me verify by finding its init site and \u001b[Cecoding the blob.\u001b[39m                \r\n                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ xrefs_to(0x1400b1ef0) · 663 chars\u001b[39m                                                                 \u001b[22;49H\u001b[90m25\u001b[24;32Hread(0x14\u001b[C002360) · 64 chars\u001b[39m     \u001b[26;45H\u001b[90ma\u001b[28;45H30\u001b[5C2\u001b[C0 chars\u001b[30;45Ha\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
