[0.098, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mThe grabber (FUN_1400082d8) uploads each grabbed file via FUN_140009814 with token at ctx+0x20, and FUN_1400200c0 parses Mozilla\u001b[93m logins.json\u001b[97m and\r\nuploads the aggregated report as\u001b[1m passwords.txt\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (DAT_1400b0410). Two caller contexts remain: the site inside stealer_main_payload (0x14002a14a) and\r\nFUN_14001b280. Let me read the code around the main-payload call site to identify the filename argument.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ read(0x14002a0d0) · 256 chars\u001b[39m                                                                                      \r\n                                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ get_function(FUN_14001b280) · 311 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                          \r\n\u001b[31m\u001b[1m⚠ ReverseEngineer(Taygete) context warning (flush findings to the forum): ~166769 of 200000 tokens\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[C                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ xrefs_to(0x1400b05b0) · 519 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ decomp_function(FUN_14001b280) · 6633 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                              \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Taygete)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mI now have the complete picture for both residuals. Context is tight, so I'll post findings immediately. First, persist the renames:\u001b[21;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ rename_function(FUN_140009814) · 140 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ rename_function(FUN_140009764) · 141 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                       \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ rename_function(FUN_14001b280) · 139 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                       \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Taygete) · ▸ rename_function(FUN_1400200c0) · 152 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                       \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Taygete)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mNow posting the evidence comments under #q-c2-residuals:\u001b[39m                 \u001b[32;90H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇\u001b[42;98H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m851\u001b[C331\u001b[10C7\u001b[C847\u001b[13C419\u001b[C178\u001b[5C71\u001b[C59\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.013, "o", "\u001b[4;1H                                                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-c2-residuals\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Taygete)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mItem 1 solved —\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m FUN_140009814\u001b[1m @ 0x140009814 (renamed\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m c2_upload_file_chunked_0x40000\u001b[1m) is a SECOND chunked\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m upload_file\u001b[1m sender, not a new message type.\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mFully decompiled.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                          \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mSignature:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m std::string* f(out_opcode, std::string* access_token, std::string* filename, byte* data, uint dataLen). Guard: empty token/filename, NULL\r\nbuffer, or 0 length → returns \"\" immediately.\u001b[39m                         \u001b[12;1H\u001b[93m\u001b[1mBehavior per decompile:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                           \u001b[14;1H\u001b[93m- total_parts = (dataLen + 0x3FFFF) >> 18 → \u001b[1m0x40000 (262,144)-byte chunks\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (vs 0x7D000 = 512,000 in the other uploader FUN_14000b690, !116).\r\n- Each chunk is base64-encoded by FUN_140009764 (renamed b64_encode_CryptBinaryToStringA) = (*DAT_1400b4d80)(buf, len, 0x40000001, out, &outLen) →\r\n\u001b[1mCryptBinaryToStringA, CRYPT_STRING_BASE64|NOCRLF\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (same crypt32 ptr proven in !116).\u001b[1m The filename string is ALSO base64-encoded once\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m through the same\r\nwrapper before being placed in the JSON (difference vs FUN_14000b690).\r\n- JSON is built by raw string concatenation from .rdata fragments, byte-verified by read @ 0x14007f588: } @0x14007f588, \"total_parts\": @0x14007f590,\r\n, @0x14007f5a0, \"part_index\": @0x14007f5a8, \", @0x14007f5b8, \": \" @0x14007f5bc, \" @0x14007f5c4, { @0x14007f5c8.\u001b[39m                     \r\n\u001b[93m- Fields in build order (keys resolved via #strtable-global-map): access_token (0x1400b20b0) = param_2, data (0x1400b0bb0) = b64 chunk, filename\r\n(0x1400b1310) = b64(filename), type (0x1400b0c90) = upload_file (0x1400b0ed0), \"part_index\": N, \"total_parts\": M → {\"access_token\": \"…\", \"data\":\r\n\"<b64>\", \"filename\": \"<b64>\", \"type\": \"upload_file\", \"part_index\": N, \"total_parts\": M}\r\n- Whole JSON → memcpy-to-vector FUN_14000d9f0 →\u001b[1m base64 encode\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m FUN_140023290 → sent per chunk via c2_http_post_json_base64 @ 0x14000b384 with\u001b[1m host\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93mDAT_1400b0490\u001b[1m (45.93.20.28) and URI\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m DAT_1400b0630\u001b[1m (/3d15e67552d448ff.php)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m converted to wide by FUN_14003a204 — identical transport/wrapping to\r\n!112/!116.\u001b[39m                                                               \r\n\u001b[93m- Response: base64-decoded in the sender, JSON-parsed (FUN_14000daac), opcode\u001b[1m (0x1400b1570) extracted and returned\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m (last part's opcode) — same as\r\nFUN_14000b690.\u001b[39m                                                           \u001b[29;1H\u001b[93mSo the 5th endpooint consumer sends the already-documented upload_file message; the protocol picture in !116/!123 is unchanged, only this raw-buffer\r\nuploader variant (0x40000 chunks, base64ed filename) is new detail.\u001b[32;90H\u001b[39m \u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mReverseEngin\u001b[Cer(Taygete)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: ca\u001b[Cling create_comment\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
