[0.012, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Chaldene)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                 \r\n\u001b[97mThe sites appear to be mid-instruction in my manual reads (misaligned). Given my tight context, I'll delegate precise instruction-level resolution to\r\nthe developer.\u001b[39m                                               \u001b[9;1H\u001b[90m○\u001b[CReverseEngineer(Chaldene) · ▸ developer(Resolve the data references at five cod…) · …running\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m▶ Developer(Harpalyke) — goal: Resolve the data references at five code sites in the Stealc v2 main program so the decoded constants can be posted to\r\nthe forum.\u001b[39m                                                                                    \u001b[15;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ follow_link(#q-residual-decodes) · 767 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ list_programs() · 211 chars\u001b[19;28Hrhai_docs() · 634 lines\u001b[39m                     \u001b[21;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                               \r\n\u001b[97mLet me test how the script disassembly binding behaves with mid-function addresses.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ create_script(test_disasm_anchor) · 73 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ run_script(test_disasm_anchor) · 258 chars\u001b[39m              \u001b[28;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                \r\n\u001b[97mThe binding starts disassembly at the given address. Now I'll build a script that walks from each function start in 100-instruction chunks\r\n(guaranteeing correct alignment), finds the containing instruction, and dumps the ±8 window with resolved data refs.\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.007, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mThe sites appear to be mid-instruction in my manual reads (misaligned). Given my tight context, I'll delegate precise instruction-level resolution to\r\nthe developer.\u001b[39m              \r\n                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[90m○\u001b[39m \u001b[90mReverseEngineer(Chaldene) · ▸ developer(Resolve the data references at five cod…) · …running\u001b[9;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                       \r\n\u001b[97m▶ Developer(Harpalyke) — goal: Resolve the data references at five code sites in the Stealc v2 main program so the decoded constants can be posted to\r\nthe forum.\u001b[39m             \r\n                                                                                                                                                     "]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ follow_link(#q-residual-decodes) · 767 chars\u001b[15;28Hlist_programs() · 211 chars\u001b[39m                 \u001b[17;28H\u001b[90mrhai\u001b[Cdocs() · 634\u001b[Clines\u001b[39m    \u001b[19;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                           \r\n\u001b[97mLet me test how the script disassembly binding behaves with mid-function addresses.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ create_script(test_disasm_anchor) · 73 chars\u001b[39m            \u001b[24;28H\u001b[90mrun_script(tes\u001b[C_disasm_anchor) · 258 chars\u001b[39m  \u001b[26;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                              \r\n\u001b[97mThe binding starts disassembly at the given address. Now I'll build a script that walks from each function start in 100-instruction chunks\r\n(guaranteeing \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mcorrect alignment), finds the containing instruction, and dumps the ±8 window with resolved data refs.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ create_script(site_context) · 68 chars\u001b[39m                                                   \u001b[32;96H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠴ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThink\u001b[2Cg…\u001b[39m \u001b[35m\u001b[1mDeveloper(Harp\u001b[Clyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: calling create"]
