[0.007, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[90m○\u001b[CR\u001b[3CrseEngineer(Chaldene) · ▸ developer(R\u001b[2Colve th\u001b[C data referen\u001b[Ces at five cod…) · …running\u001b[7;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                               \r\n\u001b[97m▶ Developer(Harpalyke) — goal: Resolve the data references at five code sites in the Stealc v2 main program so the decoded constants can be posted to\r\nthe forum.\u001b[39m                                        \u001b[11;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ follow_link(#q-residual-decodes) · 767 chars\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ list_programs() · 211 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ rhai_docs() · 634 lines\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mLet me test how the script disassembly binding behaves with mid-function addresses.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                          \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ create_script(test_disasm_anchor) · 73 chars\u001b[39m                                             \u001b[22;28H\u001b[90mrun_script(test_disasm_anchor) ·\u001b[C258 chars\u001b[24;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                       \r\n\u001b[97mThe binding starts disassembly at the given address. Now I'll build a script that walks from each function start in 100-instruction chunks\r\n(guaranteeing correct alignment), finds the containing instruction, and dumps the ±8 window with resolved data refs.\u00