[0.025, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                               \r\n\u001b[97mLet me test how the script disassembly binding behaves with mid-function addresses.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                                                \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ create_script(test_disasm_anchor) · 73 chars\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                     \r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mDeveloper(Harpalyke) · ▸ run_script(test_disasm_anchor) · 258 chars\u001b[39m              \u001b[11;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Harpalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                \r\n\u001b[97mThe binding starts disassembly at the given address. Now I'll build a script that walks from each function start in 100-instruction chunks\r\n(guaranteeing correct alignment), finds the containing instruction, and dumps the ±8 window with resolved data refs.\u001b[15;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mDe\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
