[0.000, "o", "\u001b[93m\u001b[1m two independent routes:\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                         \r\n\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m\u001b[3m Writer trace:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m [0x1400b4c58] is written only at\u001b[1m 0x14003d31e\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m in resolve_api_ptrs_from_decrypted_strings (@0x14003c2ac). The resolver interleaves\r\nGetProcAddress calls: the MOV [slot],RAX stores the result of the\u001b[1m preceding\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m call, whose name argument was DAT_1400b10b0 (CMOVA at 0x14003d2ec); the\r\nLEA RDX,[0x1400b1990] just before th\u001b[C store stages the\u001b[3m next\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m name. DAT_1400b10b0 is filled at init site 0x140005608–0x140005617 from ciphertext\r\n@0x14007e370 jE78SmASp1Dcy95E8sCmTk6s → decrypt_string_b64_rc4 → GetFileAttributesA (re-decoded natively with base64→RC4 CgeOvEO7hu).\r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m\u001b[3m Call-site semantics:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m CMP EAX,-1 = INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES and TEST AL,0x10 = FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DIRECTORY —\u001b[Cexactly the\u001b[CGetFileAttributes\u001b[C return\r\ncontract.\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
