[0.036, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Kallichore)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                \r\n\u001b[97m⚑ flagged for analyst review: Library candidate: consolidated RIP-relative data-ref scanner (not promoted)\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                  \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Kalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                         \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mCuration complete.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Report:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                             \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mPromoted (1 script):\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                         \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[93m \u001b[Culk_de\u001b[2Cy\u001b[2C_b64_rc4\u001b[97m → persistent library. The bulk base64→RC4 string-table decryptor used for #q-bulk-strings (!88/!89, validated: 337 candidates,\r\n270 plaintexts, 0 decode errors, cross-checked against an independent raw-file decode route). It was already fully generic — all binary-specific\r\ninputs (VA base, size, RC4 key like\u001b[93m \"CgeOvEO7hu\"\u001b[97m, min token length, keyword list) flow through args; nothing hardcoded. Promoted unchanged, with docs\r\npositioning it as the\u001b[1m program-memory twin\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m of the existing library script\u001b[93m scan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m (which scans a raw\u001b[3m file\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m window) — so it adds\r\ndistinct value rather than duplicating: use it on loaded/imported programs working in VAs; use the file-window script on raw/unimported artifacts.\r\nThis also executes the promotion !114 recorded as having failed at context limit.\u001b[39m                                                                    \r\n                                    \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mNot promoted, with reasons:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                          \r\n                                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mscan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mwalk_b64rc4_strtable\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mdisasm_site_window\u001b[97m — already in the library from earlier in this run; no duplicates created.\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mmap_strtable_globals\u001b[97m — duplicates library \u001b[93mwalk_b64rc4_strtable\u001b[97m's purpose (blob→global mapping) via a less robust decompile-parsing route.\r\n- \u001b[93mstealc_fulltabl\u001b[C_\u001b[Cweep\u001b[97m — superseded by its already-promoted form \u001b[93mscan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                                                       \r\n\u001b[97m-\u001b[C\u001b[93mscan_rip_refs\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m sca\u001b[C_rva_disp\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m verify_rip_sites\u001b[97m — useful technique (RIP-relative disp32 refs, a real gap in native\u001b[93m scan_refs\u001b[97m), but they hardcode\r\n\u001b[93mTEXT_BASE=0x140001000\u001b[97m and image-base-specific imm64 heuristics (verified by reading the source), span three scripts, and required manual\r\nfalse-positive triage. Promoting as-is violates the args-only rule; rewriting now would ship an unverified script.\u001b[1m Flagged for review\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (flag 10, ref\r\n#rdata-ranges-xref-scan) as a consolidation candidate for a future run.\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mdbg_one/dbg_scan/dbg_decode/dbg_cerrent\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mtest_disasm_anchor\u001b[97m, \u001b[93msite_context\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mgrep_decomp_for_ranges\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mresolve_globals\u001b[97m — one-off debug helpers.\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                      \r\n\u001b[97mCuration summary po\u001b[2Ced as comment !148 under the #q-bulk-stri\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mngs thread.\u001b[39m                                 \u001b[32;97H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠋\u001b[42d\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m332\u001b[C245\u001b[9C20\u001b[C701\u001b[13C952\u001b[C9\u001b[C6\u001b[6C5\u001b[C86\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
