[0.011, "o", "\u001b[4;1H \u001b[C                      \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m Developer(Kalyke)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                      \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mCuration complete.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m Report:\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[C                  \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mPromoted\u001b[C(1 script):\u001b(B\u001b[m      \u001b[10;1H\u001b[97m-\u001b[93m bulk_decrypt_b64_rc4\u001b[97m → persistent library. The bulk base64→RC4 string-table decryptor used for #q-bulk-strings (!88/!89, validated: 337 candidates,\r\n270 plaintexts, 0 decode errors, cross-checked against an independent raw-file decode route). It was already fully generic — all binary-specific\r\ninputs (VA base, size,\u001b[CRC4 key like\u001b[93m \"CgeOvEO7hu\"\u001b[97m, min\u001b[Ctok\u001b[Cn length, keyword list) flow through args; nothing hardcoded. Promote\u001b[C unchanged, with docs\r\npositioning it as\u001b[Cthe\u001b[1m program-memory twin\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m of the exi\u001b[2Cing\u001b[Clibrary s\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[97mcript\u001b[93m scan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m (which scans a raw\u001b[3m file\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mwindow) — so it adds\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mdistinct value rather than\u001b[Cduplicating: use it on\u001b[Cloaded/imported programs working in VAs; \u001b[Cse\u001b[Cthe file-w\u001b[2Cdow script on \u001b[Caw/unimported artifacts.\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97mThis also executes the promotion !114 recorded as having fa\u001b[Cled at \u001b[Context limit.\u001b[39m                                                              \r\n                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mNot promoted, with reasons:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                      \u001b[19;1H\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mscan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mwalk_b64rc4_strtable\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mdisasm_site_window\u001b[97m — already in the library from earlier in this run; no duplicates created.\r\n- \u001b[93mmap_strtable_globals\u001b[97m — duplicates library \u001b[93mwalk_b64rc4_strtable\u001b[97m's purpose (blob→global mapping) via a less robust decompile-parsing route.\u001b[21;4H\u001b[93mtealc_fulltable_sweep\u001b[97m — superseded by its already-promoted form \u001b[93mscan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m                                                  \u001b[22;2H\u001b[93m scan_rip_refs\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m scan_rva_disp\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m verify_rip_sites\u001b[97m — useful technique (RIP-re\u001b[Cative disp32 refs,\u001b[Ca re\u001b[Cl gap\u001b[Cin na\u001b[Civ\u001b[C\u001b[93m scan_refs\u001b[97m), but they hardcode\r\n\u001b[93mTEXT_BASE=0x140001000\u001b[97m and imag\u001b[C-bas\u001b[C-spec\u001b[Cfic imm64 heuris\u001b[Cics (verified by reading the source), span three scripts, and required manual\r\nfalse-positive triage. Promoting as-is violates the args-only rule; rewriting n