[0.011, "o", "\u001b[5;1H\u001b[97m-\u001b[93m bulk_decrypt_b64_rc4\u001b[97m → persistent library. The bulk base64→RC4 string-table decryptor used for #q-bulk-strings (!88/!89, validated: 337 candidates,\r\n270 plaintexts, 0 decode errors, cross-checked against an independent raw-file decode route). It was already fully generic — all binary-specific\r\ninputs (VA base, size, RC4 key like\u001b[93m \"CgeOvEO7hu\"\u001b[97m, min token length, keyword list) flow through args; nothing hardcoded. Promoted unchanged, with docs\r\npositioning it as the\u001b[1m program-memory twin\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m of the existing library script\u001b[93m scan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m (which scans a raw\u001b[3m file\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m window) — so it adds\r\ndistinct value rather than duplicating: use it on loaded/imported programs working in VAs; use the file-window script on raw/unimported artifacts.\r\nThis also executes the\u001b[Cpromot\u001b[Con !114 recorded as having failed at co\u001b[Ctext \u001b[Cimit.\u001b[39m                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                                \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mNot promoted, with reasons:\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                          \r\n                                                                                                                                               \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mscan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mwalk_b64rc4_strtable\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mdisasm_site_window\u001b[97m — already in\u001b[Cthe library\u001b[Cfrom earlier in\u001b[Cthis run;\u001b[Cno d\u001b[Cplicates created.\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[93mmap_strtable_globals\u001b[C\u001b[97m— dupl\u001b[Ccates library \u001b[93mwalk_b64rc4_strtable\u001b[97m's\u001b[Cpurpose\u001b[C(blob→global mapping) via a less robust decompile-parsing route.\r\n- \u001b[93mstealc_fulltable_sweep\u001b[97m — superseded by its already-promoted form \u001b[93mscan_b64_rc4_string_table\u001b[97m.\r\n-\u001b[93m scan_rip_refs\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m scan_rva_disp\u001b[97m /\u001b[93m verify_rip_sites\u001b[97m — useful technique (RIP-relative disp32 refs, a real gap in native\u001b[93m scan_refs\u001b[97m), but they hardcode\r\n\u001b[93mTEXT_BASE=0x140001000\u001b[97m and image-base-specific imm64 heuristics (verified by reading the source), span three scripts, and required manual\r\nfalse-positive triage. Promoting as-is violates the args-only rule; rewriting now would ship an unverified script.\u001b[1m Flagged for review\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (flag 10, ref\r\n#rdata-ranges-xref-scan)\u001b[Cas a \u001b[Consolidation\u001b[Ccandidate for a future\u001b[Cr\u001b[Cn.\u001b[39m                                                                    \u001b[21;3H\u001b[93mdbg_one/dbg_scan/dbg_decode/dbg_cerrent\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mtest_disasm_anchor\u001b[97m, \u001b[93msite_\u001b[Co\u001b[Ctext\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mgrep_decomp_for_ranges\u001b[97m, \u001b[93mresolve_globals\u001b[97m — one-off debug helpers.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97mCuration summary posted as comment !148 under\u001b[Cthe #q-b\u001b[Clk-strings threa\u001b[C.\u001b[39m                                                               \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[31m●\u001b[39m \u001b[90mmain · ▸ finish() · 362 chars\u001b[39m                                        \r\n                                                                                                                                             \r\n\u