[0.078, "o", "\u001b[32;119H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠇\u001b[42;98H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90m127\u001b[C473\u001b[10C3\u001b[C015\u001b[13C770\u001b[C488\u001b[6C9\u001b[C18\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.025, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mchunked\u001b[93m upload_file\u001b[97m (512,000/262,144-byte chunks, inner base64) →\u001b[93m loader\u001b[97m tasking →\u001b[93m done\u001b[97m. Only endpoint in the binary.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 5. Cryptography\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                                   \r\n                                                                                                                                                  \r\n\u001b[97mS\u001b[Cngle\u001b[1m RC4 key\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m CgeOvEO7hu\u001b[97m @ 0x14007d6e0; all ~270 embedded strings are base64(RC4) blobs decrypted pre-main (decryptor @ 0x140007d04, RC4 @\r\n0x140023048). All plaintexts recovered and published. Detector's 18 \"candidate keys\" were ciphertext fragm\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[97ments. Build/campaign ID:\u001b[93m 512e7bd984984fb6\r\n\u001b[97m(plaintext).\u001b[39m        \u001b[12;1H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 6. Anti-analysis\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                                \r\n                                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mCIS kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: exits on LANGIDs 0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443 (RU/UA/BY/KZ/UZ), before any C2 contact\u001b[39m                                            \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mNamed-event single-instance guard\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93m<%p>_<Computer>_<User>\u001b[97m, with a\u001b[Cdeveloper bug form\u001b[Ct\u001b[2Cng\u001b[Ca function poi\u001b[2Ce\u001b[C)\u001b[39m                         \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mDate kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: ha\u001b[Cd\u001b[Coded expiry \u001b[1m11 April 2025\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m assembled from 4 RC4 blobs (@ 0x14002a774)\r\n- No\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m anti-VM, no HAL9TH/JohnDoe check, no anti-debug beyond CRT (verified negatives)\r\n\u001b[39m                         \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 7. Injection\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                       \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mEarly-Bird APC injection\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (@ 0x14003a048): CreateProcess suspended → VirtualAllocEx RWX → WriteProcessMemory of the embedded 64-bit helper DLL\r\n(pre-mapped, sRDI reflective loader appended) → QueueUse\u001b[CAPC. The helper uses the\u001b[1m IElevator COM service\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m to decrypt Chrome's app-bound key and returns\r\nit over a volume-serial-derived named pipe. Optional\u001b[93m runas\u001b[97m elevation for loader tasks; no other privilege escalation.\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                              \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 8–9. IOCs & Attribution\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                     \u001b[27;1H\u001b[97mFull list in forum \u001b[Cost\u001b[1m #final-iocs\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m; attribution evidence\u001b[C(YARA ×3, protocol, buil\u001b[Ce\u001b[C path\u001b[2Ctypo\u001b[93m Error dumping proccess list\u001b[97m)\u001b[Cin\u001b[1m #final-verdict\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\r\nNote: the oft-cited\u001b[C\"Ge\u001b[CCerrentProcessId\" \u001b[Cypo is\u001b[1m not\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97min this build — the earlier claim was corrected by byte-level re-verification.\u001b[30;1HAll 15 questions raised were solved with byte-level evidence; detector false positives (ransomware, fake ADD/XOR decodes) were explicitly refuted,\r\nand low-confidence items (IElevator GUID naming, event-name %p bug) were flagged for analyst review.\u001b[32;119H\u001b[39m           \u001b[C                    \u001b[34;2H"]
