[0.002, "o", "                            \u001b[30C            \u001b[3C    \u001b[C        \u001b[6C    \r\n\u001b[97mSingle\u001b[1m RC4 key\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m CgeOvEO7hu\u001b[97m @ 0x14007d6e0; all ~270 embedded strings are base64(RC4) blobs decrypted pre-main (decryptor @ 0x140007d04, RC4 @\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97m0x140023048). All plaintexts recovered and published. Detector's 18 \"candidate keys\" were ciphertext fragments. Build/campaign ID:\u001b[93m 512e7bd984984fb6\r\n\u001b[97m(plaintext).\u001b[39m                \u001b[C                             \u001b[44C            \u001b[2C                      \r\n                            \u001b[C                           \u001b[46C            \u001b[3C               \u001b[7C        \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 6. Anti-analysis\u001b(B\u001b[m         \u001b[C                      \u001b[51C            \u001b[3C              \u001b[8C        \r\n                            \u001b[C                  \u001b[55C            \u001b[3C          \u001b[12C        \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mCIS kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: exits on LANGIDs 0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443 (RU/UA/BY/KZ/UZ), before any C2 contact\u001b[39m         \u001b[3C          \u001b[12C        \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mNamed-event single-instance guard\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93m<%p>_<Computer>_<User>\u001b[97m, with a developer bug formatting a function pointer)\u001b[39m  \u001b[3C           \u001b[11C        \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mDate kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: hardcoded expiry \u001b[1m11 April 2025\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m assembled from 4 RC4 blobs (@ 0x14002a774)\u001b[9C\u001b[39m            \u001b[3C         \u001b[13C        \r\n\u001b[97m- No anti-VM, no HAL9TH/JohnDoe check, no anti-debug beyond CRT (verified negatives)\u001b[18C\u001b[39m            \u001b[3C           \u001b[11C        \r\n                            \u001b[C            \u001b[61C            \u001b[3C        \u001b[14C        \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 7. Injection\u001b(B\u001b[m             \u001b[C         \u001b[64C            \u001b[3C                    \u001b[2C        \r\n                            \u001b[C       \u001b[66C            \u001b[3C           \u001b[11C        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mEarly-Bird APC injection\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (@ 0x14003a048): CreateProcess suspended → VirtualAllocEx RWX → WriteProcessMemory of the embedded 64-bit helper DLL\u001b[39m      \r\n\u001b[97m(pre-mapped, sRDI reflective loader appended) → QueueUserAPC. The helper uses the\u001b[1m IElevator COM service\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m to decrypt Chrome's app-bound key and returns\r\nit over a volume-serial-derived named pipe. Optional\u001b[93m runas\u001b[97m elevation for loader tasks; no other privilege escalation.\u001b[39m             \u001b[9C        \r\n                            \u001b[C  \u001b[71C            \u001b[3C         \u001b[13C        \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 8–9. IOCs & Attribution\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[74C            \u001b[3C          \u001b[12C        \u001b[26;118H           \u001b[11C        \r\n\u001b[97mFull list in forum post\u001b[1m #final-iocs\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m; attribution evidence (YARA ×3, protocol, builder path, typo\u001b[93m Error dumping proccess list\u001b[97m) in\u001b[1m #final-verdict\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\u001b[39m   \r\n\u001b[97mNote: the oft-cited \"GetCerrentProcessId\" typo is\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m in this build — the earlier claim was corrected by byte-level re-verification.\u001b[7C\u001b[39m        \u001b[29;118H           \u001b[11C        \r\n\u001b[97mAll 15 questions raised were solved with byte-level evidence; detector false positives (ransomware, fake ADD/XOR decodes) were explicitly refuted,\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97mand low-confidence items (IElevator GUID naming, event-name %p bug) were flagged for analyst review.\u001b[17C\u001b[39m               \u001b[7C        \u001b[32;118H            \u001b[10C  