[1.004, "o", "\u001b[2G\u001b[90mHow can Thorium help?                                                                                                                               \u001b[35;2H                                                                                                                                                    \u001b[36;2H                                                                                                                                                    \u001b[37;2H                                                                                                                                                    \u001b[38;2H                                                                                                                                                    \u001b[39;2H                                                                                                                                                    \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[34;2H"]
[0.012, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[97mSingl\u001b[C\u001b[1m RC4 key\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m CgeOvEO7hu\u001b[97m @ 0x14007d6e0; all ~270\u001b[Cemb\u001b[Cdded strings are base64(RC4) blobs\u001b[Cdecrypted pre-main (decryptor @ 0x140007d04, RC4 @\r\n0x140023048). All plaintexts recovered and published. Detector's 18 \"candidate keys\" were ciphertext fragments. Build/campaign ID:\u001b[93m 512e7bd984984fb6\r\n\u001b[97m(plaintext).\u001b[39m      \u001b[8;1H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 6. Anti-analysis\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                        \r\n                                                                                                                                                   \r\n\u001b[97m- \u001b[1mCIS kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: exits on LANGIDs 0x419/0x422/0x423/0x43F/0x443 (RU/UA/BY/KZ/UZ), before any C2 contact\r\n- \u001b[1mNamed-event single-instance guard\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (\u001b[93m<%p>_<Computer>_<User>\u001b[97m, with a developer bug formatting a\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m function pointer)\r\n- \u001b[1mDate kill-switch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m: hardcoded expiry \u001b[1m11 April 2025\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m assembled from 4 RC4 blobs (@ 0x14002a774)\r\n- No anti-VM, no HAL9TH/JohnDoe check, no anti-debug beyond CRT (verified negatives)\r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                         \r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 7. Injection\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                 \r\n                                                                                             \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mEarly-Bird APC injection\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (@ 0x14003a048):\u001b[CCreateProcess suspended → VirtualAllocEx RWX → WriteProcessMemory of the embedded 64-bit helper DLL\r\n(pre-mapped, sRDI reflective loader appended) → QueueUserAPC. The helper uses the\u001b[1m IElevator COM service\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m to decrypt Chrome's app-bound key and returns\r\nit over a volume-serial-derived named pipe. Optional\u001b[93m runas\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m elevation for loader tasks; no other privilege escalation.\u001b[21;1H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## 8–9. IOCs & Attribution\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                                                                   \r\n                                                                                                                                                     \r\n\u001b[97mFull list\u001b[Cin forum post\u001b[1m #final-iocs\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m; attribution evidence (YARA ×3, pr\u001b[Ctoc\u001b[Cl, builder path, typo\u001b[93m Error dumping proccess list\u001b[97m) in\u001b[1m #final-verdict\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m.\r\nNote: the oft-cited \"GetCerrentProcessId\" typo is\u001b[1m not\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m in this build — the earlier claim was corrected by byte-level re-verification.\r\n\u001b[39m                          \r\n\u001b[97mAll 15 questions raised were solved with byte-level evidence; detector false positives (ransomware, fake ADD/XOR decodes) were explicitly refuted,\r\nand low-confidence\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[C\u001b[97mitems (IElevator GUID naming,\u001b[3Cent-name %p bug)\u001b[Cwere flagged for an\u001b[Clyst review.\u001b[39m                                            \r\n                                                                                                                                    \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\r\nWriting r\u001b[Cport to report.md…\u001b[39m                                                                                                                      \r\n                                                                                                    \u001b[32;117H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m⠼ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[90mThinking…\u001b[C\u001b[35m\u001b[1mreport\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m: writing report\u001b[34;2H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
